PVD("nigeria_ndp_2021-2025",{"docs":["","NG National Development Plan 2021 2025 Vol I"],"s":{"1":[[1,"5","1","National Development Plan 2021-2025","Nigeria's National Development Plan (NDP), 2021 - 2015 is a medium-term blueprint designed to unlock the country's potentials in all sectors of the economy for a sustainable, holistic and inclusive national development, developed by the different facet of the Private Sector, Sub-national Government, Civil Society Organization (CSO) and facilitated by the Federal Government of Nigeria.",""],[1,"5","5","Plan Implementation Framework Strengthening","Government will also put in place a robust implementation framework that promotes performance and accountability.",""],[1,"5","5","Development Plan Implementation Unit and Monitoring System Strengthening","In this regard, the development Plan Implementation Unit and the National Monitoring and Evaluation system will be strengthened for assessment and tracking of government policies and programmes.",""],[1,"8","1","Implementation Capacity Strengthening at National and Subnational Levels","The country can achieve these targets through high quality economic growth and a more inclusive economy, leveraging its young workforce, and enhancing implementation capacity at national and subnational levels.",""],[1,"11","3","Strengthened National Plan Implementation and Coordination Framework","The success of this Plan will depend, to a large extent, on the establishment of a strong implementation mechanism and framework that promotes performance and accountability.","Ministry of Finance, Budget and National Planning"],[1,"11","4","Development Plan Implementation Unit Establishment","a Development Plan Implementation unit (PIU) that reports to NSC headed by the VP, with the HM/HMS Budget and National Planning as Vice Chair, will be established in the Budget and Planning Arm to promote overall coordination with the MDAs, private sector operators, CSOs, amongst others.",""],[1,"11","4","National Monitoring and Evaluation Framework Operationalization","The National M&E framework will be fully operationalized and Coordinated by the Budget and Planning Arm, for deliberate alignment of the National Budget with the Plan and deployment of technologies to drive a result-based implementation of the Plan in the country.",""],[1,"27","17","Plan-Budget Linkage Framework","This requires ensuring a proper linkage of the annual budget to this Plan during implementation.",""],[1,"27","18","Centralized Plan Implementation Coordination Mechanism","Need to adhere to a centralized plan implementation coordination mechanism (i.e., avoid multiplicity of coordinators)",""],[1,"27","22","Plan Monitoring and Evaluation Coordination","There is the need for agencies contributing inputs into the M & E system to ensure proper coordination.",""],[1,"27","23","Legislative Backing for Plan-Budget Linkage","To ensure a proper linkage of the plan to budgets and expenditure frameworks, there is a need for appropriate legislative backing as was contemplated under NV 20: 2020.",""],[1,"30","6","Economic Blueprint Development and Coordination Mechanism","The CWG coordinates the work of the 26 TWGs to drive the development of an actionable plan aimed at tackling national challenges and transforming the national economic trajectory.",""],[1,"34","19","Plan Implementation Coordination Mechanism","Strengthen coordinating mechanism for plan implementation.",""],[1,"177","5","Continuity of Programme Implementation Measures","Adopt measures that will prevent the disruption of programmes and activities due to transition in government.",""],[1,"177","10","Legal Institutionalization of Plan Implementation","Institutionalization of the Plan's implementation with law at all levels of government to check frequent policy reversals, compel sustainability and consistency with commitment to attaining the desired objectives.",""],[1,"177","12","Professionalization of the Planning Function","Professionalization of the planning function to ensure capacity sustainability.",""],[1,"177","13","Skilled Manpower Development and Capacity Utilization Policy for Public Service Implementation","Deliberate policy on skilled manpower development and adequate capacity utilization in the public service to drive the implementation.",""],[1,"178","16","Strengthening of the Budget and Planning Arm","The Budget and Planning Arm being the coordinating MDA for budget and planning will be strengthened and enhanced to ensure continuity and professionalism in the planning process, budgeting, and execution.","Ministry of Finance, Budget and National Planning"],[1,"178","18","Development Plan Implementation Unit and Coordination Structure","a Development Plan Implementation unit (PIU) that reports to National Steering Committee headed by the VP, with the HM/ HMS Budget and National Planning as Vice Chair, M&E and Coordination structure will be established within the Planning Arm to provide a central coordinating mechanism; deliberate alignment of National Budget with the Plan and deployment of technologies to drive a result-based implementation of the Plan in the country.",""],[1,"179","11","Development Policy Framework Review and Approval","Review and approve development policy framework",""],[1,"179","11","Policy Planning and Implementation Oversight","Oversee policy planning and implementation",""],[1,"179","12","Annual Budget Alignment and Legislative Support for Plan Implementation","Approve annual budgets and ensure alignment with plan · Oversight function on the MDAs'Plan implementation · Enact requisite legislations in relation to the Plan",""],[1,"179","14","Policy Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","Coordinate, monitor and ensure full implementation of government policies and programmes",""],[1,"179","14","Annual Policy Prioritization Alignment Exercise","Ensure strategic policy priorities agreed annually at the annual agenda-setting and prioritization exercise are consistent with the MTNDP",""],[1,"179","14","Nigeria Development Report Submission","Submit the Nigeria Development Report (NDR) to the Presidency and National Assembly",""],[1,"179","16","Inter-Ministerial Planning and Budget Coordination Mechanism","Ensure inter-ministerial coordination of plans and budget",""],[1,"179","16","Policy Proposal Implementation and M&E Planning Requirement","Ensure that policy proposals put forward by MDAs for the consideration of the Federal Executive Council have clear implementation and M&E plans",""],[1,"179","16","Technical Advisory Support to the Steering Committee","Advise the steering committee on questions requiring technical input",""],[1,"179","16","DPRS Inter-Ministerial Coordination Arrangement","Ensure inter-ministerial coordination through the representatives of the DPRS across all MDAs",""],[1,"179","17","Plan Activation and Alignment Mechanism","Work with all actors to activate the plan and ensure effective alignment of the priorities in the MTNDP, the annual national budgets, the priority policies and programmes across all stakeholders",""],[1,"179","17","MDA Implementation Capacity Support","Expand the implementation capacity of MDAs by working closely with them and providing execution support",""],[1,"180","9","Budget Appropriation Alignment with Plan Execution Timeline","The budget appropriation process should be aligned with the plan execution timeline and disbursement delays avoided.",""],[1,"180","13","Macroeconomic Policy Coordination Framework","Thus, strengthening the coordination of monetary, fiscal, trade and industrial policies, in a manner that recognises and resolves any trade-offs or indeed, tensions, across these policies to maintain the optimal growth trajectory, is critical.",""],[1,"180","14","Strengthening Statutory Fiscal, Monetary and Trade Institutions","the government will strengthen the statutory fiscal, monetary and trade institutions to deliver on their core mandates.",""],[1,"180","14","Policy Coordination through Existing Fiscal and Monetary Committees","This is to acknowledge the need for improved policy coordination.",""],[1,"181","2","Legislative Framework to Prevent Policy Reversals","the government will establish structures to ensure that this Plan is implemented throughout the 2021-2025 period by enacting appropriate legislation to prevent policy reversals and ensure implementation.",""],[1,"181","5","Plan Implementation Enabling Measures","successful implementation of the Plan will require legislative actions, a strong funding strategy, a robust M&E framework, citizens and stakeholders'engagement.",""]],"2":[[1,"5","1","Inclusive Participation and Citizen Engagement in Planning","This was deliberately done for inclusiveness, participation and citizen engagement to ensure no one is left behind.",""],[1,"11","5","Stakeholder Communication and Engagement Strategy","The government will also seek to develop an efficient communication strategy to create awareness among the stakeholders and their engagement in the implementation.",""],[1,"27","19","Bottom-Up Stakeholder Engagement in Development Planning","Need to adequately engage stakeholders and beneficiaries in the formulation and implementation of development plans and programmes through the adoption of a bottom-up approach.",""],[1,"181","3","Stakeholder Engagement and Public Communication for Planning Participation","The government recognizes the importance of effective communication and stakeholder engagement in mobilising the Nigerian citizenry to participate in the planning process.",""],[1,"181","4","Stakeholder Communication and Citizen Participation Strategy","Thus, the government will deploy the necessary communication strategies to ensure broad participation of the citizens to take ownership and actively track the implementation process.",""]],"3":[[1,"10","5","Enabling Investment Climate and Business Environment Reform","the government will create an enabling investment climate and business environment, underpinned by a highly capable, motivated and well-resourced world-class public service.",""],[1,"34","13","Institutional Reforms to Improve the Private Sector Environment","Institutional reforms and measures to create a conducive environment for private economic activity,",""],[1,"37","2","Ease of Doing Business Reform","Government will sustain current efforts at improving the business and investment climate via the enhancement of the ease of doing business reforms, the fight against corruption and strengthening of institutions to lay a foundation for future growth.",""],[1,"39","9","Private-Sector Crowding-In Policy Framework","the plan assigns a critical role to the government in complementing private-sector activities. The public sector will focus on implementing policies that crowd in the private sector.",""],[1,"55","8","Industrial Policy Reform and Business Environment Programme","Industrial policy reforms and enabling business environment programmes focused on developing policies that ensure business growth for manufacturing companies.",""],[1,"57","3","Manufacturing Sector Enabling Environment and Investment Promotion","Nigeria will accelerate progress by removing manufacturing impediments and creating an enabling environment for large-scale industrial investment, while at the same time promoting the development of small and medium-sized manufacturing firms.",""],[1,"57","5","Manufacturing Climate Improvement Programme","As part of its efforts to improve the business environment for manufacturing, the government will simultaneously improve infrastructure, deepen and expand existing enabling business environment reforms, and align fiscal and monetary policy to strengthen the economy.",""],[1,"58","2","Manufacturing Policy and Regulatory Review","Review existing manufacturing policies, laws and regulations to ensure business friendliness and trade.",""],[1,"58","8","Enabling Environment for Private Investment","Government will demonstrate its commitment towards creating an enabling environment for private investment to thrive in the country.",""],[1,"72","1","Business Environment Reform Programme","This was achieved through the concerted action by the Presidential Enabling Business Environment Council (PEBEC), established to tackle the constraints associated with doing business in Nigeria.",""],[1,"72","3","Public Sector Process Improvement Initiatives","The government invested in process improvement initiatives to increase efficiencies in public sector agencies and reduce overheads with a view to improving the business environment.",""],[1,"72","3","Business Registration Process Simplification","The Corporate Affairs Commission (CAC) simplified company registration processes that reduced overall processing time by half.",""],[1,"72","3","Centralised Tax E-Payment Channels","The Federal Inland Revenue Service (FIRS) launched centralised e-payment channels contributing to a 20 percent reduction in the time businesses spent on documentation and payment of taxes.",""],[1,"72","4","Airport Service Efficiency Improvements","Federal Airports Authority of Nigeria (FAAN) improved efficiencies and overall user experience at airports by eliminating passenger service charge (PSC) stickers and manual check-in bag searches.",""],[1,"72","4","Digital E-Visa Processing Initiative","a new immigration initiative fully digitised e-visa processes guaranteeing visa approvals in 48 hours was introduced.",""],[1,"72","4","NAFDAC Registration Process Reengineering","the National Agency for Food and Drug Administration and Control (NAFDAC) reengineered registration processes and reduced processing time from almost a year to less than three months.",""],[1,"72","5","Business Environment Reform Package","Lagos and Kano States introduced reforms to further ease the business environment for the private sector.",""],[1,"72","5","Specialized Commercial Claims Court Divisions","Between 2018 and 2019, both states introduced specialized court divisions to fast- track resolution of small commercial claims involving liquidated money demand cases of N5 million and below within 60 days and facilitate electronic access to judgments.",""],[1,"72","5","E-Planning Platform for Property and Permits","They both also implemented an e-planning platform, reducing the cost of property registration and obtaining construction permits by up to 25 percent.",""],[1,"73","3","Business Environment Reform and Process Automation","There is an opportunity to build on existing progress made by the Presidential Enabling Business Environment Council (PEBEC) to automate and improve the quality of existing integrated and industrially relevant processes.",""],[1,"74","2","Institutional Framework Harmonization for Business Environment Improvement","Strengthen and harmonize institutional frameworks to improve on the business environment and competitiveness.",""],[1,"74","3","Business Environment Institutional Reform","Institutional frameworks for several aspects of doing business in Nigeria will be reviewed and strengthened to reduce time and increase efficiencies.",""],[1,"74","8","Business Environment Budget Tracking Mechanism","Going forward, a tracking mechanism to determine the allocations to business environment, trade, and competitiveness through federal, state and local government budgets will be developed by activating existing codes in the Chart of Accounts.",""],[1,"74","8","Business Environment Reform Financing","Part of this funding will go to the funding of ongoing and new reforms initiatives by the Presidential Enabling Business Environment Council (PEBEC), the Nigerian Investment Promotion Commission (NIPC) and their equivalent institutions at the sub-national level.",""],[1,"74","8","Private Sector Co-Financing for Business Environment Investment","Given the required investment in the sector, public spending will be enhanced by private sector financing; however, the government will still undertake significant investments in the sector in the short-term owing to the current incentive structure in the private sector.",""],[1,"74","9","Business Environment Reform and Regulatory Harmonization Initiative","The government will continue to build on recent improvements in its business environment through targeted initiatives to harmonize regulations and eliminate constraints in infrastructure and other critical areas as well as create a level playing field.",""],[1,"160","14","Business Environment and Infrastructure Improvement","This will be achieved by implementing the strategies identified in other chapters of this plan including improving the business environment and infrastructure stock to stimulate private sector activity and resolving other sector-specific constraints.",""],[1,"164","14","Targeted Sector Investment Programme","Targeted investments in promising sectors such as agriculture, manufacturing, construction, education, mining, ICT, health, sports, tourism, hospitality, and entertainment will spur massive employment opportunities.",""],[1,"166","5","Innovation and Indigenous Technology for Waste Management","Government will encourage innovation and indigenous technology for proper waste management to spur employment generation",""],[1,"166","7","Petroleum Industry Act Implementation","Full implementation of the Petroleum Industry Act to unlock potentials in the oil and gas sector that has both backward and forward linkages;",""],[1,"166","9","Mining Sector Regulatory Framework for Investment Expansion","Government's plan to provide the regulatory framework to increase investment and activities of large-scale mining corporations and artisanal miners in the solid minerals and mining sector will contribute significantly to job creation.",""],[1,"166","10","Structural Reforms in the Culture, Creative, Tourism and Hospitality Sector","Government will eliminate the binding constraints through the implementation of structural reforms in the Culture, Creative, Tourism and Hospitality Sector to foster job creation across diverse areas like film production, theatre arts, music, fashion, art, television, radio, sports, information technology, media, advertising and tourism.",""],[1,"166","11","Presidential Enabling Business Environment Council Action Plan Implementation","There will be effective implementation of the Presidential Enabling Business Environment Council action plans at the national and subnational levels to boost the performance of the real sector while increasing investor confidence in fostering job creation.",""],[1,"166","12","National Trade Policy Framework","Government will also ensure the conceptualization and implementation of a comprehensive National Trade Policy framework to boost enterprise competitiveness at all stages of the supply chain.",""],[1,"166","14","Land Administration Law Review and Transparent Real Estate Processing","Government will review existing land administration laws and ensure transparent processing in the real estate sector to spur real sector growth for employment generation.",""],[1,"167","2","Investment Facilitation in High-Growth Sectors","The government will facilitate investments in high- growth sectors such as light manufacturing, value- added agriculture, the digital economy and mining to create jobs and improve citizens' welfare.",""],[1,"167","3","Efficient Financial System Support","Government will further support an efficient financial system to provide opportunities for mobilising savings and investments that are job-generating.",""],[1,"185","1","Tax Base Broadening and Private Sector Investment Promotion","Nigeria will generate revenue by broadening the tax base and enhancing the capacity of the private sector through creating investment opportunities and deliberate policy engagements and incentives.",""],[1,"185","1","Growth Funds and Public-Private Partnership Financing Mechanisms","Funding vehicles such as growth funds and public-private partnerships (PPP) will be set up to finance the Plan.",""],[1,"185","1","Fiscal Discipline and Governance Efficiency Reform","Additionally, there will be a focus on fiscal discipline through institutional compliance with the fiscal responsibility act, deliberate policy, and drastic reduction of inefficiencies in governance.",""],[1,"185","1","Contract Cost Control and Anti-Inflation Measures","Other measures that will be implemented include a deliberate policy to address inflation of contracts and high cost of projects, and privatisation of some public enterprises that can be self-financing.",""],[1,"185","1","Privatisation of Self-Financing Public Enterprises","Other measures that will be implemented include a deliberate policy to address inflation of contracts and high cost of projects, and privatisation of some public enterprises that can be self-financing.",""],[1,"185","1","Transparency and Accountability Campaigns","Above all, transparency and accountability campaigns will be vigorously pursued and implemented.",""],[1,"185","6","Plan Implementation Financing Assurance","Ensure that adequate finance is available for implementing the Plan;",""],[1,"185","8","Strategy for Revenue Growth Initiatives","The target is to increase national government revenue up to 15 percent of GDP at the end of 2025 to reduce the deficit-GDP ratio with the implementation of the recently launched 'Strategy for Revenue Growth Initiatives (SRGIs)'.",""],[1,"185","8","Operational Efficiency Improvement for Government-Owned Enterprises","These initiatives focus on optimizing the operational and collection efficiency of GOEs, restricting the cost-to-revenue ratio",""],[1,"186","1","Debt Management Strategy Improvement","Thus, the government will improve on current debt management strategies to ensure sustainability.",""],[1,"186","3","Alternative Funding Initiatives for Private Capital Investment","Thus, to address the challenges above, the government will adopt three alternative funding initiatives:",""],[1,"186","6","Nigeria Investment and Growth Fund","Establishing the Nigeria Investment and Growth Fund (NIG-Fund).",""]],"4":[[1,"56","13","Long-Term Manufacturing Finance Support","Development finance institutions, such as the Bank of Industry, are about the only institutions that can finance long-term projects of up to 10 years with moratorium opportunities due to their ability to raise long-term capital.",""],[1,"57","10","Manufacturing Financing Expansion","Increase financing for manufacturing activities",""],[1,"57","18","Manufacturing Expansion Finance Facility","Launch interventions to finance manufacturing expansion: Improve the availability and affordability of long-term single-digit financial facilities for Nigerian manufacturers.",""],[1,"58","6","Strengthen State-Owned Development Finance Institutions","Strengthen state-owned development finance institutions by injecting additional equity capital towards enabling them to support enterprises more effectively.",""],[1,"58","7","Manufacturing Sector Financing Optimization","the government will optimise financing for various initiatives aimed at eliminating binding constraints in the manufacturing sector.",""],[1,"58","7","Industrial Investment Promotion","the government will prioritise the promotion of investment in the industry.",""],[1,"58","8","Public Investment Support for Manufacturing Growth and Competitiveness","Within the planning period, an estimated public investment of about N868.56bn is committed to complement private sector investment on this sector to achieve the objectives.",""],[1,"58","8","Industrial Development Capital Expenditure Prioritisation","Along with the Government's contribution to relevant ministries' capital expenditures, other government agencies involved in industrial development in the three-tiers of government will use their resources to prioritise initiatives aimed at fostering manufacturing growth and competitiveness.",""],[1,"58","9","Manufacturing Sector Revitalization and Value Chain Linkage Support","Nigeria will facilitate the rebirth of the manufacturing sector by improving the enabling environment, crowding in additional capital, and strengthening value chain linkages.",""],[1,"163","6","Development Bank of Nigeria MSME Financial Support","The Development Bank of Nigeria (DBN) provided financial backing to MSMEs to drive job creation.",""],[1,"163","11","MSME Lending and Credit Guarantee Support Programme","DBN lending programme issued N191 billion to 34,144 MSMEs to ease access to finance across various sectors of the economy, with a particular focus on youth and women start-ups.",""],[1,"163","11","MSME Capacity-Building Programme","The bank also built the capacity of 125 MSMEs to increase operational efficiency and developed credit guarantees to support MSME lending.",""],[1,"165","10","MSME Business Viability Support Programme","Support MSMEs business viability to spur job creation through standardization of operations and increasing access to finance.",""],[1,"165","11","MSME Training and Mentoring for Formalization","Support the growth, professionalization, and transition of MSMEs from the informal to the formal market through training and mentoring, which will ensure their sustainability and bolster their hiring",""],[1,"165","12","MSME Finance Access Facilitation","Increased access to finance by MSMEs to be facilitated with support from the DBN.",""],[1,"167","6","MSME Formalization Support","The 2025 vision will build on past plans' progress to support the formalization process of MSME's and align strategies across high growth sectors to facilitate massive job creation.",""]],"5":[[1,"33","5","Regional Development and Population Management Interventions","Interventions to foster regional development and aid population management will be introduced to reduce uneven development across the country.",""],[1,"34","3","Population and ID Management System Strengthening","strengthening existing population and ID management systems by supporting family planning measures and adopting technological tools.",""],[1,"144","1","Robust Population Management System","A robust population management system will be necessary to strike a balance between the country's growth and its resource availability.",""],[1,"144","2","Population and Identity Management System Strengthening","This Plan will, therefore, take proactive measures to improve current population and identity management systems and ensure that Nigeria's development is sustainable and inclusive.",""],[1,"144","3","Accelerating the Realization of Demographic Dividend","Accordingly, Chapter 26A is devoted to Accelerating the Realization of Demographic Dividend in Nigeria during this plan period.",""],[1,"144","6","Periodic Population Enumeration","undertake periodical enumeration of population through sample surveys and population censuses;",""],[1,"144","7","Continuous Planning Machinery","· establish and maintain a machinery for continuous",""],[1,"144","10","Population Data Publication and Dissemination","publish and provide information and data on population for the purpose of facilitating economic and development planning;",""],[1,"144","11","Enumerator Appointment and Training","appoint and train or arrange for the appointment and training of enumerators or the staff of the Commission.",""]],"6":[[1,"34","1","Multilateral Leadership Strengthening","Interventions implemented will include, among others, ... reinforcing Nigeria's regional and global leadership role through increased multilateral leadership.",""],[1,"113","3","Economic Diplomacy through Trade and Investment Agreements","Economic diplomacy: Through bilateral-investment agreements and multilateral-trade agreements such as AfCFTA, African Growth Opportunity Act (AGOA), ECOWAS Trade Liberalization Scheme (ETLS), Nigeria has forged relationships with regional, continental, and global powers.",""],[1,"113","11","Creative Industry Intervention Funding","The creative industry benefited from government intervention funds that boosted their production for a global audience.",""],[1,"113","12","Nigeria's Economic Diplomacy Initiative","In economic diplomacy, the Nigerian government launched Nigeria's Economic Diplomacy Initiative",""],[1,"114","1","Nigerian Economic Diaspora Initiative","(NEDI) - an initiative of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in collaboration with the Federal Ministry of Industry, Trade and Investment, the Nigerian Investment Promotion Commission (NIPC) and the Nigerian Export Promotion Council (NEPC) on April 8th, 2018.","Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Federal Ministry of Industry, Trade and Investment | Nigerian Investment Promotion Commission (NIPC) | Nigerian Export Promotion Council (NEPC)"],[1,"114","2","AfCFTA Trade Integration and Export Expansion","The government also signed the African Continental Free Trade Agreement (AfCFTA), on July 7th, 2019, which holds key opportunities to increase Nigeria's non-oil exports within the continent, provides rules-based protection for domestic industries, while advancing the development of the continent.",""],[1,"114","4","Strengthening Trade and Investment Ties","Strengthening trade and investment ties, engaging the diaspora population in promoting made-in-Nigeria brands, supporting Nigerian enterprises to penetrate new markets, formalising and promoting the export of services, etc are some of the strategic tools that have been underutilised in Nigeria's foreign policy and",""],[1,"114","4","Diaspora Promotion of Made-in-Nigeria Brands","Strengthening trade and investment ties, engaging the diaspora population in promoting made-in-Nigeria brands, supporting Nigerian enterprises to penetrate new markets, formalising and promoting the export of services, etc are some of the strategic tools that have been underutilised in Nigeria's foreign policy and",""],[1,"114","4","Support for Nigerian Enterprises to Enter New Markets","Strengthening trade and investment ties, engaging the diaspora population in promoting made-in-Nigeria brands, supporting Nigerian enterprises to penetrate new markets, formalising and promoting the export of services, etc are some of the strategic tools that have been underutilised in Nigeria's foreign policy and",""],[1,"114","4","Formalisation and Promotion of Services Exports","Strengthening trade and investment ties, engaging the diaspora population in promoting made-in-Nigeria brands, supporting Nigerian enterprises to penetrate new markets, formalising and promoting the export of services, etc are some of the strategic tools that have been underutilised in Nigeria's foreign policy and",""],[1,"114","6","Foreign Investment Tax Incentives","The government has also rolled out attractive tax incentives for foreign investors",""],[1,"114","7","AfCFTA Trade and Investment Exploitation Strategy","Nigeria, as the largest economy in Africa, will take advantage of this free trade agreement, especially that AfCFTA is now one of the world's largest trade blocs34.",""],[1,"114","7","Local Capacity and Value Chain Upgrading","However, this opportunity can only be maximized if Nigeria boosts its local capacity and builds well-equipped value chains to strengthen the competitiveness of domestic producers.",""],[1,"115","3","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion through Economic Diplomacy","Become an increasingly attractive destination for foreign direct investment by harnessing and strengthening the economic components of Nigeria's foreign policy and international relations.",""],[1,"115","4","Strengthen Missions Abroad for Investment and Cooperation Identification","improve the performance of its missions abroad especially in identifying untapped investment opportunities and areas of cooperation in the host country.",""],[1,"115","10","International Trade and Investment Mainstreaming","Promote Nigeria's economic position and improve the country's economic growth by mainstreaming international trade and investment.",""],[1,"115","10","Trade Agreement Negotiation and Implementation","Nigeria will participate effectively in trade and investment agreement negotiations and bodies; implement existing agreements;",""],[1,"115","10","International Investment and Export Promotion Programme","and embark on aggressive international investment and export promotion programmes anchored on institutional and regulatory reforms at home.",""],[1,"115","13","Cultural Diplomacy for Tourism and Creative Industry Promotion","Drive tourism and investment in the country's arts and culture industry through cultural diplomacy.",""],[1,"115","13","International Cultural and Sporting Event Engagement","Nigeria will solidify its presence in global cultural and sporting events, and actively leverage diplomatic representations abroad to drive cultural exchange.",""],[1,"115","13","Cultural Event Facilitation and Creative Industry Support","Efforts will also focus on the facilitation of cultural events in Nigeria and other countries and support to the creative industry, to strengthen Nigeria's position as a burgeoning global culture capital.",""],[1,"142","5","AfCFTA Market Access and Labour Mobility Initiative","Furthermore, the Africa Continental Free Trade Area gives Nigerian workers including women, the opportunity to access decent work in 53 other African countries and gives entrepreneurs (including women) access to the world's largest single market - the Africa Continental market.",""]],"7":[[1,"68","3","Digital Enablement for Arts, Culture, and Intellectual Property Industries","The intellectual property industries represented in this sector are all connected and, when enabled by digital platforms and technology, can create millions of jobs for Nigerians",""],[1,"70","16","CCHT Sector Policy Reform and Revenue Enhancement","Enact new policies and implement existing policies that will increase the CCHT sector revenue generation potential.",""],[1,"70","16","Intellectual Property Protection and Piracy Prevention Reform","Policies that stifle business growth will be reviewed and amended, especially for intellectual property (IP) protection and piracy prevention.",""],[1,"70","16","Nigerian Copyright Commission Capacity Support","The Nigerian Copyright Commission will also be provided with support to address copyright infringement issues.",""],[1,"70","16","Copyright Infringement Awareness Campaigns","There will also be an expansion of awareness campaigns to inform the public on copyright infringement laws, and disciplinary actions.",""],[1,"70","16","Copyright Policy Process Training","As part of efforts to strengthen the capacity of the Nigerian Copyrights Commission, policymakers and commission personnel will be trained on policy processes.",""],[1,"70","16","Tax Law and Regulation Review for CCHT Trade","Tax laws and regulations affecting the CCHT sectors will be reviewed and strengthened to eliminate bottlenecks affecting the AfCFTA market opportunities for CCHT businesses.",""]],"8":[[1,"90","2","Affordable Housing Construction and Mortgage Support Initiatives","The government has strived to stimulate construction by building affordable houses and overcoming critical constraints in the housing sector.",""],[1,"90","3","Site and Services Scheme for Housing Development","the Site and Services Scheme initiative was created for the government to provide support services such as (roads, culverts, external drains, external electrification and water supply) to encourage allottees to access their plots and build houses of their choice.",""],[1,"90","4","National Housing Programme","The National Housing Programme has focused on stimulating the economy and creating a large employment opportunity.",""],[1,"91","6","Affordable Housing Construction Programme","Building affordable houses to fill the shortfalls will increase demand for housing-related financing and drive liquidity of mortgage finance products.",""],[1,"91","9","Affordable Housing Policy Framework","Nigeria strives to provide affordable housing to all Nigerians through a strategic policy framework to bridge any gap between supply and demand by 2025.",""],[1,"91","12","Affordable Housing Access Improvement","improve access to affordable housing in Nigeria",""],[1,"92","1","Urban Slum Renewal and Affordable Housing Programme","Urban renewal of slums with social and affordable housing by 2.76 percent annually will align with Sustainable Development Goals.",""],[1,"92","2","Housing Supply Expansion and Social Housing Support","Expand the funding base and capital formation in the real estate sector.",""],[1,"92","2","Affordable Rental Housing and Vacant Housing Utilization Programme","The government will bridge the gap between housing demand and supply constraints; create rental housing opportunities for at least 500,000 citizens; reduce the demand for multiple years' rent payment; bring unused and empty houses into use especially in urban areas; make housing payment affordable by matching it with income receipts;",""],[1,"92","2","Statewide Site and Service Housing Scheme","deliver site and service schemes that engender at least 50,000 plots of land in each state of the federation including the FCT for housing development.",""],[1,"93","6","Affordable Housing Construction Programme","Both Federal and state governments will make the construction of affordable housing a priority to bridge any housing deficit, reduce slums and create opportunities for sustainable urban regeneration in Nigeria.",""],[1,"93","6","Inclusive National Housing Policy","The achievement of these goals will be underpinned by an inclusive national housing policy that will fully unlock the socio-economic potential of the housing and urban development sector.",""],[1,"93","6","Rural Development and Urban Development Expansion","The disparity between urban cities and the rural communities will be bridged through efforts to engender rural development across all states to ensure access to infrastructural facilities.",""],[1,"93","6","Urban Development Acceleration Initiative","Thus, efforts towards facilitating urban development across the country will be increased.",""]],"9":[[1,"29","13","Human Capital Skills Development and STI Investment","Nigeria will prioritise the building of the skills base of its populace, and invest in science, technology and innovation to drive competitiveness and unlock the potential of various sectors.",""],[1,"30","1","Technical and Professional Skills Development Initiative","technical and professional skills so as to take advantage of the emerging jobs.",""],[1,"41","4","Human Capital Development Capacity Building for Women and Youth","attention will also be given to the current social investment programmes to prioritise human capital development via relevant capacity building programs targeted at women and youths.",""],[1,"46","3","Knowledge and Skills Transfer with Investment Inflows","Emphasis will be placed on the transfer of knowledge, skills and capabilities in tandem with investment inflows.",""],[1,"66","8","Research and Development and Skills Development Investment","Invest in R&D and skills development to enhance greater local knowledge generation and improve sector competitiveness.",""],[1,"66","8","Workforce Upskilling Initiative","The Government will invest in up-skilling initiatives to build workforce capacity and upgrade existing geoscience institutions to enable them to function as world-class innovative and technology-driven institutions with the ability to generate qualitative geological data and upgrade the",""],[1,"66","8","Geoscience Institution Upgrade Programme","The Government will invest in up-skilling initiatives to build workforce capacity and upgrade existing geoscience institutions to enable them to function as world-class innovative and technology-driven institutions with the ability to generate qualitative geological data and upgrade the",""],[1,"98","1","Science, Technology, and Innovation Framework Enhancement","Achieving these overarching goals requires an enhanced framework for science, technology, and innovation.",""],[1,"98","3","National Research and Innovation Bill and Governance Institutions","The Bill seeks the establishment of the National Research and Innovation Council and a National Research and Innovation Foundation to administer a dedicated fund for research and innovation.",""],[1,"98","4","Pilot Technology Incubation Centres","The federal government is partnering with states to create pilot Technology Incubation Centres to strengthen technological development.",""],[1,"98","5","Nanotechnology Policy Development and Promotion","the government is developing and promoting a nanotechnology policy to accelerate research and development to produce nanotechnology products for the upgrading of industrial processes.",""],[1,"98","5","Science, Technology and Innovation Policy Review and Amendment","several old policies, including the National Science, Technology and Innovation (STI) Policy, are under review for amendment.",""],[1,"99","10","Accelerated Science, Technology and Innovation Agenda","Nigeria will pursue an aggressive agenda of accelerated science, technology and innovation; laying the foundation for a science-based and ready workforce that can apply scientific thought and concepts to solve a broad sub-set of Nigerian problems.",""],[1,"99","10","National Innovation System Development","The country will support the evolution of the national system of innovation by creating the factors and conditions essential for innovators, creators, scientists and technologists to translate ideas into products and services that scale into national and global markets.",""],[1,"99","11","Science, Technology and Innovation Policy Harmonization and STEM Coordination","Achieve harmonization in science, technology and innovation policy framework and coordination for Science, Technology, Engineering & Mathematics (STEM) including effective and coordinated curriculum development at all levels of our educational system in synergy with the Federal Ministry of Education by 2025.","Federal Ministry of Education"],[1,"99","12","National Innovation Ecosystem Development","Build a National Innovation Ecosystem that integrates all multi-stakeholders across the three tiers of government, the private sector and civil society groups to mobilize resources and commitment to build a national innovation system that encompasses new products and services that align with national and global benchmarks.",""],[1,"99","15","Technology Transfer and Acquisition Agenda","Pursue an aggressive technology transfer, acquisition and exchange agenda to deepen technology know- how in areas that limit Nigeria's economic productivity (mechanization, manufacturing machinery, tools, digital industrialization, fabrication, 3D printing, artificial intelligence and cyber-physical systems) and strengthen the National Office for Technology Acquisition & Promotion (NOTAP) in registering patents, promote and protect indigenous intellectual properties arising from such innovations to lay the foundation for high tech migration based FDI projects.",""],[1,"99","16","Systemic Triple Helix Policy for R&D Investment","Create policy incentives to support increased investments in R&D by developing a Systemic Triple Helix policy that supports Government-Academia- Industry (GIA) linkages that will support Nigeria's industrial and technological growth by 2025.",""],[1,"99","17","Technology and Innovation Centres for Global Competitiveness","Develop an innovation driven economy that attracts FDIs and domestic investments by setting up Six (6) Technology and Innovation Centres for Global Competitiveness involving the private sector, Research Institutes/Academia and the government across the six geo-political zones by 2025.",""],[1,"99","18","SHETSCO Science and Technology Park Development","Complete on-going collaboration with UNESCO on the development of the SHETSCO Science & Technology Park by 2025.",""],[1,"100","1","Digitally Driven Innovation Hub","functional, robust and up to date digitally driven innovation hub to support young innovators and inventors to close the WIPO innovation index gap.",""],[1,"100","3","Science and Technology Priority Project Investment","Allocations have been made to priority projects in the sector as well as projects essential to the operations of the relevant government MDAs both at the federal and state levels.",""],[1,"100","3","Innovation Trust Fund and Pre-tax Levy Financing Options","In addition, MDAs shall explore funding options which include pooled blended (public-private-development sector) innovation trust fund, strategic options for pre-tax levies on Medium and Big Technology Related/ Manufacturing Companies,","MDAs"],[1,"100","4","Disbursement of TETFund Research Fund to Universities","Disbursement of TETFund's existing $3.9 million research fund to universities.",""],[1,"100","5","Federal-State Science, Technology and Innovation Coordination","Strategic cooperation and coordination between Federal and State Governments is crucial to achieving the country's national policies on science, technology, and innovation.",""],[1,"100","5","State Innovation Incubator and Hub Expansion","States need to provide an enabling environment for a mature funding ecosystem to evolve and support the conditions for at least 5 new Incubators and innovation hubs in every state, which are focused on creating the support ecosystem (research, universities, government, funders) for Entrepreneurs to thrive.",""],[1,"100","5","Multi-Level Curriculum Development Collaboration","Collaboration between State, Local and Federal Government on curriculum development for primary, secondary, tertiary (vocational & technical education) and higher education that will improve Nigeria's scientific, technological and innovation base remains important.",""]],"10":[[1,"28","20","Border Anti-Smuggling and Trade Formalization Measures","Opportunity to address smuggling at borders and formalize ongoing border trade to capture revenue.",""],[1,"34","1","Border Control and Anti-Terrorism Security Measures","Interventions implemented will include, among others, increasing border control and domestic anti-terrorism measures through bilateral security agreements and support to border control agencies;",""],[1,"109","17","Border Security and Patrol Strengthening","tighten border security and patrol",""],[1,"109","18","Joint Border Security Coordination in Border Towns","Setting up joint security responsibilities between customs, NIS, the military and the local vigilante in border towns to reduce incursion of illegal aliens",""],[1,"109","19","Border Management Standard Operating Procedure Improvement","Improve standard operating procedure for border management",""],[1,"109","20","Innovative Migration Control Mechanism","Implement innovative mechanism for migration control",""],[1,"109","22","Bilateral and Multilateral Security Agreements","Sign bilateral and multilateral security agreements with countries to enhance security",""]],"11":[[1,"9","10","Security and Good Governance Capacity Strengthening Framework","to build a solid framework and enhancing capacities to strengthen security and ensure good governance",""],[1,"10","5","Public Service Capacity and Governance Strengthening","the government will create an enabling investment climate and business environment, underpinned by a highly capable, motivated and well-resourced world-class public service.",""],[1,"10","5","Open and Transparent High-Performance Governance Reform","The rejuvenated public service will drive open, transparent and high-performance governance at all levels.",""],[1,"27","20","Plan Implementation Commitment and Political Will Strengthening","Need to develop the commitment and political will to implement plans in an effective and efficient manner, as poor implementation has been the bane in achieving plan outcomes in Nigeria.",""],[1,"33","1","Governance Strengthening and Institutional Capacity Building Framework","Build a solid framework and enhance capacities to strengthen security and ensure good governance: Ensuring good governance is a necessary enabler to promote equity and improve the overall efficiency of public service delivery.",""],[1,"34","1","Intergovernmental Coordination for Public Sector Efficiency","Interventions implemented will include, among others, enhancing coordination between the various tiers of government, for improved public sector efficiency;",""],[1,"34","15","Institutional Reform for Economic Sectors and Public Institutions","Institutional reformation of economic sectors, public sector, law enforcement, judiciary, and secure property rights, including intellectual property.",""],[1,"37","2","Anti-Corruption and Institutional Strengthening Measures","Government will sustain current efforts at improving the business and investment climate via the enhancement of the ease of doing business reforms, the fight against corruption and strengthening of institutions to lay a foundation for future growth.",""],[1,"43","5","Civil Service Reform for MDA Rationalisation","Recommendations on civil service reforms will be implemented to cut the cost of running government through policies that facilitate merger and streamlining of overlapping MDAs functions and imposition of moratorium on the creation of new agencies.",""]],"12":[[1,"29","18","Educational Curriculum Revision and Access Expansion","will revise its educational curriculum to improve on educational standards, and access to further and higher education for the youths to acquire both vocational,",""],[1,"34","2","Teacher Training for Education Quality Improvement","Major strategic measures will be aimed at improving human capital development by (i) improving the quality of education for the sector to meet international standards through teacher training",""],[1,"118","6","Female Scholarship Scheme for Girls in TVET and STEM","a Female Scholarship Scheme was introduced to improve enrolment of girls in TVET and STEM",""],[1,"118","7","Proactive Teacher Training Plan","Implementation of a proactive Teacher Training Plan by the Federal Government in collaboration with States under which 2,288,091 professional teachers have been registered and licensed after passing qualifying examinations;",""],[1,"118","8","Teacher, Quality Assurance, and EMIS Officer Digital Skills Training","The registration and training of 7,400 Teachers, Quality Assurance Evaluators and Education Management and Information System (EMIS) officers, at all levels of education in Nigeria to bridge the digital skills gap, given the current emphasis on digital literacy;",""],[1,"118","9","National Skills Qualifications Framework Development","The development of a National Skills Qualifications Framework (NSQF) to stimulate and promote on a massive scale relevant skills and provide local content across all sectors of the economy;",""],[1,"118","10","Research and Innovation Steering Committee","Inauguration of a Research and Innovation Steering Committee to drive massive research and innovation activities in tertiary institutions in Nigeria.",""],[1,"118","18","Private Sector Education Regulation Framework","A robust legal instrument is needed to regulate private sector involvement in education to align quality standards and assure",""],[1,"120","2","Educational Policy and Curriculum Review","A key thrust of this plan on Education and Human Resources Development will be to review educational policies and curriculum to ensure education is demand driven and the integration of apprenticeship programme as a path to education and empowerment.",""],[1,"120","2","Apprenticeship Programme Integration","A key thrust of this plan on Education and Human Resources Development will be to review educational policies and curriculum to ensure education is demand driven and the integration of apprenticeship programme as a path to education and empowerment.",""],[1,"120","3","Competence-Based Curriculum Reform","Nigeria will overhaul its educational system to meet international standards with the ability to employ an innovative, dynamic competence-based curriculum implemented by committed teachers.",""],[1,"120","18","Teacher Training and Competence-Based Curriculum Support","The Government will significantly improve enrolment rates across the country and harmonize teaching standards.",""],[1,"120","18","Teacher Incentive and Working Conditions Improvement","In return, the Government will incentivize teachers with better remuneration and working conditions particularly in underserved communities.",""],[1,"120","18","Student Learning Materials Production Programme","To that end, the Government will engage in the massive production of student learning materials.",""],[1,"121","3","Safe Schools Initiative Harmonisation and Adoption","Harmonise and adopt the State with the National Safe Schools Initiative to secure the premises and communities for learning, without disruptions",""]],"13":[[1,"30","2","Health Development Policy","be proactive in its health development policy, against the background of the experience gained from the Covid-19 pandemic",""],[1,"34","2","Health System Service Delivery Capacity Strengthening","and (ii) strengthening Nigeria's health system service delivery capacity, to significantly improve quality and become a healthier, more productive nation.",""],[1,"41","6","Human Development Investment and Social Protection Strategy","The plan will prioritise investment in human development to provide equitable access to quality education and health services to all Nigerians.",""],[1,"42","2","Social Sector Growth Facilitation","Nigeria will take bold steps to facilitate the growth of the social sector for the realization of this plan's goals.",""],[1,"42","2","Private Investment Incentives for Health and Education Jobs","In the social sector, jobs will be generated in health and education with the right incentives to attract domestic and foreign private investment.",""],[1,"122","2","Secondary and Tertiary Healthcare Strengthening","The policy thrusts of the ERGP and the Vision include revitalizing the primary healthcare system, strengthening secondary and tertiary healthcare delivery, expanding the National Health Insurance Scheme (NHIS) to achieve universal health coverage (UHC), and building the capacity of health care personnel to improve service delivery.",""],[1,"124","25","National Health System Upgrade","the Government of Nigeria will implement six strategic measures to upgrade the national health system and ensure that every Nigerian has access to quality healthcare.",""],[1,"124","26","Health System Service Delivery Strengthening","Strengthen Nigeria's health system service delivery capacity to significantly improve quality and become a healthier nation.",""],[1,"124","29","Healthcare Financing and Facility Upgrade Initiative","Secure healthcare financing to upgrade health facilities and fund expanded access to health services in Nigeria.",""],[1,"125","6","Basic Infrastructure Upgrading for Health Facilities","Improve access to basic infrastructure such as access to water and electricity in hospitals and other medical facilities.",""],[1,"125","13","Health Infrastructure Upgrade and Financing Package","To achieve this goal in the medium term, the Government will secure financing to significantly upgrade health infrastructure, improve healthcare professionals working conditions and fund primary care access for vulnerable populations.",""]],"14":[[1,"27","3","COVID-19 WASH Emergency Response","WASH emergency response to covid-19 through fast-tracking the implementation of National WASH Programme and provision of safe water supply, sanitation and hygiene services in public places;",""],[1,"34","3","Coordinated Water and Sanitation Investment Plan","Interventions will include designing a coordinated investment plan to secure required funding for water and sanitation management;",""],[1,"131","13","State Water Agencies Reform Programme","the Government developed a reform programme for State Water Agencies to improve capacity, revenue generation, efficient operations and management of these facilities",""],[1,"131","13","Urban Water Projects Budget Support Line","a new budget line was created to support urban water projects by up to 30 percent of government contribution",""],[1,"132","1","Partnership for Expanded Water Supply, Sanitation and Hygiene (PEWASH) Programme","the Partnership for Expanded Water Supply, Sanitation and Hygiene (PEWASH) programme was set up to attain universal access to safe drinking water and adequate sanitation in rural areas.",""],[1,"132","2","PEWASH Shared Ownership WASH Investment Approach","This new approach was meant to encourage all stakeholders, including states and local governments, communities, development partners and the private sector to invest more in the provision of WASH services, particularly in rural areas through shared ownership.",""],[1,"132","2","Organized Private Sector in WASH Programme","the government has actively engaged the private sector in ending open defecation and improving access to basic sanitation through the Organized Private Sector in WASH (OPS-WASH) programme.",""],[1,"132","3","National WASH Sector Emergency Response to COVID-19 Programme","the National WASH Sector Emergency Response to COVID-19 programme was launched in 2020 with the aim of combating the pandemic through the provision of WASH services.",""],[1,"132","15","Open Defecation Elimination Initiative","The signing of Executive Order 009 by Mr President to end open defecation in Nigeria by 2025 will provide opportunities for states and the private sector to invest in sanitation facilities and generate employment for the teeming Nigerian youth.",""],[1,"133","20","Partnership Expansion for Water Sanitation and Hygiene (PEWASH) Programme","Strengthen effective collaboration to meet current demands for water and sanitation services through the Partnership Expansion for Water Sanitation and Hygiene (PEWASH) programme.",""],[1,"134","1","Water and Sanitation Infrastructure Upgrade and Service Expansion","These measures will allow for infrastructure upgrades as well as the improvement and expansion of water service delivery.",""]],"15":[[1,"186","2","Integrated Industrial Infrastructure Development","The Plan entails major infrastructure projects through the provision of integrated industrial relevant infrastructures across the six geopolitical zones and the opening up of opportunities for the rural areas to ensure even development and increased competitiveness.",""],[1,"186","2","Public-Private Partnership Framework Development","Government is aware of the urgency to increase capital accumulation to spur productivity and develop a public- private partnership framework, devoid of institutional and legal constraints, to engender transparency and accountability.",""],[1,"186","9","Public-Private Partnership Expansion for Plan Financing and Implementation","The government is committed to expanding the use of public private partnership (PPP) for the financing and implementation of programmes in this National Plan.",""],[1,"186","10","Private Financer Remuneration Options for Public Infrastructure","To repay private financers for the capital invested in public infrastructure and services, the government will provide the private financer with remuneration options, which include:",""],[1,"186","12","Availability Payment Mechanism for Private Infrastructure Investment","Availability payments: a phased repayment from the government to the private investor, based on the availability of infrastructure and services that meet international quality standards and programme output goals.",""],[1,"186","13","Annuity Public-Private Partnership Financing Mechanism","Annuity PPPs: where annual payments are paid to the private sector to offset their financing of the project.",""],[1,"186","14","PPP Project Screening and Selection Framework","careful steps will be taken to ensure that the projects, which are shortlisted, justify the likely high transaction costs of PPP procurement.",""],[1,"187","2","Strengthening the PPP Legal, Regulatory and Institutional Framework","the existing legal, regulatory and institutional framework for PPP projects will be further strengthened by the Government.",""],[1,"187","2","Streamlining BPE and ICRC Functions","Government will streamline BPE and ICRC to remove overlap between the two agencies.",""],[1,"187","2","PPP Project Preparation Units in Relevant Agencies","agencies that have a good suite of PPP projects are to set up units that can concentrate on project preparation and act as interface with ICRC and BPP as relevant.",""],[1,"187","5","Strategic Public Sector Reform and Incentives for Capital Mobilization","The government believes that through a combination of strategically selected public sector reforms, combined with transparent implementation, incentives, in line with international best practice, Nigeria stands a chance of attracting significant international and local resources to make a significant difference to the current deficit in capital spending that can substantially ease the fiscal crisis of the state.",""],[1,"187","13","Voluntary Offshore Assets Regularisation Scheme Infrastructure Financing","Funds from the Executive Order No. 8 on Voluntary Offshore Assets Regularisation Scheme, meant for infrastructure development.",""],[1,"187","14","National Development Fund","The size of the Fund is proposed to be between US$5bn and US$10bn, depending on the outcome of initial informal consultations with prospective investors.",""],[1,"187","15","Fund General Partner Appointment and Investment Management","Through a competitive process, an experienced and reputable General Partner will be appointed to lead the fund.",""],[1,"187","16","Direct Project Financing through Special Purpose Vehicles","Direct project financing through Special Purpose Vehicles (SPVs).",""],[1,"188","2","Interim Fund Management Appointment","Appoint an interim manager (until the contributors to the Fund are in place, at which point they would appoint their substantial manager).",""],[1,"188","4","Investment Incentives and Risk-Sharing Support Package","In addition to other incentives currently available, provide, where appropriate, incentives such as feasibility studies, assets (for instance. land), viability gap funding, guaranteed take-up (for example solar or wind power projects), minimum traffic volumes guarantee; partial risk guarantees; first loss arrangements; tax reliefs; back-up liquidity facilities, and credit enhancement.",""],[1,"188","5","Critical Enabling Environment Reform Package","Commit towards executing critical reforms to improve the enabling environment (including fiscal, exchange rate policies, etc.).",""],[1,"188","7","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Company","The President has approved the establishment of a Public Private Partnership-styled Infrastructure Company.",""],[1,"188","8","Road Infrastructure Development Financing Initiative","As an initiative of the government to finance critical infrastructure, the President signed Executive Order 07 of 2019 called Road Infrastructure Development",""],[1,"188","9","Refurbishment Investment Tax Credit Scheme","Refurbishment Investment Tax Credit Scheme.",""],[1,"188","10","Road Infrastructure Tax Credit Scheme","Through the Scheme, the Government aims to incentivise private sector investment in Nigerian roads across key economic corridors and industrial clusters.",""],[1,"188","12","Contingent Liability Management Framework Update and Disclosure","CLMF will be regularly updated and made available to financiers, to enable dimensioning the debt profile and risks associated with issued contingent liabilities, which will assist decision-making process in availing capital to projects supported by contingent liabilities instruments issued by government.",""],[1,"188","15","Project Preparation Facility Seed Funding","Government will catalyse a PPF with adequate seed funding that will crowd in other follow-on investors that are willing to subscribe to the PPF.",""],[1,"188","15","Project Co-development and Preparation Facility","The PPF will be used to co-develop and further prepare candidate projects that have been identified and selected for private capital and/or PPPs.",""],[1,"189","2","Viability Gap Fund Scheme","During this plan government will operationalize a VGF Scheme in accordance with its policy.",""],[1,"189","3","Minimum Revenue Guarantee Revolving Fund","Minimum Revenue Guarantee Revolving Fund (\"MRGRF\") - During the plan, government will adopt the MRGRF to ensure that fiscal shocks from crystallised guarantees are reduced to the barest minimum.",""],[1,"189","4","Collaboration with Multilateral Development Finance Institutions for Credit Risk Mitigation","The Government will continue to collaborate with Multilateral Development Finance Institutions as part of credit risk mitigating strategies.",""],[1,"189","5","Strengthening of the Infrastructure Concession and Regulatory Commission","The Infrastructure Concession and Regulatory Commission (ICRC), established with the ICRC Act 2005, as an institution of government will be properly enhanced during the planning period to better achieve its mandate of accelerating massive investment in national infrastructure by galvanizing foreign and domestic capital (private sector funding).",""],[1,"189","5","Public-Private Partnership Development and Implementation Support","This is with a view to supporting the Government and its MDAs to establish and implement effective public-private partnerships (PPPs) conditioned on assessing and considering the several PPPs models in a transparent manner.",""],[1,"189","5","Legal Amendment for More Effective ICRC Mandate Delivery","Meanwhile necessary legal amendment will be made to ensure the institution carries out its mandates more effectively;",""],[1,"189","6","Aid Effectiveness and Partnership Coordination Framework","Therefore, the Government will be at the centre of collaboration and coordination for all tiers of government to work closely with development partners to institutionalize and operationalize aid effectiveness and partnership principles within statutory regulatory framework for delivery and transparency.",""],[1,"189","9","Public-Private Partnership Framework for Infrastructure Investment","This entails galvanizing foreign and domestic capital through a PPPs framework to complement government efforts as the government cannot solely provide the financing.",""],[1,"189","10","Timely Release of Public Resources for Capital Projects and Annual Budget","The Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget and Planning in close collaboration with the Office of the Accountant General will ensure timely release of public resources for capital projects and the annual budget within the respective Medium-Term Expenditure Framework.","Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget and Planning | Office of the Accountant General"],[1,"189","10","Improved Debt Management Strategy","the Debt Management Office will be guided by improved debt management strategies within a globally acceptable Fiscal Sustainability Framework.",""]],"16":[[1,"178","1","National Development Planning Feedback Mechanism","Robust feedback mechanism to inform improvements in the national development planning process based on state-level implementation.",""],[1,"178","2","Strengthening of Planning and M&E Institutions","The States and Federal Government, will collaborate to strengthen the Department of Planning, Research and Statistics (DPRS) in ministries, establish a plan implementation unit in the ministry responsible for budget and planning; ensure proficiency of the Planning and M&E cadre in the respective MDAs.",""],[1,"178","3","National Development Plan Secretariat and Coordination Mechanism","The National Planning Arm under the FMBNP will serve as the Plan's Secretariat since it has the mandate and internal capacity to coordinate the Plan implementation efforts.",""],[1,"178","4","Strengthening DPRS Department Capacity and Institutionalization","Improve the professional capacity and institutionalization of DPRS departments.",""],[1,"178","6","Budget, Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity Strengthening","Empower and improve capacity in the Budget, Monitoring and Evaluation (BME) department.",""],[1,"178","7","Coordination and Monitoring and Evaluation Harmonisation","Harmonise coordination and M&E functions across MDAs.",""],[1,"178","17","National Monitoring and Evaluation Coordination","The Ministry also has National Monitoring and Evaluation and is better suited to coordinate execution, while integrating implementing agencies, data, monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"179","17","Programme Monitoring and Performance Tracking","Track activities and performance of outlined programmes",""],[1,"179","17","Nigeria Development Report Preparation","Prepare Nigeria Development Report (NDR) providing an account of the progress on targets and goals",""],[1,"179","17","Quarterly MTNDP Reporting to Steering Committee","Submit MTNDP quarterly reports to the Steering Committee",""],[1,"179","22","Planning Consultation and Plan Performance Monitoring","Engage in consultations with the Federal and Subnational Planning to provide feedback on relevant strategies · Monitor performance of the plan",""],[1,"180","10","Performance Monitoring and Continuous Data Collection Mechanism","A performance monitoring and continuous data collection mechanism will inform the annual plan performance review process and provide decision-makers with the necessary visibility on plan objectives progress.",""],[1,"180","11","Quarterly Reporting and Performance Review Mechanism","Quarterly reports to be drafted by the Planning Arm and submitted to the Steering Committees for review.",""],[1,"180","12","MDA Performance Incentive and Accountability Mechanism","Holding stakeholders accountable for this Plan's results is important for achieving the Plan's objectives.",""],[1,"181","5","Nigeria Development Report Performance Assessment Instrument","The Nigeria Development Report (NDR) will be the primary instrument for assessing the performance of the Plan.",""],[1,"181","5","Mid-Term Plan Review","The Plan will also undergo a mid-term review to incorporate necessary adjustments and updates.",""],[1,"189","8","Performance-Tied Capital Release Mechanism","the government will ensure value for money; as quarterly Capital releases to Ministries, Departments and Agencies, would be tied to the outcome of the reports of the periodic monitoring and evaluation exercise carried out by the National Monitoring and Evaluation Department of the Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget and National Planning.","Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget and National Planning"],[1,"189","8","Strengthening of the National Monitoring and Evaluation System","The National M&E will be strengthened to enhance its role.",""],[1,"190","1","National Monitoring and Evaluation System","The Plan includes a comprehensive National Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) system to facilitate the tracking of Plan implementation and effectiveness, and identification of bottlenecks for early resolution.",""],[1,"190","1","Results-Based Planning and Performance Monitoring","The focus of the M&E for this Plan is to institutionalize Results-Based Planning and Performance Monitoring, Reporting and use of evidence for responsive decision-making.",""],[1,"190","10","Strengthening the National M&E Department","the National M&E Department must have the authority and high visibility within the government to carry out its mandate.",""],[1,"190","11","Strengthened Monitoring and Evaluation System","A strengthened Monitoring and Evaluation System for effective implementation of the Plan (and its intended enhancements to the Quality of Life and Prosperity of Nigerians) by 2025.",""],[1,"190","13","National Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","The Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget, and National Planning (FMFBNP) will oversee the monitoring and evaluation of the Plan.","Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget, and National Planning (FMFBNP)"],[1,"191","12","State-Level Adaptation of the M&E Policy","The Functional roles of the organs are described above and are expected to be adapted at the state level for the implementation of the M&E Policy",""],[1,"191","16","Lesson-Learning Focused Monitoring and Evaluation Strategy","Promote a lesson-learning focused monitoring and evaluation strategy to inform the decision-making process across government levels",""],[1,"191","17","Strengthening the National Monitoring and Evaluation System","Promote joint working and learning on M&E among MDAs including strengthening the national M&E system",""],[1,"191","18","M&E Recommendation Follow-up and Decision-Making Integration","Follow-up on the implementation of findings and recommendations from M&E reports ensuring that M&E recommendations are feeding into government decision-making processes",""],[1,"191","21","Strategic Partnership and M&E Capacity Strengthening","· Promote strategic partnership at all levels of governance and all sectors · Promote joint working and learning on M&E among MDAs and all stakeholders with key roles in strengthening the national M&E system · Provide technical support to MDAs in building their M&E capacity · Standardize M&E functions in the federal government",""],[1,"191","22","Costed Evaluation Work Plan","Develop a costed evaluation work plan",""],[1,"191","23","Cross-Department Monitoring and Evaluation Coordination","· Coordinate M&E functions across departments and related agencies ·",""],[1,"191","23","Performance Improvement Plan Based on Monitoring Findings","Prepare a performance improvement plan based on the findings and recommendations of the Monitoring Report",""],[1,"191","24","Quarterly and Biannual MDA Performance Reporting","Prepare quarterly and biannual reports on the performance of the respective MDAs and submitting such reports to the National M&E Department of FMFBNP",""],[1,"192","1","Institutional Arrangement for M&E Support","Establish an institutional arrangement that will support relevant MDAs Monitoring and Evaluation units in the tracking of implementation progress.",""],[1,"192","2","Progress Reporting and Performance Scorecard System","Publish progress reports on a quarterly, semi-annual and annual basis to communicate progress and highlight blockers.",""],[1,"192","3","MDA Monitoring and Evaluation Leadership Framework","Ensure MDA M&E departments lead the charge in monitoring progress towards implementing the Plan in their relevant sectors and source relevant data to operationalize the framework.",""],[1,"192","4","Participatory Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Foster participatory M&E by engaging various stakeholders such as CSOs and PWDs within the Plan's M&E process.",""],[1,"192","5","National Statistical System Strengthening","Strengthen the national statistical system by adequately funding the functions of the National Bureau of Statistics and National Population Commission and other data capturing agencies",""],[1,"192","6","MDA Results-Based Scorecard System","The MDA Results-Based scorecard will be generated by respective Ministries, Departments and Agencies.",""],[1,"192","6","Strengthening Resources for the M&E Unit","That is, there will be adequate and timely resources for the M&E unit to enable it to perform its functions effectively.",""],[1,"192","8","Strengthening the National M&E Department for Performance Management Coordination","Empower the national M&E department with critical resources and institutional authority to drive centralized coordination of the Performance Management System in Nigeria",""],[1,"192","12","National Institute of Data and Performance Management","Establish and strengthen the National Institute of Data and Performance Management to bridge the M&E knowledge gap and professionalize M&E systems in the country",""],[1,"192","14","Digitize Performance Management System Coordination in MDAs","Digitize Performance Management System Coordination in MDAs across the country",""]],"17":[[1,"182","1","Strengthening the National Statistical System","It is therefore imperative to any national development plan to ensure and pursue a robust, well-funded, and responsive national statistical system.",""],[1,"182","2","National Statistical System Strengthening and Repositioning","the government will reposition and strengthen NBS and indeed the entire National Statistical System in Nigeria for sustained statistical production to guide the process of policy formulation, planning and monitoring as well as informed decision-making.",""],[1,"182","4","National Statistical Development Strategy","The Nigeria NSDS is aimed at transforming the entire statistical system in Nigeria, bringing together all agencies involved in data production across the three tiers of government.",""],[1,"182","13","State Strategy for the Development of Statistics","the State Strategy for the Development of Statistics is to drive the process of production of statistics at the sub-national level.",""],[1,"182","13","Sector Statistics Strategy","the Sector Statistics Strategy is to drive the process of producing statistics in Ministries, Departments and Agencies (MDAs) of government at both the national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"183","11","Digitization and Archiving of Data Backlogs","Digitization and archiving of backlogs, unprocessed, or unpublished data",""],[1,"183","36","National Strategy for the Development of Statistics Adoption","By 2025, the National Strategy for the Development of Statistics (NSDS) will be fully adopted, serving as the framework for statistical output across all levels of government.",""],[1,"183","36","National Statistical System Support and Advocacy","The National Statistical System through its coordinating agency the National Bureau of Statistics will receive prioritized support through resource allocation and statistical advocacy across all levels of government.",""],[1,"183","36","Statistical Production Modernization and Coordination","Statistical production will be duly regularized, modern techniques and tools will be utilized for statistics production, official statistics will be coordinated amongst agencies, and data will be open and easily accessible to all users.",""],[1,"183","36","State-Level GDP Production Support","Government will support the production of state-level GDP.",""],[1,"184","19","Revival of the Federal School of Statistics","Revival of Federal School of Statistics (FSS)",""],[1,"184","25","Implementation of the National Strategy for the Development of Statistics","Full implementation of the National Strategy for the Development of Statistics (NSDS):",""],[1,"184","26","NSDS Continuous Review and Monitoring Framework","The NSDS logical framework itself sets out the basis for continuous review - quarterly, annually, mid-term, and terminal - with NBS providing relevant datasets to the Ministry of Budget & National Planning which implements the Monitoring & Evaluation Master Plan.","Ministry of Budget & National Planning | NBS"],[1,"184","26","National Statistics Capacity Strengthening","When implemented fully, the NSDS will strengthen the country's capacity to produce quality statistics based on international best practices and standards to support policy efficacy and efficiency.",""],[1,"184","27","Strengthening the National Statistical System","The increased demand for evidence-based policy making and results-based evaluation requires the existence of a dynamic national statistical system.",""]],"18":[[1,"11","2","Privatisation of Self-Financing Public Enterprises","Other measures that will be implemented include a deliberate policy to address inflation of contracts and high cost of projects with consequences for defaulting officers, and privatisation of some public enterprises that can be self-financing.",""]],"19":[[1,"5","5","Public-Private Partnership for Plan Delivery","A strong partnership between the public and private sectors is, therefore, imperative for successful delivery of the Plan outcomes.",""],[1,"10","6","Plan Financing Strategy","the financing strategy of the Plan seeks to: i) identify various funding sources for the plan and map out strategies to ensure that the expected funds are realised; and ii) ensure that adequate finance is available for implementing the Plan.",""],[1,"10","7","Nigeria Investment and Growth Fund","Of particular significance is a new initiative, the Nigeria Investment and Growth Fund, which will invest in commercially viable projects in sectors that will (i) promote growth; (ii) enhance local value-addition through backward, forward linkages; (iii) create employment opportunities; promote technological innovation and learning; and (iv) promote exports and exports diversification.",""],[1,"10","7","Public-Private Partnership Financing Vehicles","In addition, financial vehicles such as growth funds, securitization and public-private partnerships (PPP), will be set up.",""],[1,"10","7","Tax Base Broadening and Private Sector Capacity Enhancement","Nigeria will generate revenue by broadening the tax base and enhancing the capacity of the private sector through creating investment opportunities and deliberate policy engagements and incentives.",""],[1,"11","5","Financing Strategy for Plan Implementation","The implementation framework will be supported by a financing strategy, a strengthened national economic management, citizen engagement and legislative changes.",""],[1,"41","5","Domestic and Foreign Resource Mobilisation for Job Creation","This job creation target will require the mobilisation of domestic and foreign resources through various channels including Direct Foreign Investment, Development Aid, Remittance flows and other sources, all facilitated by government policy actions.",""],[1,"44","9","Nigeria Investment and Growth Fund Launch","It will also provide the seed capital required for the launch of the Nigeria Investment and Growth Fund in line with the strategies underlying the national poverty reduction and growth strategy.",""],[1,"46","3","Foreign Investment Mobilization for Infrastructure Financing","Foreign inflows are a key financing source for the initiatives under this plan and expansion of the private sector more broadly.",""],[1,"46","3","Stable Exchange Rate and Policy Support Framework","A stable exchange rate regime and policy environment to support the attainment of these objectives will be adopted.",""]],"20":[[1,"5","3","Macroeconomic Stability and Business Environment Reform","ensure macroeconomic stability, enhance business and investment environment, and improve the living conditions of Nigerians.",""],[1,"8","1","Macroeconomic Stability and Investment Environment Reform","Hence, the Plan seeks to invest massively in infrastructure, ensure macroeconomic stability, enhance the investment environment, improve on social indicators and living conditions, implement climate change mitigation, adaptation and resilience strategies, amongst others.",""],[1,"8","6","Economic Sustainability Plan","Anchored on the government's Economic Sustainability Plan (ESP) during this period were policies comprising palliative measures, increased petroleum product prices and electricity tariffs, and fiscal and monetary policy support to various sectors.",""],[1,"11","5","Coordinated National Economic Management Framework","National economic management will be strengthened through the coordination of monetary, fiscal, trade, technology and industrial policies in a manner that recognizes and resolves any trade-offs or indeed, tensions, across these policies to maintain macroeconomic stability and the optimal growth trajectory.",""],[1,"24","9","Economic Recovery and Growth Plan","In response, the Federal Government introduced the Economic Recovery and Growth Plan (ERGP).",""],[1,"26","5","Economic Sustainability Plan","the country developed a robust and well-articulated N2.3 trillion Economic Sustainability Plan (ESP) containing policies, projects and measures aimed at stimulating/ revitalising virtually every sector ranging from agriculture and food security, job creation/ retention to internal security",""],[1,"26","6","Fiscal and Monetary Stimulus Measures","Implementing fiscal and monetary measures aimed at stimulating the economy and achieving quick recovery;",""],[1,"27","9","Exchange Rate Unification Measures","Some movements towards unification of the exchange rates to maximise the naira returns to Federation Account Allocation Committee from foreign exchange inflows;",""],[1,"36","2","Fiscal and Monetary Policy Stabilization Measures","The fiscal and monetary policy measures put forward by the ESP are presently being implemented to ensure a swift return to macroeconomic stability, forestall job losses in the economy by delivering fiscal stimulus to support private businesses and provide necessary emergency assistance to vulnerable population segments.",""],[1,"37","5","Fiscal Management and Policy Coordination Measures","The plan envisages additional fiscal measures which include improving on current debt management strategies, ensuring value for money in capital budget implementation, encouraging greater private sector participation to ensure more efficient outcomes and ensuring synergy between the fiscal and monetary authorities for proper policy coordination.",""],[1,"40","21","Fiscal and Monetary Stimulus Packages","a multiplicity of fiscal and monetary stimulus packages will be introduced to further accelerate economic growth to 2.9 percent in 2021 and continue on the same path to 6.3 percent in 2025.",""],[1,"44","10","Flexible Monetary Policy and Financial Sector Oversight","The monetary authorities will adopt a flexible and responsive monetary policy stance to stabilise prices, including foreign exchange rates, and oversee the monetary system and financial sector.",""],[1,"44","10","Exchange Rate Unification and Forex Market Reform","Unification of exchange rates and the elimination of arbitrage opportunities in the foreign exchange market due to the premium between the official and other exchange rates will also be a key priority,",""],[1,"44","10","Financial Sector Regulatory Oversight for Credit Expansion","The CBN will continue to provide regulatory oversight to the financial sector to attain an optimal level of credit in the economy to spur real sector growth (Table 3.4).",""]],"21":[[1,"34","10","Tax Administration and Revenue Diversification Reform","Adoption of measures to diversify revenue and increase tax to GDP ratio by improving tax administration, integrating the informal sector, and widening the tax base.",""],[1,"37","4","Domestic Resource Mobilization and Non-Oil Revenue Enhancement","a concerted effort will be geared towards domestic resource mobilization; especially in enhancing non-oil revenues to significantly decouple the economy from the impact of volatile oil prices.",""],[1,"37","4","Strategic Revenue Growth Initiatives","Current government efforts to improve revenue through the 'Strategic Revenue Growth Initiatives (SRGIs)' will drive the restructuring of the financial sources.",""],[1,"37","5","Annual Finance Bill Tax Law Reform","Under the new annual Finance Bills, existing tax laws will be amended and new tax laws will be introduced to reflect the emergence of new economic sectors.",""],[1,"42","4","Non-Oil Revenue Enhancement Strategy","At the centre of this plan is an emphasis on enhancing non-oil revenues to increase public infrastructure, scaling up social interventions, and reducing the fiscal deficit and debt service obligations (Table 3.3):",""],[1,"42","5","Domestic Non-Oil Revenue Mobilization","This evolution brings to the fore the criticality of enhancing domestic non-oil revenue mobilization.",""],[1,"42","6","Tax Law Reform and Revenue Mobilization Measures","Existing tax laws have been strengthened while new taxes are introduced in the Finance Bills accompanying the annual federal budgets since the 2019 budget cycle.",""],[1,"42","6","Tax Expenditure Monitoring and Rationalization","Fiscal incentives and exemptions to support key sectors of the economy are also being monitored and scaled back when necessary to ensure value for money in exchange for tax expenditures.",""],[1,"42","7","Strategic Revenue Growth Initiative","Efforts to improve revenues through the 'Strategic Revenue Growth Initiative (SRGIs) will be intensified as the focus shifts from improving revenue collection to ensuring tax compliance.",""],[1,"43","1","Tax Law Reform and Revenue Administration Improvement","tax laws.",""],[1,"43","2","Review and Amendment of Fiscal and Revenue Remittance Laws","The Fiscal Responsibility Act, 2007, Finance Acts and other enabling laws will be reviewed and amended accordingly in line with the current government's stance on remittances of revenue by MDAs and also to facilitate other relevant aspects of the SRGIs.",""],[1,"11","2","Fiscal Discipline and Institutional Compliance Reform","Additionally, there will be focus on fiscal discipline through institutional compliance with the fiscal responsibility act, deliberate policy, and drastic reduction of inefficiencies in governance.",""],[1,"11","2","Contract Inflation and Project Cost Control Policy","Other measures that will be implemented include a deliberate policy to address inflation of contracts and high cost of projects with consequences for defaulting officers, and privatisation of some public enterprises that can be self-financing.",""],[1,"43","3","Reduce Non-Critical Administrative Spending","and a significant reduction of non-critical administrative spending",""],[1,"44","9","Domestic Resource Mobilization and Fiscal Buffer Strengthening","The fiscal position for the general government is projected to improve from a deficit of 4.1 percent of GDP in 2021 to a surplus of 1.4 percent in 2025, reflecting mainly increased domestic resource mobilization.",""],[1,"44","9","Oil Price-Based Fiscal Rule Adherence","Adherence to the oil price based fiscal rule of a benchmark oil price lower than the futures price of oil (ranging between US$52.4-59.7 during the period 2021-2025) would cumulatively yield additional revenues of about N3.9 trillion.",""]],"22":[[1,"43","4","Expansion of Integrated Public Financial Management Systems","The government will continue to extend the roll-out of IPPIS, GIFMIS, the TSA and other technology-enabled solutions to ensure real-time management and tracking of government spending.",""],[1,"54","8","Rural Development Budget Tracking Mechanism","Going forward, a tracking mechanism to determine the allocations to rural development through federal, state and local government budgets will be developed by activating existing codes in the Chart of Accounts.",""]],"23":[[1,"5","3","Critical Infrastructure Investment Programme","We will continue to invest in critical infrastructure such as Power and alternative energy, Rail, Roads, and Housing",""],[1,"8","1","Infrastructure Investment and Climate Resilience Strategy","Hence, the Plan seeks to invest massively in infrastructure, ensure macroeconomic stability, enhance the investment environment, improve on social indicators and living conditions, implement climate change mitigation, adaptation and resilience strategies, amongst others.",""],[1,"9","10","Critical Infrastructure Investment Programme","to invest in critical physical, financial, digital, and innovation infrastructure",""],[1,"10","3","Major Infrastructure and Development Projects","To accomplish the objectives, the Plan provides for the implementation of major infrastructure and other development projects across the six geopolitical zones and the opening up of opportunities for the rural areas to ensure balanced development and increased competitiveness.",""],[1,"32","5","Critical Physical, Financial, Digital and Innovation Infrastructure Investment","Invest in critical physical, financial, digital and innovation infrastructure",""],[1,"32","15","Critical Infrastructure Investment Programme","Invest in critical physical, financial, digital, science, technology, and innovation infrastructure:",""],[1,"33","8","Transport Infrastructure Innovative Financing Mechanisms","This will include exploring innovative financing mechanisms for continued development of transport infrastructure;",""],[1,"34","7","Critical and Strategic Infrastructure Investment Programme","Prioritization and implementation of critical and strategic infrastructure projects that will directly raise production and productivity in the MSMEs, agriculture, manufacturing and service sectors, in line with rapid growth, revenue and foreign exchange diversification objectives.",""],[1,"36","2","Critical Infrastructure Financing for Growth and Jobs","Resources are also targeted at funding critical infrastructure to support economic growth and stimulate the creation of jobs in productive economic sectors.",""],[1,"39","9","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Financing","New infrastructure projects will either be privately funded or financed through PPP arrangements.",""],[1,"39","10","Nigeria Infrastructural Company (Infraco) Establishment","Government will drive this realignment through initiatives such as the establishment of the Nigeria Infrastructural Company (Infraco) with an initial seed capital of one trillion naira",""],[1,"39","10","Road Infrastructure Development and Refurbishment Investment Tax Credit Scheme","the continued rollout of the Road Infrastructure Development and Refurbishment Investment Tax Credit Scheme (RIDRITCS) by which private capital finances the construction of roads along key economic corridors and industrial clusters across the country",""],[1,"61","2","Strategic Investment in Critical Sectors and Infrastructure","the oil and gas sector should create substantial financial resources that can be channelled into the concentric diversification of the Nigerian economy through strategic investments in critical sectors and building key infrastructure components to ensure a stable and competitive business environment.",""],[1,"68","5","Critical Infrastructure and Enabling Environment Support for Priority Sectors","the government shall unlock the potentials of these sectors within the plan primarily in critical infrastructure, the right laws and an enabling environment.",""],[1,"68","5","Private Sector Partnership for Connected Markets and Local Manufacturing","Government shall also partner with the private sector to spur connected markets, push local manufacturing and secure retail and distribution channels for products of these sectors.",""],[1,"68","5","Targeted Business Support and Policy Alignment Measures","This is envisaged through targeted interventions, policy alignment and with clear policy focus to build these industries and increase the technical as well as financial support for businesses in the sector.",""]],"24":[[1,"21","12","Road Infrastructure Development and Refurbishment Investment Tax Credit Scheme","Road Infrastructure Development and Refurbishment Investment Tax Credit Scheme",""],[1,"27","2","Road Construction and Rehabilitation Job Creation Programme","Creation of 296,000 jobs through construction and rehabilitation of roads in the six geopolitical zones;",""],[1,"53","15","Rural Transportation Infrastructure Expansion","Increase rural transportation infrastructure",""]],"25":[[1,"26","13","Solar Power for Households Strategy","Energy for all through solar power strategy - solar power for 5 million households by 2023 and 250,000 jobs in the energy sector;",""],[1,"33","8","Energy Capacity Optimization Measures","resolving value-chain specific constraints to unlock added energy for Nigerians by optimizing existing capacity;",""],[1,"57","16","Energy and Transportation Infrastructure Expansion","the government plans to expand Nigeria's infrastructure stock, beginning with energy and transportation infrastructure.",""]],"26":[[1,"33","8","Digital Economy Investment Support","The digital economy ecosystem will be strengthened by increasing financial and technical support through local and foreign investment.",""],[1,"58","4","Digital Innovation Support for Industrialisation","Leverage technology and other digital innovations to aid Nigeria's industrialisation process and competitiveness.",""],[1,"55","7","Industrial Database Development and Digitization","The government has developed, populated and digitised an industrial database.",""]],"27":[[1,"26","12","Mass Housing Strategy","Mass housing strategy to create jobs through homes - 1.8 million jobs and construction of 300,000 homes across the country;",""],[1,"33","8","Affordable Housing Delivery Innovation","introducing and adopting low-cost production technologies and innovative affordable housing delivery methods.",""],[1,"32","8","Social Infrastructure and Services Investment","Invest in the social infrastructure and services required to alleviate poverty and drive inclusive economic empowerment",""],[1,"33","4","Social Infrastructure and Services Investment","Invest in the social infrastructure and services required to alleviate poverty, drive inclusive economic empowerment, and reduce unemployment:",""],[1,"54","5","Private Sector Support for Rural Social Infrastructure","Across rural communities, the federal, states and local governments will facilitate private sector innovations in building quality and affordable health centres, schools and skills development centres to improve",""]],"28":[[1,"27","1","MSME Support Grants and Interest-Free Loan Scheme","Support for small businesses (MSMEs) including conditional grants and interest-free loans;",""],[1,"27","11","Targeted Credit Facility for Affected MSMEs","Creation of N50.00 billion targeted credit facility for affected MSMEs;",""],[1,"44","10","Targeted Credit Interventions for Key Sectors","Ongoing regulatory forbearance to banks, moratorium and interest rate reductions on credit facilities and targeted interventions for key sectors will be maintained as required.",""],[1,"58","5","Manufacturing Sector Credit Guarantee Scheme Expansion","Work with key partners, especially development finance institutions, to develop and expand the credit guarantee schemes available to players in the manufacturing sector, particularly the MSMEs.",""]],"29":[[1,"26","7","Local Materials Job Creation Initiative","Preserving and creating jobs using locally sourced materials;",""],[1,"27","8","Local Manufacturing and Production Loan Support","N1.0 trillion naira in loans to boost local manufacturing and production across critical sectors;",""],[1,"33","7","Value Chain Linkage and Local Sourcing Promotion","strengthening value chain linkages by promoting local sourcing and value addition",""],[1,"33","7","Manufacturing Expansion Financing Initiative","launching financial interventions to finance manufacturing expansion",""],[1,"33","7","Mineral Sector Value Addition and Linkage Initiative","creating linkages across the mineral sector and beyond for value addition to enhance local production and job creation",""],[1,"33","7","Technology-Enabled Business Environment Efficiency Initiative","Business environment initiatives such as leveraging technology to improve efficiencies and overall competitiveness will be initiated to support these interventions.",""],[1,"34","8","Supportive Market-Driven Interventions for Productive Sectors","Continued supportive market-driven interventions for manufacturing, agriculture and MSME subsectors to encourage broader concentric diversification efforts.",""],[1,"36","2","Private Sector Investment and Industrial Diversification Promotion","This Plan, which succeeds the ERGP and ESP, builds on this foundation by promoting private sector investment in the economy, incentivizing the emergence of new and innovative sectors in the service industry, as well as promoting industrialization as a key driver of economic growth.",""],[1,"36","9","Critical Infrastructure Support for Private Sector Development","Government will continue to facilitate the growth process with the provision of critical infrastructure germane to private sector development, with a focus on innovative technology-driven economic sectors.",""],[1,"39","6","Backward Integration and Beneficiation Strategy","Although a backward integration strategy will be pursued to encourage the beneficiation of primary resources, there will still be a need for capital goods imports in the medium term, while the domestic capacity to produce capital goods is being developed.",""],[1,"39","7","Strategic Fiscal Policy Support for Private Sector-Led Growth","On the demand side, this plan is structured to provide support for private sector-led growth through complementary and strategic fiscal policy interventions.",""],[1,"40","20","Coordinated Fiscal and Monetary Support for Domestic Production Expansion","this plan forecasts an industrial sector-led expansionary path with significant support from coordinated fiscal and monetary policies to ensure a steady expansion in domestic production.",""],[1,"41","2","Non-Oil Sector Growth Strategy","This plan will place greater emphasis on non-oil sector growth to insulate the economy from exogenous commodity shocks and ensure exchange rate and fiscal stability.",""],[1,"41","2","Local Sourcing of Essential Inputs Initiative","The outbreak of COVID-19 alongside its disruption of global supply chains has shown the need for countries to explore local sourcing of essential primary and intermediate inputs.",""],[1,"41","2","Domestic Value Chain Development and GVC Linkage Strategy","An outcome of this strategy is the need for the development of DVCs with the prospect of linking up to GVCs in a strategic manner.",""],[1,"41","3","Inter-Sectoral Linkages for Industrial Base Expansion","Exploring backward and forward inter-sectoral linkages amongst the agricultural, services and manufacturing sectors would expand the country's industrial base by enabling the development of technological and export capabilities as well as local production systems and networks.",""],[1,"41","6","Job Creation and Business Growth Support Package","A multi-faceted approach will be adopted to support job creation including tools already in use such as cash transfers to vulnerable groups, incentives to support business growth and expansion, addressing structural factors undergirding high-interest rates and lack of access to finance, identification and expansion of existing industrial clusters in the country and attainment of macroeconomic stability.",""],[1,"42","1","One-Product Initiative for Youths and Women","to job creation efforts through the One-Product Initiative Targeting Youths and Women.",""],[1,"42","2","Labour-Intensive Industry Revitalization","Development and revitalization of labour-intensive industries will be encouraged under the Plan and government regulation will be recalibrated to promote competition, support the emergence of new economic sectors, and protect the underserved segments of the population.",""]],"30":[[1,"34","9","Non-Oil Foreign Exchange Earnings Enhancement","Enhancement of non-oil foreign exchange earnings by attracting FDI, improving diaspora remittances, raising productivity and promoting non-oil exports.",""],[1,"39","6","AfCFTA Export Competitiveness Support","The plan recognizes the need to place Nigeria in an advantageous position as the AfCFTA is rolled out and Nigerian exporters face and overcome challenges in export markets with the goal of making the country's exports more competitive.",""],[1,"39","6","Business Cost Reduction and Export Stimulation Measures","The efforts to reduce the cost of doing business, increased public and private sector investments combined with expenditure switching policies are expected to stimulate exports and rebalance imports to support increased manufacturing activities.",""],[1,"46","1","Export Diversification and Trade Balance Improvement Strategy","A key objective is to diversify the composition of exports to include manufactured goods and high value-added services as the digital economy expands.",""],[1,"46","2","Non-Oil Export Expansion and AfCFTA Market Diversification","Nigeria intensifies efforts to grow its non-oil sector exports, and Nigeria will also be taking advantage of the opportunities offered by the African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA) to explore new markets for its goods and service exports.",""],[1,"42","3","Export Diversification and Structural Reform Agenda","Further diversification of exports and foreign exchange earnings will be pursued alongside social development to ensure inclusive growth and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"49","8","Agricultural Value Chain Market Expansion under AfCFTA","The AfCFTA will provide agricultural value chain actors with a more accessible export market that ensures wealth generation and job creation.",""],[1,"51","10","Export Market Linkage Support for Priority Agricultural Products","Government will strengthen NEPC's ability to facilitate market linkages to private sector exporters via targeted research, leveraging embassies and trade missions.",""],[1,"51","12","Targeted Export Training and Capacity Building","NEPC and SON will partner with training institutions to provide targeted export training and capacity building through commodity associations focusing on standards.",""],[1,"51","13","Exporter Financing and Repatriation Incentive Scheme","In partnership with financial service providers, the Government will raise awareness about funding opportunities for exporters, develop tailored financing instruments and provide incentives for the repatriation of proceeds from export sales.",""],[1,"51","14","Embassy Trade Desks and Export Support Targets","All Nigerian Embassies/High Commissions will have a trading desk, and clear targets to support Nigerian exports.",""],[1,"51","14","Streamlined Exportation Process and Agricultural Export Logistics Window","NPA will also develop and implement a streamlined process for exportation in collaboration with all levels of government with clear and transparent steps including the creation of a special export logistics window for agricultural products.",""],[1,"55","5","Manufacturing Input Access and Export Promotion Measures","The government prioritised resolving several manufacturing-related issues, from access to raw materials to export promotion.",""],[1,"55","6","Export Expansion Grant Fund","there has been increased funding of the export expansion grant (EEG) fund to stimulate demand for locally manufactured goods and to ensure Nigeria's export-oriented businesses remain stimulated and competitive.",""],[1,"55","6","Export Market Expansion Programmes","Various government agencies are implementing export market expansion programmes in line with their mandates, and often with the support of development partners.",""],[1,"55","6","Exporter Capacity-Building and Market Linkage Support","These initiatives have increased SME exporters' capacity to access specific export markets in the EU, the US, Asia, and Africa.",""],[1,"55","9","Non-Oil Export Promotion through Market Information and Order Generation Systems","Promotion of non-oil exports through integrated Market Information Systems (MIS) and Order Generation Systems (OGS).",""],[1,"58","8","AfCFTA Implementation to Attract Private Investment","Furthermore, the implementation of the AfCFTA should attract significant private sector investment.",""]],"31":[[1,"57","12","Value Chain Integration for Domestic Manufacturing Inputs","Improve value chain integration to promote domestic sourcing of manufacturing inputs",""],[1,"57","19","Value Chain Linkage Strengthening for Primary Sectors","Strengthen value chain linkages to primary sectors: Strengthen linkages between the agro-allied and",""],[1,"58","1","Value Chain Development Programmes","This will be accomplished by implementing value chain development programmes and incentives to encourage local sourcing of raw materials in areas where Nigeria has a comparative advantage.",""],[1,"58","1","Local Raw Material Sourcing Incentives","This will be accomplished by implementing value chain development programmes and incentives to encourage local sourcing of raw materials in areas where Nigeria has a comparative advantage.",""],[1,"58","1","Inter-Ministerial Value Chain Productivity Coordination","There will be emphasis on fostering synergies among the Ministries of Industry, Trade and Investment and other relevant MDAs such as the Ministries of Agriculture and Rural Development and Ministries of Science and Technology, both at the federal and state levels, to implement initiatives that improve the productivity of value chains to provide critical input for manufacturing.","Ministries of Industry, Trade and Investment | Ministries of Agriculture and Rural Development | Ministries of Science and Technology"],[1,"58","2","Industrial Policy and Competitiveness Council","Through the Industrial Policy and Competitiveness Council, the government will provide the private sector with a channel to share feedback on its policies.",""],[1,"58","3","Development of Industrial Cities, Parks, and Clusters","Facilitate the development of industrial cities, industrial parks, and industrial clusters, while focusing on making hard infrastructure available within these industrial zones",""]],"32":[[1,"30","1","Labour Market Entry and Mobility Policies","Nigeria will drive economic expansion and pursue policies and programmes to make for easier entry into the labour market, as well as greater labour mobility.",""],[1,"26","14","Youth and Women Jobs through the Digital Economy","Jobs for youths and women post-covid-19 through digital economy, National public works programme, empowerment schemes for women, etc;",""],[1,"25","2","Social Inclusion, Job Creation, Youth Empowerment and Human Capital Programmes","Investing in the Nigerian people through programmes on social inclusion, job creation, youth empowerment and improved human capital;",""],[1,"41","4","Structural Reforms for Job Creation and Economic Diversification","the government's priority in this plan is to eliminate the binding constraints on sustainable job creation through the introduction of structural reforms to ensure concentric economic diversification, the emergence of a thriving and competitive private sector and the attainment of inclusive growth.",""]],"33":[[1,"30","2","Food Security Programme","Nigeria will also provide improved nutrition through its food security programme",""],[1,"40","23","Agricultural Sector Support and Investment Expansion","With improved security prospects, effective and efficient government support and additional opportunities for private sector investment in the plan period, the agricultural sector will expand by 1.2 percent in 2021 and increase steadily until it reaches 3.7 percent growth in 2025",""],[1,"48","4","Agricultural Input and Agro-Processing Support Programmes","Nigeria has implemented a wide range of industry support programmes in inputs and agro-processing.",""],[1,"48","4","Agricultural Value Chain Support in Cropping, Fisheries and Livestock","The country has intervened in specific value chains such as, cropping, fisheries and livestock, as well as support services in agriculture research and extension.",""],[1,"48","4","Presidential Fertilizer Initiative","Fertilizer production was revitalised, leveraging the Presidential Fertilizer Initiative for the domestic production of urea and importation of phosphate.",""],[1,"48","4","Improved Seeds, Seedlings and Stems Production Support","There was also a concerted effort to facilitate the production of improved seeds, seedlings and stems for several crops, including (but not limited to) potatoes, vitamin A-enriched cassava, sesame, soybean and yam.",""],[1,"54","3","Agricultural Productivity and Market Access Improvement","the government will focus on improving agricultural productivity, quality and timely access to markets.",""]],"34":[[1,"49","9","Agricultural Productivity Enhancement through Technology and Climate-Smart Practices","By 2025, Nigeria's agricultural productivity is expected to increase as technology, innovation and climate-smart practices are introduced to ensure the continuous availability of affordable and nutritious food.",""],[1,"50","26","Climate-Adapted Priority Crop Value Chain Productivity Programme","Production systems and technology to increase national output and productivity in priority crop value chains, including cassava, rice, maize, soybean, yam, and tomatoes, will be leveraged for climate adaptation in sustainable production practices.",""],[1,"50","27","Climate Shock Adaptation Support through Extension Services","Development partners and extension services will be consulted to access relevant information, technology, and training to address current and future climate shocks.",""],[1,"50","28","Strengthen Agricultural Insurance Coverage","Relevant institutions such as the Nigerian Agricultural Insurance Corporation (NAIC) will be strengthened to increase insurance coverage for floods and post- harvest losses suffered by farmers.",""]],"35":[[1,"50","29","Commodity Exchange and Warehousing Legal Reform","Existing legislation will be strengthened and necessary ones enacted for commodity exchange operations, warehousing, and trading of produce.",""],[1,"50","30","Silo Complex and National Reserve Mechanism Revamp","The management and capacity of silo complexes at Lafia, Minna, Gusau, Dutsinma, Yola, Akure, and Ilesha and the National Reserve mechanism will be revamped to ensure efficiency, effectiveness, and transparency.",""],[1,"50","31","Post-Harvest Loss Reduction Support","supported to reduce post-harvest losses via efficient storage, logistics, and development of market linkages.",""],[1,"50","32","Critical Rural Infrastructure Development for Post-Harvest Loss Reduction","As part of measures to reduce post-harvest losses, the government will also prioritise developing critical rural infrastructure such as roads, reactivation of grain aggregation centres, off-grid energy solutions and ICT",""],[1,"52","11","Rural Agricultural Infrastructure Improvement","Against this background, proper attention will be given to agricultural sector relevant infrastructure, including; good roads, off-grid power and storage capacity.",""],[1,"53","1","Local Agro-Processing Capacity Enhancement","Furthermore, improved local processing capacity will increase the quality of certain high-value crop products produced in rural areas (e.g., ginger, sesame seed etc.) and help generate incomes for rural dwellers and foreign exchange for the country on a sustainable basis.",""],[1,"51","1","Local Food Processing and Value Addition Initiative","Additionally, there will be an increased focus on local processing and value addition to ensure the year-round availability and affordability of nutritious food.",""],[1,"55","5","Value Chain Resilience and Market Linkage Programmes","Over the last three years, several projects aimed at enhancing value chain resilience through market linkage programmes, particularly in the agriculture sector, have been launched.",""],[1,"55","5","Sugarcane Out-grower Support and Farm Infrastructure Programme","Among these programmes is one that assists out-growers of sugarcane and provides farm infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"55","5","Low-Interest Loan Support for Sugarcane Farmers","Farmers on sugar plantations have benefited from the programme by obtaining low-interest loans to cultivate sugarcane and supply it to sugar mills.",""]],"36":[[1,"50","33","National Livestock Transformation Plan","The government will implement key policies including the National Livestock Transformation Plan (with key programmes on animal breeding and conservation, grazing reserves development, dairy value chain development and small ruminant development);",""],[1,"50","34","Anti-Smuggling and Fisheries Regulation Policy","The government will also eliminate the smuggling of fish and poultry by instituting policies for freshwater, deep sea, coastal fishing to curb illegal fishing and develop the blue economy generally.",""],[1,"50","34","Animal Health and Slaughterhouse Upgrading Programme","This will also include addressing related issues including; pests and diseases, upgrading abattoirs and slaughterhouses and establishing veterinary services.",""]],"37":[[1,"51","5","Agriculture Financing Scheme Realignment","Existing agriculture financing schemes and initiatives to support value chain actors in maintaining and scaling up their operations will be realigned, while ensuring inclusion for women and youth-owned agro-businesses.",""],[1,"51","7","Women and Youth Inclusion in Agriculture Initiative","Government will leverage the National Agricultural Gender Policy by the Federal Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development, the National Gender Plan of the Federal Ministry of Women Affairs and existing youth initiatives by FMYSD, FMARD, FMLP as well as other similar agencies at the subnational levels to ensure the inclusion of women and youth in the agriculture sector.","Federal Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development | Federal Ministry of Women Affairs | FMYSD | FMARD | FMLP"],[1,"34","3","Women’s Economic Empowerment Financing Access Support","supporting the economic empowerment of women by facilitating access to financing;",""]],"38":[[1,"51","2","Private Sector R&D Support Prioritization","Existing institutions with a mandate to strengthen local businesses, such as SMEDAN, NIPC, NOTAP, NAFDAC, SON, RMRDC and their equivalents at the subnational level will be authorised to prioritise support for private sector R & D for key products.",""],[1,"51","3","Agricultural Research Commercialisation Framework","Agriculture research institutions will be strengthened with appropriate frameworks developed for the commercialisation of their research findings and produce.",""]],"39":[[1,"51","4","Port Inspection and Quality Management Lab Strengthening","Inspection capacity at ports and quality management labs in central food processing states will be strengthened.",""],[1,"51","11","Automated Exportation Process for Produce and Food Products","Government will fully automate the exportation process for produce and food products from Nigeria to ensure transparency and accountability at the ports with a special window for agricultural products.",""]],"40":[[1,"53","6","Integrated Rural Development Programme","The government will adopt a holistic approach to ensure rural development by focusing on programmes and policies that harness the potential of the rural economy to create opportunities for its inhabitants.",""],[1,"53","6","Critical Rural Infrastructure Development","This will begin with developing critical rural infrastructure and progress with the development of sectoral linkages to create economic opportunities and improve livelihoods.",""],[1,"53","6","Rural Sectoral Linkages Development","This will begin with developing critical rural infrastructure and progress with the development of sectoral linkages to create economic opportunities and improve livelihoods.",""],[1,"53","20","Critical Rural Infrastructure Development","Prioritise the development of critical rural infrastructure such as roads, off-grid energy, and",""],[1,"54","2","Private Sector Rural Infrastructure Investment Facilitation","Facilitate private sector investment to accelerate the provision of infrastructure in rural areas.",""],[1,"54","4","Mapping of Rural Intersectoral Linkages for Investment","Intersectoral linkages within rural economies will be mapped out to identify precise opportunities to attract investments and enhance non-farm incomes towards improved employment generation and poverty reduction among rural dwellers",""],[1,"54","8","Private Sector Financing for Rural Development","Given the required investment in the sector, public spending will be enhanced by private sector financing; however, the government will still undertake significant investments in the sector in the short term due to the current incentive structure in the private sector.",""],[1,"54","9","Rural Market Linkage and Value Chain Development Measures","In the years leading up to 2025, the government will implement the necessary measures to link rural communities to urban, regional, and global markets and support value chain development in agribusiness and other sectors.",""]],"41":[[1,"54","4","Digital Market Access and Financial Services for Rural Farmers","Digital access to markets for farmers in rural areas and the provision of digital financial services through private sector providers will be prioritised to improve productivity and create access to credit facilities.",""],[1,"54","5","Rural Education and Healthcare Access Expansion","the government will also increase access to quality education and healthcare in rural areas.",""],[1,"54","5","Rural Skills Alignment Initiative","The education and skills systems will be linked with the comparative strengths of rural communities to ensure the alignment of skills and opportunities.",""],[1,"54","7","Rural Microenterprise Credit and Economic Opportunity Expansion","Increase access to credit and other economic opportunities available to micro enterprises in rural areas.",""]],"42":[[1,"27","4","Social Investment Programme Support for Vulnerable Households","Social Investment Programme - increased support to vulnerable individuals and households in the context of covid-19;",""],[1,"33","4","Expanded Poverty Alleviation and Social Protection Programmes","the government will invest in expanded poverty alleviation and social protection programmes, to ensure that the most vulnerable are not left behind.",""],[1,"34","3","Social Protection Financing Diversification Initiative","Underpinning social development measures will be job creation and poverty alleviation initiatives, such as diversifying revenue-generating streams to finance social protection initiatives and creating inter- sector linkages to unlock the potential of high growth sectors critical to achieving the job target.",""],[1,"34","16","Social Protection for the Most Vulnerable","Implementation of social protection for the most vulnerable, backed by an effective M&E framework and impact assessment methods.",""],[1,"37","2","Expanded Social Investment Programmes","Government will also continue to expand its current social investment programmes, which are designed for implementation by both the federal and subnational governments, to directly address the twin problems of unemployment and poverty in the country.",""],[1,"41","5","Social Investment Programme","The new jobs will be generated through a combination of several interventions, including the Social Investment Programme, but primarily as a result of accelerated economic recovery and increased private sector participation prompted by the implementation of the strategies and policies outlined in this plan.",""],[1,"41","6","Expanded Social Protection for Vulnerable Groups","Social protection for the young, elderly and all vulnerable segments of the population is also at the core of this strategy.",""],[1,"44","8","Prioritization of Social Intervention Programmes for the Poor","Social intervention programmes targeted at the poor and job-creating programs and projects will be prioritised.",""]],"43":[[1,"41","6","Gender- and Youth-Responsive Development Interventions","gender and youth-responsive approaches to development will be incorporated into the direct policy interventions of government and other partners to support the attainment of the relevant Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).",""],[1,"51","9","Gender-Sensitive Data Collection and Gender Statistics Promotion","(NBS) will be utilised to promote the use of gender- sensitive data collection and gender statistics for evidence-based planning, policy, and programme design, implementation, and evaluation.",""]],"44":[[1,"46","4","Remittance Inflow Incentive Measures","the monetary authorities will continue to offer incentives to encourage inflows.",""]],"45":[[1,"61","2","Petroleum Industry Act Implementation for Investment Unlocking","However, with the Petroleum Industry Act (PIA) now in place, there should be a shift in this narrative to unlocking investment opportunities in the sector.",""],[1,"61","3","Petroleum Industry Act Reform Implementation","The Act is an attempt to implement the much-needed reforms to improve the structure, governance and fiscal policy of the Nigerian oil and gas sector.",""],[1,"61","6","Oil and Gas Sector Reform and Value Chain Transformation","By 2025, Nigeria would have reformed its oil and gas sector to increase investor confidence and accelerate revenue generation through increased production, refining capacity and efficient downstream operations.",""],[1,"61","6","Downstream Operations Efficiency and Transparency Reform","Nigeria plans to achieve a series of transformation across the oil and gas value chain by increasing crude oil production, commercializing 80 percent of produced gas, improving refining capacity through privatisation and construction of new refineries, improving efficiency and transparency of downstream operations and ensuring all oil and gas operators have and implement a decommissioning and asset retirement (DAR) plan.",""],[1,"62","7","Petroleum Industry Act Implementation","Commitment to the full implementation of the Petroleum Industry Act will improve investors' confidence and overall sector efficiencies.",""],[1,"62","10","Priority Projects for Oil and Gas Sector Enabling Environment","This will be used to execute priority projects in the sector to create an enabling environment for a private sector-led oil and gas industry.",""],[1,"62","10","Petroleum Industry Act Implementation","Furthermore, the implementation of the provisions of the PIA will attract significant investments into the sector.",""],[1,"62","11","Oil and Gas Sector Investment Attraction and Value Maximization","In the years ahead, the Nigerian government will work towards maximizing the value of the sector to create the wealth needed to expand other aspects and components of the economy, create meaningful jobs for Nigerians and improve the overall business environment by creating the enabling environment to attract investment into the sector.",""],[1,"60","17","Oil and Gas Sector Global Competitiveness Initiative","During the plan period, the oil and gas sector in the country would be positioned for global competition, including exploring the capacity to assist other countries prospecting for oil;",""]],"46":[[1,"59","2","Oil Production and Local Refining Support Programmes","Policies were introduced to increase oil production and improve local refining through various programmes.",""],[1,"59","3","Modular Refinery Development Support Initiative","Additionally, structures were established to encourage the development of modular refineries to increase local refining capacity.",""],[1,"59","5","Modular Refinery Support and Funding Programme","The government supported and encouraged the development of these modular refineries by approving duty-free imports of associated equipment.",""],[1,"59","5","Licensing of Modular Refinery Operators","The government then licensed ten operators to establish modular refineries, including the Niger Delta Petroleum Resources (NDPR) 10,000 bp/d refinery in Rivers State, Walter Smith (Petroman) 5,000 bpd modular refinery in Imo State, and Opac 7,000 bpd facility in Delta State.",""],[1,"59","5","Modular Refinery Funding Committee and Credit Facility","Finally, a technical committee on Modular Refinery Funding (MRF) was established to develop an intervention funding programme for Modular Refineries investors to access a credit facility to resolve fund gaps faced by investors in the sector.",""],[1,"60","10","Oil Refinery Rehabilitation Programme","the planned rehabilitation of the oil refineries in the country.",""],[1,"60","14","Refinery Rehabilitation and Completion Programme","The rehabilitation of government refineries and the completion of other private refineries will contribute significantly to self-reliance in",""],[1,"61","6","Refinery Privatisation and New Refinery Construction","Nigeria plans to achieve a series of transformation across the oil and gas value chain by increasing crude oil production, commercializing 80 percent of produced gas, improving refining capacity through privatisation and construction of new refineries, improving efficiency and transparency of downstream operations and ensuring all oil and gas operators have and implement a decommissioning and asset retirement (DAR) plan.",""],[1,"62","2","Private Sector Refinery Investment Support Framework","Provide the framework to support private sector participation and initiative at building new refineries.",""],[1,"62","5","Downstream Petroleum Sector Deregulation","Deregulate the downstream sector to improve efficiencies and revenue.",""],[1,"62","5","Private Sector Transfer of Downstream Petroleum Assets and Retail Trading","Improve efficiencies in the downstream segment by transitioning complete control of critical assets such as petroleum pipelines and processes such as retail trading to the private sector.",""]],"47":[[1,"61","4","Gas Production and Crude Oil Output Enhancement","It further seeks to ensure that gas production targets are achieved to meet domestic and industrial market demands as well as improve crude oil production both at the onshore and deep-water segments.",""],[1,"61","6","Gas Commercialisation Programme","Nigeria plans to achieve a series of transformation across the oil and gas value chain by increasing crude oil production, commercializing 80 percent of produced gas, improving refining capacity through privatisation and construction of new refineries, improving efficiency and transparency of downstream operations and ensuring all oil and gas operators have and implement a decommissioning and asset retirement (DAR) plan.",""],[1,"61","7","Gas Processing Plant and Energy Park Development","the government will pay attention to gas feedstock availability, construction of Gas Processing Plants (GPPs) and development of industries that consume intermediate products produced by these GPPs.",""],[1,"61","7","Gas Aggregation Support to Energy Parks","That Nigeria's gas fields are widely dispersed and medium-sized require arrangements to support gas aggregation to energy parks as centres for industrial development.",""],[1,"62","1","Upstream Gas Commercialization and Gas Infrastructure Investment","Commercialize up to 80 percent of upstream gas for use in powering gas power plants as well as for export purposes, rather than increase environmental pollution through flaring.",""],[1,"62","1","Gas Production Sharing Contract Reform","This will involve investing in additional gas infrastructure and strengthening current gas production sharing contract terms to increase viability and investment appetite.",""],[1,"62","1","Methanol Fuel Production Technology Policy","The government will also promote the policy on methanol fuel production technology already approved by the Federal Executive Council.",""]],"48":[[1,"60","16","Pipeline Network Repair and Expansion","In the implementation of this Plan, the pipeline network will be repaired and extended to ensure efficient transportation of petroleum products.",""],[1,"62","3","Pipeline Rehabilitation and Expansion under PPP Concessions","Repair and extend the coverage of pipelines to serve as an efficient transportation pathway for petroleum products.",""]],"49":[[1,"61","6","Decommissioning and Asset Retirement Plan Requirement","Nigeria plans to achieve a series of transformation across the oil and gas value chain by increasing crude oil production, commercializing 80 percent of produced gas, improving refining capacity through privatisation and construction of new refineries, improving efficiency and transparency of downstream operations and ensuring all oil and gas operators have and implement a decommissioning and asset retirement (DAR) plan.",""],[1,"62","8","Holistic Oil and Gas Security Policy","Develop a holistic oil and gas security policy enforced by relevant security agencies, including the police force and the Nigeria Security and Civil Defence Corps.",""],[1,"62","11","Energy Sector Sustainability Mainstreaming","The government would pay attention to the overall energy sector considering the current need for environmental sustainability.",""]],"50":[[1,"62","4","Petrochemicals Sector Enabling Environment","Provide an enabling environment for the petrochemicals sub-sector to thrive and reduce imports.",""],[1,"62","4","Completion and Operation of Fertilizer Plants","The government will ensure the needed enabling environment for existing fertilizer plants to be completed and made operational whilst encouraging other projects through an enabling regulatory framework and favourable business environment.",""],[1,"61","21","Crude Oil Production Expansion and Cost Optimization Initiative","Increase crude oil production to 2.38mbpd by ensuring the stability of the Niger Delta environment, reducing the cost of operations to US$10 per barrel through cost optimization and cost-sharing initiatives amongst Joint Venture participants.",""]],"51":[[1,"63","4","Geophysical and Geochemical Assay Laboratory Development","geophysical and geochemical assay laboratory to improve availability of geoscience data of interest to local actors and potential foreign investors",""],[1,"63","4","Minerals Resource Centre Construction","building minerals resource centres in Kagara, Niger and Kogi state",""],[1,"63","4","Safer Mining Technique Centres","safer mining technique centres for precious metals and tin in Kaduna and Osun states",""],[1,"67","1","Mining Geo-Data Bank","mining geo-data bank.",""],[1,"60","16","Reliable Data and Information System Improvement","The information asymmetry, owing to lack of reliable data constrains proper policy formulation in critical areas such as storage and financial management, will be rectified.",""]],"52":[[1,"66","2","Mineral Sector Regulatory Authority Establishment","The Government will establish an independent and well-resourced regulatory authority responsible for the orderly development of the mining industry.",""],[1,"66","2","Mineral Licensing Transparency and Compliance Reform","A regulator will guarantee fair competition to boost private investors' confidence in the sector, improve transparency in the award of mineral titles and facilitate public access to information on issued licenses.",""],[1,"66","2","Mining Sector Investment Climate Reform","Additionally, legislative reforms will focus on initiatives that will improve the sector's investment climate by promoting stability, predictability, and effectiveness, such as collaborating with security agencies to guarantee the safety of mining sites.",""],[1,"66","2","National Council on Mining and Mineral Resources Development Stakeholder Participation","Broad-based stakeholders' participation in policy formulation through the annual National Council on Mining and Mineral Resources Development (NCMMRD) will be encouraged to secure buy-in.",""],[1,"66","2","State Participation Streamlining in Minerals Sector","Finally, the federal government will streamline state participation in the minerals sector by including states in national regulatory activities to ensure policy alignment.",""],[1,"67","5","Solid Minerals Sector Investment Promotion and Reform","the Government's contribution of capital expenditure to the Ministry will be used mainly as an investment to facilitate the entry and operations of the private sector.",""],[1,"67","5","Mining Sector Reform and Policy Package","Therefore, the government will prioritise reforms and other necessary policies to attract investment from global and domestic large-scale mining corporations and from registered artisanal miners that are to be integrated into the large-scale players.",""],[1,"67","6","Sustainable and Transparent Mining Sector Development","This plan will foster an investment-friendly mineral sector that is well-managed with transparent revenues and good governance.",""]],"53":[[1,"65","10","Foreign Investment Attraction in the Minerals Sector","Attract foreign investment in the minerals sector",""],[1,"65","15","Minerals Sector Production Capacity Expansion","Increase the production capacity of the minerals sector",""],[1,"66","3","Revitalization of Ajaokuta Steel Company and NIOMCO","Government will revitalize Ajaokuta Steel Company Limited (ASCL) and the Nigerian Iron Ore and Mining Company (NIOMCO) by adopting the best arrangement to free them from all hindrances and ultimately make them operational and viable.",""],[1,"66","6","Seed Fund and Investment Mobilization for Value-Added Mineral Processing","Increase access to finance to develop value-added products through the establishment of seed funds and the attraction of foreign and local investments.",""],[1,"66","6","Mineral Sector Infrastructure Investment","The government will invest in increased infrastructure for activities in this sector and further leverage the Natural Resources Development Fund to develop the sector.",""],[1,"66","6","Mineral Processing Machinery Procurement Support","This will be used to provide the needed financing for several actors in this sector, especially for the procurement of machinery to process minerals to meet quality standards for export and local use.",""],[1,"66","6","Mineral Exploration and Raw Steel Materials Investment Promotion","Other efforts include attracting investment to explore and produce raw steel materials (iron ore, coal and bitumen, among others) and exploring the World Bank's Mineral Sector Support for Economic Diversification (Mindiver) project.",""],[1,"66","7","Mining Economic Clusters and Value-Addition Linkages","The Government will create mining economic clusters with extensive backward and forward linkages both orientated around the minerals sector and the broader economy.",""],[1,"66","7","Mining-to-Processing Infrastructure and Power Supply Support","Linking mines to processing facilities and providing power to guarantee uninterrupted operations will boost productivity and competitiveness.",""],[1,"66","7","Steel Industry Capacity Reinforcement","Additionally, Nigeria will reinforce the emerging steel industry's production capacity to aid these upstream-downstream linkages and increase value addition.",""]],"54":[[1,"66","4","Inclusive Host Mining Communities Development Strategy","Adopt an inclusive strategy that will improve the socio-economic and environmental sustainability of host mining communities.",""],[1,"66","4","Artisanal and Small-Scale Mining Rural Development Policy","Develop an Artisanal and Small-Scale Mining (ASM) policy into a broad rural development strategy aligned with development plans at all levels of government and linked to other national rural sector strategies.",""],[1,"66","5","Local Content Regulations for ASM Subcontracting and Mentoring","by using local content regulations to require large corporations to integrate ASM subcontracting and mentoring programmes into their activities.",""],[1,"67","6","Inclusive Artisanal and Environmentally Responsible Mining","Establishing a sustainable mining sector inclusive of artisanal mining, environmentally friendly and socially responsible, will enhance Nigeria's mineral attractiveness to exploration and mining investors.",""]],"55":[[1,"67","2","Nigerian Circular Economy and Environmental Protection Programme","Develop a Nigerian circular economy and environmental protection programme to reduce the footprint of mine waste and create new job opportunities.",""],[1,"67","2","Mine Closure, Pollution, and Waste Control Regulatory Strengthening","Nigeria will strengthen the policy framework and regulations around mine closures, pollution and waste control.",""],[1,"67","2","State-Level Mine Energy Efficiency and Emissions Reduction Strategy","The Government will collaborate on a strategy with states to improve energy efficiency and reduce greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions associated with Nigerian mines.",""],[1,"67","2","State Environmental Management Capacity Building for Mining Areas","The Government will work to build state institutions' environmental management capacity, so they are better equipped to protect host communities and uphold environmental regulations.",""]],"56":[[1,"70","3","Infrastructure Development for CCHT Sector Growth","To unlock the potential of these sectors, infrastructural development will be prioritised with policies that strengthen the overall enabling environment for businesses in this industry.",""],[1,"70","3","Public-Private Partnership for Local Manufacturing and Distribution","Furthermore, the government will partner with the private sector to encourage local manufacturing and secure local retail and distribution channels.",""],[1,"70","12","Creative Industry Technical and Financial Support","improve technical and financial support for the creative industry",""],[1,"70","17","Tourism Sector Reform and Promotion Campaigns","Increase focus on the tourism sector through local asset maintenance and global marketing campaigns.",""],[1,"70","18","Tourism Promotion Campaigns","including increased funding for maintenance of public assets, local and international campaigns to boost tourism, and the training of public servants for efficient service delivery.",""],[1,"70","18","State Tourism Office Establishment","Tourism offices will also be established in states to identify tourism opportunities and ensure that heritage sites are properly renovated and maintained.",""],[1,"70","19","Creative Hubs and Market Linkage Support","The government will strengthen market linkages and provide technical support to establish creative hubs that will deliver start-ups and market access support to creatives, including MSMEs.",""],[1,"71","1","Creative Sector Recovery and Development Plan","Address the long-term effects of the COVID-19 pandemic on the creative sector by introducing a 10-year recovery plan in partnership with the private sector actors.",""],[1,"71","1","Creative Industry Funding Support","(i) providing funding for stakeholders in the creative industry;",""],[1,"71","1","Creative Think Tank Formation","(ii) forming creative think tanks in the six geopolitical zones;",""],[1,"71","1","Creative Talent Training Programme","(iii) providing training for talent across Nigeria;",""],[1,"71","1","Online Platform for Nigerian Creatives","(iv) improving local and international market linkages by developing an online platform for Nigerian creatives;",""],[1,"71","1","International Festivals Promotion Initiative","(v) holding international festivals in Nigeria to promote Nigeria's art and culture to the world.",""],[1,"71","2","Innovative Financing Framework for the Creative Sector","Leverage successes achieved by institutions, such as Bank of Industry, through an innovative financing framework to support the creative sector towards further deepening the growth of the sector in Nigeria.",""],[1,"71","3","Blended Financing Support for Public Agencies, Artists, and MSMEs","Investments in these sectors will be significantly boosted through increased access to financing for public agencies, artists, and MSMEs through the use of blended financing tools.",""],[1,"71","5","Intellectual Property Collateral Lending Framework","the CBN's classification of intellectual property as collateral will increase lending to the creative sector",""],[1,"71","5","Investment Facilitation for CCHT Sectors","Facilitating investments in CCHT sectors will benefit a wide range of actors, encourage innovation, and ultimately increase revenue",""],[1,"71","6","Public Investment and Private Capital Mobilization for CCHT Infrastructure","The government will commit approximately N114.24bn as public investment during the planning period to achieve the goals outlined in the CCHT sector and facilitate significant private capital.",""],[1,"71","6","Critical Infrastructure Support for the Private Sector","This is to foster a globally competitive investment climate for the CCHT sector and prioritise projects identified as critical infrastructural support for the private sector.",""],[1,"71","7","Creative Sector Technical and Financial Support","Nigeria will focus on improving technical and financial support for CCHT businesses, increase institutional capacity, and introduce policies to safeguard and encourage innovation.",""]],"57":[[1,"73","4","Quality Policy Improvement","Quality Policy will improve Nigeria's trading potential and overall competitiveness through improved products and services.",""],[1,"73","6","Export-Led Trade Policy and Market Expansion Strategy","Nigeria plans to make effective and proactive policies and strategies to advance its trade potential and create new markets for 'Made in Nigeria' goods and services, completely digitise and automate trade processes and increase the contribution of non- oil exports.",""],[1,"74","4","Export Market Access Support for Nigerian Businesses","Deepen domestic and international market penetration for Nigerian products and services by supporting businesses to increase their exports.",""],[1,"74","5","Trade Policy Review and Modernisation","Reviewing current trade policies, conceptualising and adopting a 21st-century trade policy focusing on trade facilitation and exports promotion.",""],[1,"74","5","Trade Process Automation and Facilitation Reform","Automation of critical processes to address inefficiencies, prioritising the implementation of the WTO Trade Facilitation Agreement, to which Nigeria is a signatory.",""],[1,"74","6","Regional Trade Reform and Trade Remedies Plan","Launch reforms to ensure the effectiveness of regional trading whilst minimizing negative externalities such as dumping.",""],[1,"74","6","ECOWAS Trade Standardisation Framework","Maximise regional trade benefits by standardising informal components of trade among ECOWAS member states and providing a framework for expansion to the rest of Africa in light of the continental free trade area.",""]],"58":[[1,"76","4","Inland Dry Port and Inland Container Depot Development","Existing deep seaports were further decongested through the establishment of an Inland Dry Port and several inland container depots, in addition to other initiatives to improve internal operations and vehicular",""],[1,"76","5","Inland Dry Port and Inland Container Depot Development","The Ministry of Transport established Nigeria's first inland dry port in Kaduna and six inland container depots in Oyo, Abia, Katsina, Kano, Kaduna, Jos and Borno States to reduce congestion in Nigeria's ports.","Ministry of Transport"],[1,"76","5","Truck Transit Parks Development under PPP Model","the Road Transport and Mass Transit Administration Department and the Nigerian Shipper's Council are facilitating the development of \"Truck Transit Parks\" (TTPs) under a PPP Model to further reduce congestion on the road transport corridors.",""],[1,"76","5","Rail Link Construction to Apapa and Port Harcourt Ports","rail links are being constructed to lead to the Apapa and Port Harcourt ports to aid the fast evacuation of cargo and reduce cargo dwell time.",""],[1,"76","6","Deep Seaport Development and PPP Structuring","The Ibom deep seaport is in the fifth stage project development process (Government Approval/Procurement Stage), while the Lekki Deep Seaport is under construction, with a mandate from the current government to commence operations in 2022.",""],[1,"76","7","Targeted Road Construction and Rehabilitation Programme","Road construction and rehabilitation across the country followed a targeted and sequenced approach based on prioritised funding over the reported period.",""],[1,"76","7","Public-Private Partnership Road Development Methodology","The Federal Ministry of Works and Housing has adopted a PPP methodology to enable private partners tap into the numerous commercial opportunities along the 35,000 km of Federal Roads Network.","Federal Ministry of Works and Housing"],[1,"76","7","Highway Development Maintenance Initiative","Under the ongoing Highway Development Maintenance Initiative (HDMI), PPP method is being applied to the following routes across the geopolitical zones.",""],[1,"77","2","International Airport Terminal PPP Projects","There are ongoing PPP initiatives in the sector, comprising four international terminals - Port-Harcourt, Lagos, Abuja and Kano.",""],[1,"77","2","National Carrier Establishment","Other PPP initiatives in the sector include Establishment of a National Carrier, Development of the Aviation Leasing Company (ALC) as well as the Development of a Maintenance Repairs and Overhaul (MRO) Facility.",""],[1,"77","2","Aviation Leasing Company Development","Other PPP initiatives in the sector include Establishment of a National Carrier, Development of the Aviation Leasing Company (ALC) as well as the Development of a Maintenance Repairs and Overhaul (MRO) Facility.",""],[1,"77","2","Maintenance, Repair and Overhaul Facility Development","Other PPP initiatives in the sector include Establishment of a National Carrier, Development of the Aviation Leasing Company (ALC) as well as the Development of a Maintenance Repairs and Overhaul (MRO) Facility.",""],[1,"77","15","Completion and Rehabilitation of Ajaokuta-Itakpe-Warri Rail Line","Completion and Rehabilitation of Ajaokuta - Itakpe - Warri Rail Line: The project has also been completed, plain line only; and has commenced some limited passenger operations.",""],[1,"78","24","Standard Gauge Railway Line Development","Ajaokuta(Eganyi)-Obajana-Jakura-Baro-Abuja with an additional line from Ajaokuta-Otukpo(533km) (standard gauge);",""],[1,"79","3","Inland Waterways Transport Development","This leaves much room to explore the potentials in inland waterways as an alternative and cost-effective means of transport connectivity.",""],[1,"79","3","Airport Concession Programme","the concession of the airports which have started will be pursued to its logical conclusion.",""],[1,"79","9","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Investment","Recognising the urgent need to reduce the infrastructure deficit and for deliberate efforts to involve the private sector in the provision of these basic infrastructure facilities, the government encourages private sector investment through the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) projects and direct ownership of assets by the private sector.",""],[1,"79","10","Transport Infrastructure PPP Framework","The government will establish the necessary legal and regulatory frameworks to crowd in additional capital to expand the existing stock of transport infrastructure.",""],[1,"79","10","Public-Private Partnership Mainstreaming for Infrastructure","There is an opportunity for Nigeria to mainstream Public- Private Partnerships (PPPs) to attract additional capital into key infrastructure projects in aviation, railway, road and maritime.",""],[1,"79","11","Integrated Multimodal Transport System Upgrade","By 2025, Nigeria aims to upgrade its current infrastructure to become a well-integrated multi-modal and intermodal transportation system that is economically efficient, socially equitable and environmentally sustainable.",""],[1,"79","11","Private Sector Participation and Transport Financing Reform","The government will incentivize the private sector to attract alternative sources of funding.",""],[1,"79","11","Transport Sector Reform for Private Financing and Infrastructure Expansion","Government will thus promote reforms to enable increased private sector participation for financing, maintenance, and expansion of the existing stock alongside the inauguration and completion of new fit-for-purpose transport infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"80","2","Railway Modernization and Expansion","This will build on the current railway development in progress to further develop into a modernized, dynamic, efficient, and competitive system that provides competitive transport options for industry, commerce, and travellers, fitting seamlessly as a key component of an integrated transport network.",""],[1,"80","3","Road Network Improvement for Intermodal Connectivity","The road network will be improved upon to facilitate intermodal connections and seamlessly support economic activity, enhancing the quality of life and the environment.",""],[1,"80","6","Port Competitiveness and Efficiency Improvement Strategy","Nigerian ports will become the preferred destination in West and Central Africa through deliberate collaborative strategies to grow throughput, improve safety and security, leverage technology to improve efficiency and the ease of doing business.",""],[1,"80","6","Inland Waterways Freight Diversion Initiative","Additionally, the inland waterways will serve as an alternative cheap mode of transportation to decongest the seaports and deliver cargo closer to the hinterland.",""],[1,"80","10","Aviation Infrastructure Expansion","Expand aviation infrastructure",""],[1,"80","13","Road Infrastructure Expansion for Safe Transport","Expand road infrastructure to enable safe transportation of people",""],[1,"80","20","Maritime Sector Collaboration and Efficiency Improvement Strategy","through deliberate collaborative strategies to grow throughput, improve safety and security, leverage on technology to improve efficiency and ease of doing business.",""],[1,"80","31","Multimodal Transport Infrastructure Development",". Improve multimodality to improve the quality of transport services and reduce strain on existing infrastructure by improving operational efficiencies.",""],[1,"81","1","Infrastructure Privatization and Private Sector Participation Framework","This will involve establishing appropriate governance and operational frameworks to attract private sector participation and, in some cases, completing privatizing specific infrastructure.",""],[1,"81","2","Innovative Transport Infrastructure Financing Mechanisms","Explore innovative financing mechanisms for the continued development of transport infrastructure using a mix of financing tools and funding streams.",""],[1,"81","3","Transport Sector Investment Alignment","Align the implementation of this Plan with the National Integrated Infrastructure Master Plan's aspirations, private sector expectations and priorities and required investment for the transportation sector.",""],[1,"81","5","Rail Link Rehabilitation and Expansion Programme","Drive economic development through the delivery of a cost-effective alternative for haulage of cargo by rehabilitating existing rail linkages (e.g. phase 2 and 3 rehabilitation of the Western and Eastern narrow- gauge rail lines), constructing new rail linkages (e.g. to agricultural hubs, solid mineral sites, manufacturing, and industrial hubs).",""],[1,"81","11","Road Linkage Improvement for Economic Diversification","Facilitate concentric economic diversification and GDP growth through the improvement of road linkages to real sectors of the economy and economic centres.",""],[1,"81","12","Integrated Transport Network Connectivity Improvement","Integrate the transport network through improved road connectivity that ensures easy movement of goods from the ports, ICDs, inland waterway terminals, and rail stations",""],[1,"81","13","National Road Network Improvement","Improve on the national road network to accommodate population and traffic growth and facilitate economic and social development through effective movement of goods and people.",""],[1,"81","14","Private Sector Road Financing and Management Enabling Framework","Create an enabling environment for private sector participation in financing and managing roads.",""],[1,"81","15","Road Infrastructure Development to International Standards","Build a globally competitive economy through the provision of road infrastructure that meets internationally acceptable standards.",""],[1,"81","16","Road Construction Programme Improvement","Improve on road construction programme and PPP funding and project delivery",""],[1,"82","5","Deep Seaport and Inland Dry Port Development","The objectives and targets for this sector are anchored on the development of at least two deep seaports and five inland dry ports to decongest existing ports and increase inter-port competition to reduce costs.",""],[1,"82","5","Port Clearance and Vessel Processing Efficiency Improvements","Additionally, investments will be made to reduce the waiting time of vessels, increase the speed of documentation and clearing, and increase overall throughput and ship registry tonnage.",""],[1,"82","6","Ports Infrastructure Upgrade and Trade Facilitation Reform","Implement process infrastructure upgrade to make the Nigerian ports the main destination for shipment in west and central Africa.",""],[1,"82","7","Port Vessel Navigation and Safety Improvement","Improve navigation and safety of vessels within the port limit",""],[1,"82","12","Inland Waterways Safety and Security Improvement","Enhance safety, security on the Inland Waterways while improving integration with other modes of transport and creating the enabling environment to attract private sector participation in the sub-sector that would contribute to the diversification of the economy.",""],[1,"82","16","Sovereign Sukuk Bond Road Financing","Raising the sum of N100 billion on an annual basis via the Sovereign Sukuk Bonds.",""],[1,"82","17","Presidential Infrastructure Development Fund Portfolio","Presidential Infrastructure Development Fund Portfolio (managed by the Nigeria Sovereign Investment Authority): The sum of US$321 million was made available to this fund from the proceeds of the last tranche of\"Abacha Loot\" recovered.",""],[1,"82","17","Lagos-Ibadan Expressway Construction","The proceeds of the fund will be applied to fund the execution of Lagos - Ibadan Expressway, Abuja - Kaduna - Kano Expressway and the 2nd Niger Bridge.",""],[1,"82","17","Abuja-Kaduna-Kano Expressway Construction","The proceeds of the fund will be applied to fund the execution of Lagos - Ibadan Expressway, Abuja - Kaduna - Kano Expressway and the 2nd Niger Bridge.",""],[1,"82","17","Second Niger Bridge Construction","The proceeds of the fund will be applied to fund the execution of Lagos - Ibadan Expressway, Abuja - Kaduna - Kano Expressway and the 2nd Niger Bridge.",""]],"59":[[1,"80","29","Transport Infrastructure Regulatory Harmonization Framework","Establish a clear regulatory framework for sustainable development of transport infrastructure through policy harmonization.",""],[1,"80","30","Railway Bill Passage","the accelerated passing of the Railway Bill to provide direction on how Nigeria's railway system will be operated.",""],[1,"80","30","Transport Sector Bills Passage","the government will accelerate the passing of the various pending Bills on Roads, Aviation, Ports and Harbour, and Inland Waterways that seek to remove binding constraints to unlock investments.",""],[1,"81","4","Railway Regulatory Reform and Sector Modernization","Government will promote reforms to create a modern, flexible and efficient regulatory regime that ensures improved and safe railway operations driven by deep private sector participation and a strong local content base.",""],[1,"81","6","Rail Connectivity Linkage to Inland Container Depots and Ports","Facilitate rail connectivity through the linkage of the NG rail to the six ICDs as identified by the Nigerian Shippers Council, completion of Lagos, Port Harcourt, Onne, Calabar, Warri and Lekki Port-to-rail projects.",""],[1,"81","8","Local Content Expansion in the Railway Value Chain","Expand Nigerian local content in the railway value chain",""]],"60":[[1,"81","18","Airport Concession and Aviation Infrastructure Upgrade Programme","Nigeria's aviation industry will be elevated through the concession of major airports in the country to encourage private sector participation in the development of critical aviation infrastructure.",""],[1,"81","18","Critical Airport Infrastructure Expansion and Maintenance","critical airport infrastructure including runways, air communication and relay stations, terminals and emergency response equipment will be expanded, upgraded and maintained to ensure operational efficiency and minimize congestion.",""],[1,"81","19","Bankable Aviation Infrastructure Development Programme","Accelerated bankable aviation infrastructure development plans to enhance sustainability including PPP projects, concessions and robust aviation business continuity plans;",""],[1,"82","2","Safe and Secure Air Transportation Compliance Programme","Achieve Safe and Secure Air Transportation through comprehensive national compliance to ICAO and IATA standards and regulations;",""],[1,"82","3","Aviation Connectivity Improvement","Improve Aviation Linear Connectivity through efficient and effective airport connectivity that links critical stations across the country;",""]],"61":[[1,"82","8","Port Management Systems Automation","Achieve Efficient port operations through complete automation of port management systems",""],[1,"82","11","Maritime Safety and Security Compliance Programme","Achieve comprehensive compliance with international maritime instruments (IMO&ILO) for enhanced maritime safety and security.",""]],"62":[[1,"83","12","Power Sector Reform and Unbundling Programme","The Power Reform Act 2005 was preceded by the National Electric Power Policy of 2001.",""],[1,"83","12","Presidential Task Force on Power","A major development after the enactment of the Act was the setting up of the Presidential Task Force on Power (\"PTFP\") in June 2010, and the subsequent launching of the Roadmap for Power Sector Reform in August 2010.",""],[1,"83","12","Roadmap for Power Sector Reform","A major development after the enactment of the Act was the setting up of the Presidential Task Force on Power (\"PTFP\") in June 2010, and the subsequent launching of the Roadmap for Power Sector Reform in August 2010.",""],[1,"83","13","Power Sector Assessment and Medium- to Long-Term Planning","To properly develop a medium and long-term plan for the power sector, the Government will carry out an objective assessment of the state of the sector and identify constraints as well as provide sustainable solutions.",""],[1,"85","10","Electricity Distribution Network Privatization","As part of the privatisation programme, the Power Holding Company of Nigeria's (PHCN) distribution network was split into 11 regional grids.",""],[1,"87","10","Liquidity Support to the Nigerian Electricity Supply Market","the Nigerian government to intervene on several occasions with liquidity support to the Nigerian electricity supply market via the Nigeria Bulk Electricity Trader (NBET).",""],[1,"89","2","Power Sector Reform Coordination and Market Tariff Reform","Deepen coordination of power sector reform initiatives across the Electricity Supply Industry to achieve generation, transmission and distribution of 10 MW, while simultaneously improving on liquidity and market confidence through market- reflective tariffs and performance-based industry cost structure.",""],[1,"89","6","Energy Sector Governance and Regulatory Reform","The government will review and strengthen the policy and regulatory environment ensuring appropriate support for Nigeria's energy goals and eliminating conflicting policy positions that may emerge, or duplicative mapping of responsibilities amongst regulatory agencies.",""],[1,"89","6","Energy Sector Data, Tariff, and Compliance Framework Strengthening","Additionally, strengthen the existing operating framework to ensure adequate data and knowledge management, cost-reflective tariffs, and increased compliance by sector players.",""],[1,"89","8","Plan Implementation Alignment with Energy and Infrastructure Priorities","Align the implementation of this Plan with the energy sector aspirations, private sector expectations, priorities and required investments as provided in the National Integrated Infrastructure Master Plan.",""]],"63":[[1,"85","9","Transmission Network Strengthening Projects","Also, 126 approved TCN projects worth about US$1.5 billion are underway to strengthen the transmission network and additional 118 NIPP projects have been approved.",""],[1,"88","1","Additional Power Generation and Grid Optimization","additional generation capacity will be unlocked, and additional generation assets installed in northern Nigeria particularly in Zungeru (Niger) and Kudenda (Kaduna), to balance subnational load requirements. Then the transmission and distribution end will be optimized to ensure that all generated power is efficiently transmitted to the end-users with minimal technical and fiscal losses.",""],[1,"88","19","Presidential Power Initiative Power System Upgrades","The government, through the Presidential Power Initiative (PPI), has engaged Siemens to provide targeted upgrades to the power system in Nigeria.",""],[1,"88","19","Transmission and Distribution Investment Programme","The transmission company of Nigeria and the eleven distribution companies have also shown commitment towards embarking on investments in the sector that would push up power delivery to Nigerians to 7GW by 2023 and 10GW by 2025.",""],[1,"88","20","Completion of the Abuja Transmission Ring Scheme","Completion of the ongoing Abuja Transmission Ring Scheme funded by Agence Française de Développement (AFD).",""],[1,"88","21","Nigeria Electricity Transmission Access Project Completion","Completion of the ongoing Nigeria Electricity Transmission Access Project funded by the World",""],[1,"88","22","WAPP North Core Transmission Project","WAPP North Core Transmission Project funded by the World Bank.",""],[1,"88","23","Northern Corridor Transmission Project","Commencement of the Northern Corridor Transmission Project, funded by the World Bank and the EU.",""],[1,"88","24","Distribution Network Expansion Projects","Several distribution projects aimed at resolving Interface challenges and expanding distribution capacity to 7GW in 2025",""],[1,"89","2","Transmission and Distribution Infrastructure Acceleration","Accelerated execution of Transmission and Distribution Infrastructure projects to utilize existing Generation Capacity/ Successful Implementation of Siemens PPI.",""],[1,"89","3","Power Sector Value-Chain Constraint Removal and Infrastructure Upgrade","The government will work to eliminate constraints across the energy value chain including gas-to-power, generation, transmission, and distribution.",""],[1,"89","3","Proactive Gas-to-Power Interface Management and Planning","The government will pay attention to proactive gas-to-power interface management and planning, to ensure the continued growth of the electricity supply industry.",""],[1,"89","3","Transmission and Distribution Infrastructure Acceleration","The government will ensure the accelerated execution of transmission and distribution infrastructure projects, particularly the successful implementation of the Siemens Presidential Power Initiative (PPI), to utilise existing generation capacity.",""],[1,"89","3","Urban Area Enumeration and Smart Meter Deployment","In the distribution segment, the government will ensure urban area enumeration and proliferation of smart metering systems for revenue assurance of the Power Sector.",""],[1,"89","11","Transmission Network Optimization and Expansion","As the transmission network is further optimized and expanded, idle generating capacity will be progressively unlocked so that Nigerians can benefit from the full breadth of available generating assets.",""]],"64":[[1,"83","3","Alternative Energy Expansion Initiative","In this plan, the government will prioritise efforts to maximise these alternative energy sources to increase energy per capita so as to spur industrialisation.",""],[1,"85","16","Alternative Energy Supply Expansion","consumers have resorted to alternative energy sources to supplement the inadequate supply from the grid.",""],[1,"86","5","Energizing Economics Initiatives","Energizing Economics Initiatives (EEI): This programme supports the rapid deployment of off-grid solutions in economic clusters such as markets and agricultural industrial complexes.",""],[1,"86","6","Energizing Education Programme","Energizing Education Programme (EEP): This programme aims to develop off-grid Independent Power Plant (IPP) Projects for powering 37 Universities and 7 University Teaching Hospitals and to provide street lighting and develop and operate Training Centres to train university students.",""],[1,"86","7","Nigeria Electrification Project","Nigeria Electrification Project (NEP): This programme",""],[1,"86","8","Off-Grid Market Catalyzation Support","It provides a pipeline of local investments and incentives required to catalyse the off-grid market through Market Data, Grant Funding and Technical Assistance.",""],[1,"86","9","Rural Electrification Fund","Rural Electrification Fund (REF): This provides funds for cost-effective expansion of electricity in un- electrified areas.",""],[1,"86","10","Nigerian Energy Support Programme","Nigerian Energy Support Programme (NESP): This program is supported by the German Government and the European Union and is implemented by GIZ.",""],[1,"86","10","Mini-Grid Acceleration Scheme","Under this programme, two schemes are rolled out to support the mini-grid market: The mini-grid acceleration scheme (MAS) and the Inter-connected Mini-Grid acceleration scheme (IMAS).",""],[1,"86","10","Inter-connected Mini-Grid Acceleration Scheme","Under this programme, two schemes are rolled out to support the mini-grid market: The mini-grid acceleration scheme (MAS) and the Inter-connected Mini-Grid acceleration scheme (IMAS).",""],[1,"86","11","Rural Solar Lighting Distribution Initiative","In February 2017, Nigeria launched an initiative to distribute 20,000 solar-powered lighting systems to rural communities in the country.",""],[1,"86","11","Off-grid Solar Power Expansion Target","the Federal Government plans to work towards adding 13GW of off-grid solar power by 2030.",""],[1,"86","11","Lagos Solar Off-grid Electrification Project","the Lagos state government through the Lagos Solar project, a joint investment of Lagos State Electricity Board (LSEB) and the UK Department for International Development (DFID) has installed nearly 5 MWp of solar-generated off-grid power for 172 schools and 11 clinics within Lagos State.",""],[1,"86","11","Solar Nigeria Off-grid Health Clinic Electrification","An additional 1.5 MWp is being installed at public health clinics in Kaduna State under the Solar Nigeria programme by DFID.",""],[1,"88","1","Rural Renewable Energy Expansion","The government will ramp up and leverage renewable energy to reduce the number of residents without access to electricity, especially in rural areas not currently connected to the grid.",""],[1,"88","2","Rural and Urban Renewable Energy Expansion","It is envisaged that over 75 percent of rural and remote locations will be provided with power via renewable energy sources (including small hydropower, solar, biomass and wind).",""],[1,"88","16","Renewable Energy Supply Improvement","Improve renewable energy supply",""],[1,"88","25","Solar Independent Power Producer Projects","1,125MW will be realized from 14nos Solar IPP Projects that have existing licenses and PPAs with NBET",""],[1,"88","25","Off-Grid Renewable Energy Projects","a cumulative of 475MW will be realized from Off-Grid Renewable energy projects",""],[1,"89","4","Renewable Energy Policy, Regulatory, and Infrastructure Support","the government will ensure appropriate policy and regulatory support and then build associated infrastructure to drive renewable energy generation, rural electrification expansion and the development of both isolated and interconnected mini-grid systems to serve various locations.",""],[1,"89","4","Off-grid and On-grid Renewable Energy Project Acceleration","To successfully accelerate ongoing off-grid and on-grid renewable energy projects, the Government will continue to",""],[1,"89","5","Off-Grid Electrification Strategy","drive the Rural Electrification Agency (REA) Off-Grid Electrification Strategy and Rural Electricity Fund (REF).",""],[1,"89","5","Rural Electricity Fund","drive the Rural Electrification Agency (REA) Off-Grid Electrification Strategy and Rural Electricity Fund (REF).",""],[1,"89","7","Alternative Energy PPP Framework","Government will facilitate the prerequisite framework for a PPP arrangement to fully develop alternative energy resources across the country to increase energy per capita in the country.",""],[1,"89","11","Alternative Energy Development through Public-Private Partnerships","Priority will also be geared towards developing the abundant alternative energy sources such as wind, solar, biomass through a robust PPP arrangement to increase energy use per capita and also ensure the use of environmentally sustainable energy sources.",""]],"65":[[1,"87","14","Reliable Natural Gas Supply to Thermal Power Plants","Firstly, this requires the reliable and sustainable supply of natural gas to all operational thermal generating plants in the country to achieve 10,000 MW of electricity supply.",""],[1,"88","26","Gas Supply Activation for Thermal Power Plants","With regards to gas supply, the target is to achieve the full supply of gas required for all thermal power generation plants currently installed all over Nigeria (private Gencos, NIPPs and IPPs), and to activate all subsisting contracts.",""]],"66":[[1,"91","19","Housing and Mortgage Finance Reform","Also, unlocking Housing and Mortgage Finance and Capital Formation through the market and legislative reforms is essential to unlocking the potential of the sector for shelter, jobs and economic growth.",""],[1,"92","3","Mortgage Finance Sector Funding Mechanisms","Facilitate real estate specific capital formation and funding mechanisms for growing the mortgage finance sector: The government, in partnership with the private sector, will create a market that has multiple long-term funding sources including full integration with the Nigerian capital market where",""],[1,"92","4","Mortgage Market Development and Housing Finance Expansion","establish a robust mortgage market that provides access to housing finance to a minimum of 20 percent of Nigerians in all social classes in urban centres for the purpose of owning their own houses; integrate housing financial products into the Nigerian capital market to facilitate access to homeownership for millions of Nigerians and build up demand for housing; create long term mortgage financing by developing financial tools for buyers and put in place financial instruments to boost the supply of housing; and expand financing options from commercial banks, insurance companies and pension funds through incentives, tax breaks and guarantees.",""],[1,"93","6","Long-Term Housing Finance Access Mechanism","Securing the availability of long-term housing financing to facilitate access to home ownership for everyone will ultimately improve social inclusion and allow low- income Nigerians to build wealth.",""],[1,"93","6","Mortgage Bank and Family Homes Efficiency Improvement","The operational efficiency of the Federal Mortgage Bank and the Family Homes in collaboration with the primary Mortgage Banks and the private real estate firms will be a priority.",""]],"67":[[1,"91","7","Digital Land Mapping for Housing Sector Development","the government will leverage current opportunity around technology advancements to further drive growth in the housing sector.",""],[1,"91","8","Technology-Enabled Urban Planning and Smart Housing Solutions","the use of technology and data analytics would enable local authorities to better understand the scope of planning and administration required to build sustainable cities across Nigeria.",""],[1,"91","19","Urban and Regional Development Boards Establishment","The establishment of the Urban and Regional Development Boards (URDB) charged with the responsibility for the overall supervision including monitoring and management of urban development as well as planning across states will bridge the gap between current housing supply and demand in Nigeria.",""],[1,"91","19","Housing Sector Coordination Mechanism","This is critical as efforts will be geared towards proper collaboration and coordination among the Federal Mortgage Bank, Primary Mortgage Banks, family homes and other private real",""],[1,"91","21","National Urban Development Policy and Plan","Develop and implement a national urban development policy and plan that focuses on urban renewal, provision of low/ medium income housing, while checking rural to",""],[1,"92","1","National Urban Development Institutional Framework","Support the national urban development policy and plan with an institutional framework that recreates the Federal Ministry of Housing and Urban Development and establishes Regional Development Boards (URDB) across the states including the FCT.","Federal Ministry of Housing and Urban Development"],[1,"92","6","Data-Driven Housing and Informal Settlement Management System","A two- pronged approach, focusing on building affordable housing and informal settlements and infrastructure upgrades for the poor will be designed.",""],[1,"93","5","Urban Road Development Investment","This includes an estimated public investment in the urban road development of about N1.68trn.",""]],"68":[[1,"93","1","Land Registry Digitalization Initiative","to map and digitalise land registries to improve accountability and transparency across the sector.",""],[1,"93","2","Comprehensive Land Management System Reform","Develop an effective land management system to provide transparency and ease the administrative burden of the land administration process: The comprehensive system will include policies and implement legislation that will reform land administration, title acquisition, registration, and transferability to establish clear property rights.",""]],"69":[[1,"91","6","Local Building Materials Promotion Initiative","Massive housing construction will also significantly boost demand for locally crafted materials to reduce construction costs as well as stimulate job creation, particularly in the construction and manufacturing sectors of the economy.",""],[1,"92","6","Local Building Materials and Affordable Housing Innovation Programme","The government will promote and increase the use of local building materials to achieve a target of 75 percent of building components through the creation of an investment climate that engenders building manufacturing investment; promote and increase the use of alternative building materials and new technologies in housing delivery through incisive research and development and execution of pilot projects in each state of the federation and the FCT; apply building materials focused research and development by way of pilot housing schemes built majorly from alternative locally produced materials and new technology; Incentivise and adopt low-cost housing construction technologies and innovative affordable housing delivery methods.",""],[1,"93","1","Housing Startup Innovation Support","Moreover, the government will incentivise housing start-up development through innovation hubs and accelerator programs.",""],[1,"93","3","Housing Sector Skills Capacity Building Initiative","Design capacity building initiatives to secure a qualified labour force with technical skills aligned with the needs of the housing sector:",""],[1,"93","4","Housing Market Legal Reform Package","Undertake the necessary legal reforms to unlock the opportunities in the housing market: This would include pursuing outstanding legal reforms, specifically Bills pending in the National Assembly, that relate to the National Housing Fund and Federal",""],[1,"93","5","Housing Sector Public Investment Programme","To achieve the goals outlined in the housing sector, the estimated public investment is N3.53trn from 2021- 2025.",""]],"70":[[1,"94","2","Digital Economy Foundation-Building Initiative","In the medium-term, the country is committed to establishing the critical building blocks for the digital economy and laying the foundation for its increased contributions to improved economic competitiveness across sectors.",""],[1,"94","7","National ICT Infrastructure Backbone Expansion","Further, 98 percent of the approximately 1400 Km of the National Information Communications Technology Infrastructure Backbone (NICTIB) phase 1 has been completed and is in operation across 11 states.",""],[1,"94","7","NICTIB II Fibre Optic Connectivity Project","Further, in 2020, the Nigerian government supported leading fibre and transmission infrastructure companies to extend coverage through the second phase of the NICTIB II project, with over 3,250 km of fibre optic cables running across the six geopolitical regions.",""],[1,"94","7","Private Credit-Financed Broadband Connectivity Expansion","The NICTIB II, which is being funded through a US$328 million private credit facility, will provide connectivity across several towns and cities along its routes, thus facilitating access to broadband services for an estimated population of over 9.2 million people.",""],[1,"94","8","Digital Economy Policy and Broadband Plan Regulatory Support","The government has focused on expanding regulatory support through policy design, including the National Digital Economy Policy and Strategy, Nigerian National Broadband Plan and Smart Nigeria Digital Economy",""],[1,"95","1","Right-of-Way Charge Pegging for ICT Infrastructure","The Government's recent decision to peg right of way charges should make it easier to lay fibre optic cables, as well as boost the construction of base stations and other ICT infrastructure",""],[1,"96","26","Digital Infrastructure Investment and Innovation Fund","Efforts will focus on driving investment in the development of digital infrastructure, especially for internet connectivity, to increase fast, inclusive, and affordable access to the internet across Nigeria.",""]],"71":[[1,"95","15","Digital Economy Regulatory Strengthening","Thus, the introduction of a stronger regulatory environment to protect and include more Nigerians in a digital economy is critical to eliminating bottlenecks and guaranteeing the competitiveness of Nigerian businesses.",""],[1,"95","16","Economy Digitisation Initiative","the government will take measures to digitise the economy and make digitalization a key driver of national economic development strategies.",""],[1,"96","23","Patent Protection Policy Reform","To encourage future technological advancements, policies that focus on patent protection will be implemented to boost the protection of businesses that foster the progress of a digital economy.",""],[1,"96","23","Regulatory Sandbox Operations","The Nigerian government will also implement Regulatory Sandbox Operations, aimed at establishing a controlled environment where disruptive technology in financial services can be tested.",""],[1,"96","23","Digital Economy Policy Harmonization","The government will also ensure policy harmonization to guide the development of the digital economy.",""],[1,"96","24","Digital Transformation Policy Implementation","(AUC) to introduce and implement policies that support the commission's Digital Transformation",""]],"72":[[1,"96","16","Digital Entrepreneurship Promotion","Encourage Digital Entrepreneurship",""],[1,"97","1","Technology Company Incentive Support","The government will also encourage technology companies to take advantage of existing incentives such as the pioneer status incentives.",""],[1,"97","1","Subsidized Land for Technology Hubs and Villages","the government will work with states to provide land at subsidized rates to companies that wish to establish hubs or technology villages in Nigeria.",""],[1,"97","4","Digital Economy Investment and Innovation Hub Support","Increase financial and technical support in the digital economy ecosystem, through local and foreign investments and strategic partnerships.",""],[1,"97","4","Investor One-Stop-Shop for High-Technology Hubs","the government will incentivize local and foreign investments, through access to land and other capital, as well as creating a one-stop-shop for local and foreign investors in the high technology hubs.",""],[1,"97","4","Support for Existing and New Digital Innovation Hubs","The government will also support existing innovation hubs in the digital space and provide incentives for the creation of many more",""],[1,"97","8","Financial Inclusion and Digital Business Support Measures","the government will implement the identified strategic measures that focus on digital skills development, financial inclusion, job creation and provision of technical and financial support to businesses that are powered by digital technologies.",""]],"73":[[1,"97","2","STEM and Digital Curriculum Reform","the Education Ministry will revise and update the school curriculum to include such subjects as coding, data science and advanced applied science, that include artificial intelligence, robotic science, and bioinformatics.","Education Ministry"],[1,"97","2","Teacher and Student Digital Skills Development Programme","the Ministry of Communications and Digital Economy and other relevant MDAs will work closely with the Ministry of Education, to drive skills development for teachers, and to train students at all levels.","Ministry of Communications and Digital Economy | Ministry of Education"],[1,"97","4","Digital Upskilling Partnership with Microsoft","An example of this is the government's recent partnership with Microsoft which aims to digitally upskill 5 million Nigerians.",""],[1,"97","8","Digital Skills Development Programme","the government will implement the identified strategic measures that focus on digital skills development, financial inclusion, job creation and provision of technical and financial support to businesses that are powered by digital technologies.",""]],"74":[[1,"101","1","Financial Sector Resilience and Resource Mobilisation","Consequently, it is imperative to increase the robustness and resilience of Nigeria's financial sector to ensure availability of financial resources for economic growth and development.",""],[1,"101","2","Banking Supervision and Financial Stability Oversight","The apex Bank is maintaining the stability and soundness of the banking institutions by enhancing its on-site and off-site supervision.",""],[1,"101","2","Credit Channeling to Critical Economic Sectors","It encourages banks and other financial institutions to channel credit to critical sectors of the economy and increased efforts are targeted at building a robust payment system.",""],[1,"101","2","Financial Inclusion and Digital Financial Services Expansion","These efforts have assisted in achieving the Bank's cashless policy, financial inclusion and digitisation of financial services, leveraging Fintechs and other financial agents.",""],[1,"101","2","Bank Verification Number Expansion","Enrolment into the Bank Verification Number (BVN) system is about 50 million and this is anticipated to double by the end of the Plan.",""],[1,"101","2","BVN-NIN Integration for Financial Access","With the on-going integration of the BVN system with the National Identification Number (NIN), it is expected that access to financial services will become far easier going forward.",""],[1,"101","4","Derivatives Trading Regulation and Central Counterparty Registration","These include the new regulation on derivatives and the registration of Central Counterparty (CCPs) aimed at the commencement of derivatives trading in Nigeria.",""],[1,"101","4","Digital Capital Market Rules for Fintech-Enabled Trading Platforms","To further expand the product space and align with recent developments in fintech, the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) in recent times has released rules and regulation of Warehousing and Collateral Management, Robo-advisory, Crowdfunding and other digital trading platforms.",""],[1,"101","6","Insurance Sector Automation and Risk-Based Supervision Reform","The National Insurance Commission (NAICOM) has worked towards improving the effectiveness and efficiency of the insurance sector through investments in automation and risk-based supervision.",""],[1,"101","6","Insurance and Reinsurance Recapitalisation Exercise","It has also embarked on a recapitalisation exercise to increase the minimum paid- up share capital of insurance and reinsurance companies.",""],[1,"101","6","Multi-Fund Pension Structure","Furthermore, the National Pension Commission (PenCom) recently introduced a multi-fund structure to align the age and risk profile of retirement savings account holders.",""],[1,"101","6","Micro Pension Coverage Expansion","PenCom is equally pursuing the micro pension plan to cover the self-employed and persons working in organizations with less than 3 employees.",""],[1,"102","12","Innovative Domestic Capital Mobilization Instruments","Nigeria can mobilize additional domestic capital through innovative instruments and measures.",""],[1,"103","1","Financial Formalization, Literacy and Inclusion Initiatives","it is, therefore, important to target formalization, financial literacy, and inclusion initiatives at a wide range of demographic segments and industries.",""],[1,"103","1","Fintech-Enabled Financial Service Expansion","Recent innovations in Fintech are enabling the extension of financial services to the underserved population and this will be leveraged in executing this Plan.",""],[1,"103","11","Capital Markets Development for Debt and Equity Financing","Capital Markets: Provide direct debt financing for governments and businesses, and market valuation and equity funding for their companies",""],[1,"103","17","Non-Bank Financial Institution Financing for Underserved Sectors and Clusters","NBFIs: Provide financing for sectors and clusters that might otherwise have been excluded from financing by banks and markets",""],[1,"104","5","Framework to Unlock Pension Assets for Infrastructure and Mortgages","appropriate frameworks will also be developed to unlock pension assets for the development of infrastructure and mortgages.",""],[1,"104","5","Financial System Coordination and Stability Framework","The framework for financial system coordination and stability will be strengthened",""],[1,"104","5","Fintech Sector Regulatory and Policy Reform","necessary regulatory and policy reforms will be made to foster and regulate the growth of the fintech sector.",""],[1,"104","9","Leveraging Development Finance Institutions to Support Private Sector Investment","The investments of these government institutions will be leveraged to organise and support the private sector to realise the goals of the Plan.",""],[1,"104","11","Private Capital Mobilization and Financial Inclusion Measures","By establishing the right structures to crowd-in private capital into the financial markets and increasing financial inclusion, Nigeria can attract much-needed financial resources to achieve its desired level of economic growth and development.",""],[1,"95","15","Mobile Money and Digital Payments Expansion","Financial services providers can be encouraged by government policies and incentives to expand mobile money services and digital payment solutions for seamless operations across borders.",""]],"75":[[1,"103","2","Government Asset Equity Issuance and Private Asset Management","Nigeria also stands the chance of attracting foreign capital inflows. This will be facilitated as Nigeria augments the current debt financing strategies with some opportunities to issue equities on government assets and allow qualified private players to manage relevant government assets in a transparent and result-oriented manner.",""],[1,"103","4","Private Finance Arrangements for Infrastructure Delivery","are well positioned to grow and contribute to the general development of the country when properly harnessed to raise funds to finance Nigeria's infrastructure needs by issuing revenue bonds, securitising government assets and adopting other private finance arrangements, that allow private sector to provide services and infrastructure to the public in a transparent and competitive manner, thereby allowing for efficiency and improved revenue generation.",""],[1,"103","22","Asset Register Creation for Investable Assets","The plan, therefore, is to create Asset Registers to know what",""],[1,"103","23","Asset Monetization and Securitization Programme","This will enable Nigeria to unlock liquidity by leveraging assets to issue large scale brownfield and greenfield equity as well as asset-based and asset-backed securities.",""],[1,"103","23","Idle Land and Built Structure Commercialization Programme","Efforts will also be made to commercialize idle/underutilized lands and built structures by repurposing and redeveloping them to open new streams of large, growing, and securitise rental/",""],[1,"104","1","Asset Transaction Framework Review and Liberalization Policy","relevant legal and policy frameworks will be reviewed to eliminate loopholes and impediments to successful asset transaction plans.",""],[1,"104","1","Investment Liberalization Policy for Asset Flows","Government will also put in place policies that will liberalize and remove barriers to attract and drive both domestic and foreign investment flows into such assets.",""],[1,"104","2","Automated Online Deal Origination and Consummation Platform","Create a transparent one-stop automated online deal origination/consummation process for connecting projects listed in the investable asset register with global liquidity.",""],[1,"104","3","Public Asset Optimization Transparency and Communication Campaign","To make this successful, the government will ensure transparency to reassure the populace that the public asset optimization efforts will serve the public rather than private interest.",""],[1,"104","3","Global Roadshows for Asset Promotion","Also, a robust communication and media campaign strategy will be developed, including global roadshows, to drive global and regional awareness for the various assets on offer.",""],[1,"82","18","Infrastructure Company (InfraCo) Establishment","The Central Bank of Nigeria is putting together an Infrastructure Company (InfraCo) in collaboration with the NSIA and some Private Capital Funding sources.",""],[1,"82","19","Pension Fund Investment in Infrastructure Financing","An additional US$1.5 billion could be sourced from pension funds, assuming Nigeria's pension fund assets valued at over US$31.3 billion in 2019 grows at an average rate of 15.0 percent per annum over the five years and pensions funds opt to invest in infrastructure funds and infrastructure bonds up to the thresholds they are allowed to do.",""]],"76":[[1,"104","6","Financial Sector Roadmap for AfCFTA Integration","A roadmap will be developed for the financial sector to facilitate the achievement of AfCFTA and ensure the integration of the Nigerian financial sector with the region.",""],[1,"95","15","Digital Trade and E-Commerce Ecosystem Development","The trade sector will require a digital payment and ecommerce ecosystem to reach new markets and reduce operation costs for traders, especially for women and small businesses, who are heavily involved in cross border trading.",""],[1,"95","15","Digital Agricultural Market Linkage Platforms","Finally, the agricultural sector can utilise digital platforms to address market linkage bottlenecks.",""]],"77":[[1,"106","7","Armed Forces Operational Capability Upgrade","Nigeria has continued to scale up the operational capability of the AFN in terms of human capacity and operational hard wares - some of which are being manufactured or revamped locally.",""],[1,"107","14","Creation of a Nigerian Defence Industrial Base","Among these is the creation of a Nigerian Defence Industrial Base.",""],[1,"108","1","Armed Forces Capability Strengthening and National Security Architecture","Nigeria will aim to have a robust Armed Forces of Nigeria (AFN) that will act within its mandate to combat present and future threats, internal and external, to the Nigerian State and its people.",""],[1,"108","2","Strengthening the AFN for Agility and Adaptability","Strengthen the AFN to make it more agile and adaptable, with enhanced capabilities to respond to",""],[1,"108","4","National Defence Intelligence and Security Technology Upgrade","Augment national defence through a robust intelligence system by adopting AI, ICT, robotics, and drone technology, with an active military science research organisation to design, develop, and boost security capacity to reduce cyber threats, counterterrorism, and boost disaster readiness.",""],[1,"108","5","Military Operations Funding Mobilization","Mobilize funding to sustain military operations including war operations, border security, and counterterrorism.",""],[1,"108","20","Defence Capability Enhancement and AFN Professionalisation","The Nigerian government will enhance defence capabilities that enable the AFN to attain security and defence objectives, especially forthe neutralization of domestic terrorist threats in Nigeria.",""],[1,"108","20","AFN Training, Monitoring, and Disciplinary Reform","The government will also introduce examinations, courses, and technological systems to train and track armed officers' activities and increase remuneration for AFN officers.",""],[1,"108","20","Independent Audit-Based Disciplinary Enforcement","Finally, there will be strict disciplinary processes, which will involve independent auditors, to ensure that acts of infringement are adequately addressed.",""],[1,"108","21","Security and Conflict Mitigation Capacity Building","Boost security and conflict mitigation measures through tactical training and MDA partnerships.",""],[1,"108","22","Security Personnel Retraining and Capacity Building","and retraining of security personnel to counter existing and emerging security threats.",""],[1,"108","23","Security and Defence Innovation Investment","Drive security and defence innovation, using science and technology tools.",""],[1,"108","23","Science and Technology Skills Training for Security Agencies","Measures will also be taken to teach core science and technology skills within the security agencies, and to boost cooperation with local",""],[1,"109","5","Personnel Training Investment","Increase investment in personnel training",""]],"78":[[1,"106","7","Security Agency Coordination Improvement","The government also ensured strong coordination between security agencies through improved clarity in the management of the AFN arising from the Nigerian National Defence Policy 2017 and Nigerian National Security Strategy 2019.",""],[1,"106","8","Civil-Military Relations Units Establishment","Establishment of civil-military relations units within the Services which has facilitated growing Civil- Military Cooperation (CIMIC)",""],[1,"106","9","Establishment of the Multinational Joint Task Force","Establishment of the Multinational Joint Task Force",""],[1,"106","10","Establishment of the Regional Intelligence Fusion Unit","Establishment of the Regional Intelligence Fusion Unit (RIFU)",""],[1,"106","11","Regional Cooperation on Counterterrorism and Small Arms Control","Facilitation of regional cooperation with neighbouring countries in tackling terrorism, insurgency and control of Small Arms and Light Weapons (SALWs).",""],[1,"107","1","National Security Strategy Implementation","NSS focuses on protecting Nigerians and territory; ensuring internal security; combating terrorism and countering violent extremism.",""],[1,"107","2","Flexible and Efficient State Response Strategy","a strategy that orients state action towards current and perceived future challenges by using available resources flexibly and efficiently.",""],[1,"107","2","Security Threat Protection and Response Capacity Enhancement","The Strategy will also enhance our protection and response capabilities to security threats in an increasingly complex environment",""],[1,"107","2","Global Security Indicator Benchmarking System","this plan therefore recognizes the imperative of placing a premium on using global indicators to assess and benchmark Nigeria's performance against global security indicators for the attainment of the security goals.",""],[1,"108","6","Security Intelligence Agency Coordination Enhancement","Increase efficient partnership and coordination among security intelligence agencies",""],[1,"108","22","Security Intelligence Coordination and Analysis Strengthening","This would also deepen the intelligence gathering, analysis, coordination and utilisation capacity among the security agencies.",""],[1,"109","3","National Defence Policy and Security Strategy Implementation and Review","Effectively implement the Nigerian National Defence Policy (NNDP) and National Security Strategy (NSS).",""]],"79":[[1,"107","1","Counter-Kidnapping and Armed Banditry Measures","It also seeks to prevent and combat kidnapping, armed banditry and militia activities, promoting cybersecurity development, and promoting research and development in space technology.",""],[1,"107","1","Critical Infrastructure and Specialized Security Protection","Other objectives include combating transnational organized crime, critical national assets and infrastructure security, maritime security, airspace and aviation security, land transportation security, securing ungoverned space, and chemical, biological, radiological, nuclear and explosive security.",""],[1,"108","22","Community Policing and Community Engagement Support","States and community policing and community engagement will also be supported to complement government efforts.",""],[1,"108","22","Conflict Mitigation and Management Measures","In conflict mitigation and management.",""],[1,"108","22","Support for Displaced Persons in Conflict Areas","Further measures will also be taken to care for displaced persons in conflict areas.",""],[1,"108","23","Forensics and Digital Policing Integration","The government will also identify opportunities to integrate forensics and digital technology into policing, to increase the fight against crime.",""],[1,"109","2","Border Security and Domestic Terrorism Control Measures","Boost border control and domestic terrorism measures through bilateral security agreements and support to border control agencies.",""],[1,"109","4","Police, Security, and Judicial Reform","Enact police, other security organizations and judicial reform to ensure safety and security for all:",""],[1,"109","6","Disciplinary Enforcement for Security Personnel","Introduce and enforce strict repercussions infractions for NPF officers and other security organizations with transparent disciplinary processes.",""],[1,"109","7","Forensics and Digital Technology Integration in Policing","integrate forensics and digital technology into policing and other security management,",""],[1,"109","9","NPF-Community Policing Expansion","Increase NPF-community policing in partnership with 36 states",""]],"80":[[1,"109","11","Public Legal Aid Allocation","improve access to fair legal services through the allocation of public lawyers where necessary",""],[1,"109","12","Legal Services Accessibility Expansion","increase accessibility of legal services to more Nigerians",""]],"81":[[1,"109","24","Cybercrime Prosecution Enhancement","Increase the rate of prosecution of cybercrimes offenders",""],[1,"109","25","Cybersecurity Protection for Strategic Institutions","Significantly reduce the possibility of cyber threats and criminality to financial and other strategic institutions",""]],"82":[[1,"109","27","Security Agencies Development and Professionalisation Programme","the government of Nigeria will continue to prioritise the development, capacity building and professionalism of the security agencies to ensure peace and security for all residents.",""],[1,"109","27","Security Architecture Revision and Investment Programme","With continued investments and a revision of its security architecture, it is envisaged that Nigeria will build on successes from the 2017 to 2020 to realise a steep improvement in securing lives and property.",""]],"83":[[1,"110","2","Public Sector Capacity Building and Performance Management Reform","To improve service delivery in the public sector, the government has trained over 40,000 workers and introduced performance reviews for culture and skills development evaluation.",""],[1,"110","2","Civil Service Digital Skills and Capacity Development","To drive efficiency in public operations, the government has trained over 35,000 public sector staff on the use of computers and over 9,000 civil servants in other capacity-building areas.",""],[1,"110","2","Performance Management Systems Training Programme","In addition, the Office of the Head of the Civil Service of the Federation (OHCSF) collaborated with the United Kingdom Department for International Development (UK-DFID) and the Chartered Institute of Personnel Management of Nigeria (CIPM) on a training programme.","Office of the Head of the Civil Service of the Federation (OHCSF)"],[1,"110","2","Civil Service Accountability and Transparency Initiative","Efforts have also been geared towards introducing accountability in the country's civil service to enhance transparency in public processes.",""],[1,"110","2","Digital Civil Service Information Management System","The government has also adopted digital tools for the collection and storing of civil servants' information for proper monitoring and evaluation processes and undertaken a performance survey report on the outgoing ERGP (2017-2020) to identify skills development and management gaps to expand current training programmes.",""],[1,"111","1","Timely Policy Implementation","Moving towards a free and fair public system that would guarantee trust from citizens would require: (i) timely policy implementation;",""],[1,"111","1","Intergovernmental Coordination Improvement","improved coordination across the three tiers of governments and MDAs;",""],[1,"111","1","Civil Service Capacity Strengthening","improved civil service capacity.",""],[1,"111","1","Governance Technology and Data Management Investment","opportunities to improve governance through investments in technologies and data management remain important, contributing to the effectiveness of measurement and planning.",""],[1,"111","18","Inter-Governmental Coordination and Civil Service Efficiency Reform","Increase public sector efficiency by enhancing coordination between the various tiers of government and redefining the competency framework for civil servants.",""],[1,"111","18","Inter-Tier Government Coordination and Strategy Alignment Mechanism","The government will enhance inter-tiered governmental coordination and grassroots decision making and policy implementation by strengthening the operations of relevant agencies.",""],[1,"111","18","Civil Service Training, Performance Management, and Digitization Capacity Programme","In addition, the government will increase the efficiency of civil servants by: (i) introducing training and certification programs;(ii) defining clear key performance indices and (iii) developing digitization capacity for quicker service",""],[1,"111","19","Civil Service Skills Reassessment and Development","Other strategic measures will focus on reassessing current skills compositions and requirements to ensure that civil servants are developing the appropriate skills required for quality service delivery.",""]],"84":[[1,"110","3","Cost of Governance Reduction Policy Measures","The Office of the Secretary to the Government of the Federation (OSGF) initiated policy measures aimed at cutting cost and instilling fiscal discipline and prudence especially in government processes in line with the government's goal of reducing the cost of governance by 30 percent.","Office of the Secretary to the Government of the Federation (OSGF)"],[1,"110","3","Reduction of Recurrent Expenditure Policy Review","The government is currently implementing and reviewing policies to reduce other recurrent expenditure to promote judicious use of public funds and devote savings to developmental projects.",""],[1,"110","3","Restriction on International Travel by Government Officials","One of such efforts is a new policy to cut international travel by government officials.",""],[1,"111","3","Biometric Personnel and Payroll Information System","the biometric-based Integrated Personnel & Payroll Information System (IPPIS) has reduced the loss of revenue through ghost workers, and the introduction of the Bank Verification Number (BVN) has improved the investigation of white-collar crime and asset recovery.",""]],"85":[[1,"109","10","Examination Courses and Official Activity Tracking Systems","Introduce examination courses and technological systems to train and track around officials' activities and ensure accountability",""],[1,"110","5","Law Review and Anti-Corruption Legislative Reform","The Federal Ministry of Justice (FMOJ) inaugurated a Law Review Team to facilitate the review of existing laws on Anti-Corruption, Transparency and Accountability in Governance.","Federal Ministry of Justice (FMOJ)"],[1,"110","6","Expanded Monitoring and Evaluation for Fund Use","The government has also taken several steps to expand monitoring and evaluation efforts to ensure that funds are effectively utilized.",""],[1,"110","6","Project Inspection and Transparency Oversight","In 2020, the Ministry of Justice undertook several monitoring and evaluation projects and inspected projects at zonal offices and parastatals to ensure transparency of fund use and disbursement.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"110","6","Code of Conduct Tribunal Act Reform","Further, the Code of Conduct tribunal's Act was reformed in 2019, and the Unification of Criminal and Penal Codes was completed.",""],[1,"110","6","Unification of Criminal and Penal Codes","Further, the Code of Conduct tribunal's Act was reformed in 2019, and the Unification of Criminal and Penal Codes was completed.",""],[1,"112","2","Anti-Corruption Capacity Enhancement and Transparency Reform","Enhance anti-corruption capacity across the public, private and social sectors through technology adoption.",""],[1,"112","3","Judiciary and Public Law Personnel Training Programme","the government will engage in extensive training of public law personnel to build the skills necessary for effective policy reform and implementation for long-term results.",""],[1,"112","3","Justice Sector Legal Framework Strengthening","the government will promote a strong legal framework in accordance with the National Policy on Justice.",""],[1,"112","3","Justice and Law Enforcement Partnership Mechanism","There will also be strong partnerships with law enforcement agencies to ensure that the judicial and security sectors are adequately equipped to deliver safety and fairness for all.",""],[1,"112","6","Operationalization of the National Policy on Justice 2017","Government will adhere to the principles and objectives of the National Policy on Justice 2017 in the delivery of justice and ensure it becomes fully operational as this is considered fundamental for the NDP to achieve its objectives.",""],[1,"112","8","Institutional Accountability and Anti-Corruption Enforcement","It is important to strengthen the accountability of institutions that are already in place and tackle corruption across society.",""],[1,"112","8","Impartial Sanctions for Public Trust Violations","Sanctions must be applied impartially to those who betray public trust or break the law.",""]],"86":[[1,"111","20","Citizen Participation and Inclusion Policy Reform","The government will enact and implement policies that encourage citizen participation (particularly women and youth) to provide legal backing for citizen engagement.",""],[1,"111","20","Citizen Feedback and Engagement Mechanisms","Finally, the government will create channels and mechanisms to engage directly with citizens and allow for the collection of feedback from the citizenry, ensuring that diverse voices are heard, and corresponding actions are swiftly taken.",""],[1,"112","1","National Orientation Strengthening Initiative","To strengthen national orientation, the government will build a set of foundational national values that focus on unity, while acknowledging and appreciating Nigeria's rich diversity.",""],[1,"112","1","Public Education Campaigns for National Unity","launching public education campaigns on the importance of national unity to curb ethnocentrism.",""],[1,"112","1","Regional Exchange Programmes for Social Cohesion","Finally, more regional exchange programmes will be designed, to build societal empathy and appreciation for diverse cultures.",""]],"87":[[1,"113","1","Foreign Policy Coordination and Adaptive Diplomacy Framework","Clear and consistent foreign policy orientation and coordination among the MDAs is critical to achieving the foreign policy objectives of the country.",""],[1,"115","15","Foreign Policy Agency Reform","To improve service delivery, the government will reform its foreign policy agencies to ensure efficient activities in host countries through improved operational capacity.","Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Foreign Service | Missions Abroad"],[1,"115","16","Review of Nigeria's Official Development Assistance Policy Guide","The 2015 policy guide of Nigeria's Official Development Assistance (ODA) will also be reviewed to ensure a paradigm shift in ODA resource mobilization and",""],[1,"116","1","Cross-MDA Foreign Policy Coordination","the government will improve cross-MDA partnerships with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MFA), to ensure that foreign policy goals are clearly communicated with MDAs in other sectors, for timely collaboration to achieve targets.","Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MFA)"],[1,"116","2","Foreign Policy Institutional Efficiency Improvement","This sum will be utilised to improve the efficiency of the MFA and other relevant agencies such as NIDCOM to be able to serve the objectives of Nigeria's foreign policy.","MFA | NIDCOM"],[1,"116","4","Foreign Policy Capacity and Trade Partnership Strengthening","This will be achieved by addressing the current gaps in national foreign policy and affairs, developing the requisite institutional capacity, and bolstering trade partnerships around the world.",""]],"88":[[1,"113","9","Migrant Rights Promotion and Diaspora Support","To achieve this target, MFA collaborated with the International Organization for Migration (IOM), and the National Agency for the Prohibition of Trafficking in Persons (NAPTIP) to promote the rights of Nigerian migrants, as well as empowering them to become an integral part of their host communities.","MFA | International Organization for Migration (IOM) | National Agency for the Prohibition of Trafficking in Persons (NAPTIP)"],[1,"113","9","Emergency Evacuation and Repatriation of Nigerian Citizens","The government completed a successful evacuation of stranded Nigerians from Canada, China, the United Kingdom and United States during COVID-19.",""],[1,"113","9","Repatriation of Nigerians Affected by Xenophobic Attacks","The government also repatriated over 500 Nigerian Citizens affected by Xenophobic attacks in South Africa, and 109 from Mali.",""],[1,"113","10","Temporary Workers' Migration Programme","Another target was to launch a temporary workers' migration programme with bilateral partners.",""],[1,"113","11","Nigerian-German Centre for Jobs, Migration and Reintegration","the government recently facilitated the negotiation for the establishment of a Nigerian-German Centre for Jobs, Migration and Reintegration in Lagos, Abuja and Benin.",""],[1,"113","11","Migrant Policy Agreement with Saudi Arabia","An agreement on Migrant Policy has also been completed with Saudi Arabia and will be used as a template for Nigeria's engagement with countries with similar needs.",""],[1,"114","3","Temporary Workers' Migration Programme","for the temporary workers' migration programme, Nigerian workers are yet to successfully migrate to partner countries",""],[1,"115","7","Efficiency Improvement in Consular and Diaspora Welfare Services","Pursue efficiency in the delivery of consular services and welfare services to Nigerians in the diaspora.",""],[1,"115","14","Citizen Support and Welfare Services Enhancement","Enhance citizen support and welfare services, using inter-agency collaboration and citizen diplomacy.",""]],"89":[[1,"113","4","Cultural Diplomacy and Cultural Agreements","Cultural diplomacy: Nigeria is signatory to Cultural Agreements to establish cultural links with the rest of the world.",""],[1,"113","11","Cultural Diplomacy Collaboration with International Entertainment Partners","the Nigerian government recently facilitated collaboration between Nigerian entertainers and their counterparts in Cote d'Ivoire, Brazil, US, South Africa, and Jamaica.",""],[1,"114","7","Economic Diplomacy Integration into Foreign Policy","The African continent presents an opportunity for Nigeria to put economic diplomacy as a core component of its foreign policy.",""],[1,"115","12","Expanded Multilateral Peacekeeping Support","This will be achieved by expanding multilateral peace-keeping support in African countries and convening more African and other global leaders to design collaborative solutions to the continent's challenges.",""],[1,"115","12","African Leadership and Multilateral Diplomacy Initiative","The government will strengthen Nigeria's role as a leader in the ECOWAS region and in Africa, to support other countries in tackling local issues.",""],[1,"115","12","Expanded Engagement in the African Union","The government will also increase its engagement in the African Union, especially on issues including democracy, security, and human rights.",""],[1,"115","12","Global Advocacy for Racial Equality","Finally, Nigeria will use its soft power to support the global advocacy of racial equality, especially for black people across the world.",""]],"90":[[1,"114","2","Foreign Mission ICT Development Programme","Finally, to improve MDA service delivery, the MFA engaged in an ICT development programme, which has focused on moving Nigeria's foreign mission websites from the public domain to the Nigerian government domains.",""],[1,"114","3","Public Mission Website Migration to the Public Domain","over 50 percent of public mission websites are yet to be migrated to the public domain",""]],"91":[[1,"118","1","Targeted Education Sector Policy Interventions","To do so, the Government will support the development of a workforce with the required competencies to meet employers' needs in the 21st century through targeted policy interventions across the education sector.",""],[1,"118","2","Education Access Expansion and Teaching Quality Improvement","Expanding access to the education system and improving teaching quality will give every Nigerian the tools to realize their full potential, regardless of their background.",""],[1,"118","5","Enforcement of Free and Compulsory Basic Education Law","The enforcement of the free and compulsory basic education law by ensuring that children within the school age are brought back to school.",""],[1,"119","2","Measures to Keep Children in School During Economic Hardship","NESP policies will ease the burden on families and allow children to remain in school instead of pursuing other endeavours due to economic hardship.",""],[1,"120","19","State Education Watch Group for Basic Education Enforcement","The Government will enforce the Universal Basic Education Commission (UBEC) Act of free and compulsory basic education through the setting up of the State Education Watch Group to reduce the number of out-of-school children.",""],[1,"120","19","Inclusive Education Policy Framework","It will also foster inclusive educational policies to ensure that the sector puts equity at the centre of its initiatives.",""],[1,"120","19","Accessible School Facilities Legislation","The government will introduce legislation for schools to provide adequate facilities to increase enrolment of special needs and disabled students.",""],[1,"120","19","School Social Support Schemes","Investments will be made in school social schemes such as school feeding, uniforms and textbooks distribution.",""],[1,"120","19","Community Engagement Campaigns for School Attendance","Community engagement sensitization campaigns will be put in place to secure community buy in, and boost school attendance.",""],[1,"120","19","Girls' Education Initiative Rollout","Furthermore, there will be a rollout of girls' education initiatives to increase girls' enrolment rates.",""],[1,"121","5","Basic School Infrastructure Provision","Provide basic infrastructure such as access to water and electricity in schools to aid learning.",""],[1,"121","6","Universal Basic Education Programme Improvement and School Enrolment Incentives","Encourage school enrolment and tackle Nigeria's out- of-school children problem by improving the Universal Basic Education Programme and other necessary incentives.",""],[1,"121","7","Priority Education Sector Investment Programme","Allocations will be made to priority projects in the sector.",""],[1,"121","7","Private Investment Enablement for Education","The Government will further create an enabling environment for private investment to thrive in the education sector.",""],[1,"141","1","Girls' Education Promotion Campaign","with greater emphasis on Northern Nigeria in parallel with campaigns to promote girls' education.",""]],"92":[[1,"121","1","STEAM and TVET Centre Expansion","Nigeria will increase investments in Science, Technology, Engineering, Arts and Mathematics (STEAM) & Technical, Vocational Education and Training (TVET) centres to boost enrolment in these programs, with particular attention paid to women enrolment.",""],[1,"121","1","Statewide Vocational Hub Network","The government will establish vocational hubs across all states and partner with the nation's largest private employers across key sectors to align needed competencies with the national curriculum and develop skills certification programmes.",""],[1,"121","1","MSME Technology and Entrepreneurship Skills Support","It will also improve access to technological and entrepreneurial skills for MSMEs to boost their productivity.",""]],"93":[[1,"121","2","Education Sector Financing Expansion and Earmarking","Secure sustainable financing sources that will increase funding to the education sector through public funding allocation and direct engagement with private sector actors.",""],[1,"121","2","Education Public-Private Partnerships Framework","A public-private partnerships framework will be designed using innovative financing models that will assist with school infrastructure development and regulate private investments in education.",""]],"94":[[1,"121","4","Digital Literacy Policy and Strategic Action Plan","The Government will formulate a Digital Literacy Policy and Strategic Action Plan to train teachers and introduce digital literacy at all levels of the education system.",""],[1,"121","4","IT Facilities and ICT Tools Provision","This will involve providing IT facilities, ICT tools and developing e-learning programmes as part of this plan.",""]],"95":[[1,"122","2","Primary Healthcare Revitalization Programme","The policy thrusts of the ERGP and the Vision include revitalizing the primary healthcare system, strengthening secondary and tertiary healthcare delivery, expanding the National Health Insurance Scheme (NHIS) to achieve universal health coverage (UHC), and building the capacity of health care personnel to improve service delivery.",""],[1,"122","4","Primary Health Care Capacity Strengthening","The emphasis will also be on: (i) addressing human resource and infrastructure gaps, especially at primary health care level which is responsible for more than 70% of the disease burden, in collaboration with the private sector;",""],[1,"122","5","National Health Insurance Scheme Rollout","The ERGP health provision was to improve the accessibility, affordability and quality of healthcare and roll out the National Health Insurance Scheme (NHIS) across the entire country.",""],[1,"122","8","Primary Healthcare Centre Revitalization","The ERGP planned to revitalize 10,000 primary healthcare centres (PHCs) in the country to improve access to healthcare",""],[1,"122","10","Strengthening Primary Response Centres and Ambulance Points","Several states are yet to strengthen Primary Response Centres and Ambulance points.",""],[1,"122","10","Connecting General Hospitals to Rural Areas","The project of connecting the general hospitals to rural",""],[1,"124","1","Universal Healthcare Coverage Expansion","Extend Universal Healthcare Coverage to over half of the population in rural and urban areas in Nigeria;",""],[1,"124","28","Universal Access to Quality Health Services","Nigeria will ensure universal access to quality health services without any financial barriers, increase prompt and effective responses to all medical emergencies, and enhance equity in vaccine distribution.",""],[1,"125","13","Universal Healthcare Expansion","The Government will extend universal healthcare to all Nigerians to expand access to basic health services.",""]],"96":[[1,"122","3","Health Financing Reform and Resource Realignment","The crucial goal for this plan will be to accelerate reforms to adequately finance the health system and realign resources in line with the responsibility for health across the tiers of the healthcare delivery system.",""],[1,"122","3","Private Sector Health Financing Partnership","Government collaboration with the private sector will generate additional financing in the health sector.",""],[1,"122","3","Expanded Social Health Insurance Coverage","Implementing health care financing reforms to expand social health insurance coverage to state, LGA and community levels, and scaling up the implementation of the BHCPF in collaboration with all states, implementing agencies, partners, the private sector and other relevant stakeholders will be the focus",""]],"97":[[1,"122","2","Health Workforce Capacity Building","The policy thrusts of the ERGP and the Vision include revitalizing the primary healthcare system, strengthening secondary and tertiary healthcare delivery, expanding the National Health Insurance Scheme (NHIS) to achieve universal health coverage (UHC), and building the capacity of health care personnel to improve service delivery.",""],[1,"123","2","Health Workforce Registry Expansion","This registry is meant to identify and fill gaps to optimize the health worker-to population ratio by recruiting and training more health workers and attracting talent from abroad",""],[1,"124","27","Healthcare Workforce Retention and Incentive Scheme","Reversing the brain drain by creating jobs while providing incentives to motivate healthcare professionals to work in",""],[1,"124","28","Health Workforce Distribution and Capacity Improvement","By providing an adequate skill mix of competent, motivated, productive and equitably distributed health workforce, accessibility of healthcare services to underserved communities will be significantly improved.",""],[1,"124","2","Essential Medical Personnel and Medical Supplies Availability","Ensure availability in sufficient quantity of quality essential medical personnel, medicine and medical supplies within the country;",""]],"98":[[1,"123","3","Measles and Meningitis Vaccination Campaign","Nigeria carried out a campaign to vaccinate 28 million children in 19 Northern States against measles and meningitis in August 2019.",""],[1,"123","3","Yellow Fever Vaccination Campaigns","Four phases of yellow fever vaccination campaigns have been carried out from 2017 to 2020, though there was significant interruption in 2020 due to the COVID-19 Pandemic.",""],[1,"123","3","Expanded Antiretroviral Treatment Provision","Additionally, the provision of antiretroviral medication to people living with HIV/ AIDS increased from 31 percent in 2016 to 44% in 2018.",""],[1,"125","10","Expanded HIV Treatment and Care Access for Key Populations","Enhance access to HIV treatment and care in particular by people in detention, people using drugs and other key populations that suffer from far higher rates of infection and increasingly represent the source of the further spread of the virus.",""],[1,"124","28","Emergency Health Response and Vaccine Equity Initiative","Nigeria will ensure universal access to quality health services without any financial barriers, increase prompt and effective responses to all medical emergencies, and enhance equity in vaccine distribution.",""]],"99":[[1,"123","16","Mobile Health Technology Deployment","Already, agencies such as Nigeria Centre for Disease Control (NCDC) and National Primary Health Development Agency (NPHCDA) are deploying mobile technologies to improve reporting of priority diseases and immunization uptake statistics, respectively.",""],[1,"123","16","Mobile Health Information and Patient Follow-up Services","Mobile technologies could be deployed for the dissemination of preventive health and nutrition information, for follow-up of patients and reminders for appointments, for health surveys, etc.",""],[1,"123","16","Health Technology Enabling Infrastructure and Investment Support","However, many conditions need to be met for this potential to materialize, including stable electricity, high speed internet connectivity, macroeconomic stability, infrastructural development and investment in manpower.",""],[1,"123","16","Policy and Infrastructure Support for Private Health Technology Investment","Proper infrastructure in addition to a stable policy environment are critical elements needed to attract more private investments in health technologies.",""],[1,"125","3","Health Sector Digital Innovation Initiative","Innovation in the health sector such as mobile health, telemedicine and the introduction of electronic medical records can be used to boost productivity and potentially attract more youth to jobs in the health sector.",""],[1,"125","1","Integrated Health Information System","it will also establish an integrated, comprehensive and reliable health information system for decision-making.",""],[1,"125","7","Health Information Management System","Adopt a robust information management system to support patients and referral among levels of medical institutions as well as gather relevant information.",""]],"100":[[1,"123","18","Integrated Public-Private Healthcare System Development","Develop an integrated healthcare system between the private and public sectors for primary, secondary and tertiary health institutions in keeping with changing political, economic, social and environmental situation and changing technology;",""],[1,"124","30","Health Sector Efficiency and Policy Coordination Reform","The government will significantly improve its health sector by enabling the environment for greater efficiency, collaboration across various stakeholders, and cohesive policy formulation.",""],[1,"124","30","Health Sector Leadership and Research-Informed Programming","Establishing an effective leadership and utilizing research to inform policy and programming will create both",""],[1,"125","1","Health Sector Regulatory Framework and Accountability System","an efficient and transparent regulatory framework encompassing the entire health sector ecosystem.",""],[1,"125","1","Community Participation and Accountability in Health Sector","Fostering a collaborative enabling environment will encourage community participation in the sector for even greater accountability.",""],[1,"125","4","Public-Private Partnership Adoption and Utilization","Promoting the adoption and utilization of collaborations with the private sector on PPPs will heighten results of all initiatives.",""],[1,"125","4","Stakeholder Partnership Framework for Domestic Resource Mobilization","promoting effective partnership with professional groups and other relevant stakeholders like academic institutions, will strengthen the framework for domestic resource mobilization.",""],[1,"125","12","Health Sector Public Investment Allocation","An estimated public investment of N1.65 trillion will be allocated to achieve the goals outlined in the health sector from 2021-2025.",""],[1,"125","12","Priority Health Projects Funding","Allocations will be made to priority projects in the sector as well as projects essential to the operations of the Health Ministries at federal and subnational levels.",""]],"101":[[1,"125","2","Nutrition, Maternal, Child and Neonatal Investment Initiative","Prioritize investments in nutrition, maternal, child and neonatal initiatives by securing funding.",""],[1,"125","2","Universal Reproductive, Maternal, Newborn, Child and Adolescent Health Services","it is critical to ensure there is universal access to quality reproductive, maternal, new-born, child, adolescent services.",""]],"102":[[1,"125","5","Healthy Environment Promotion and Health Awareness Campaign","Increase the promotion of healthy environment approaches.",""],[1,"125","8","Drug Abuse Prevention and Treatment Support","Reduce incidence of drug abuse through enlightenment campaigns and provision of drug counselling and referral capacities at community level, access to drug treatment across all urban centres in line with the Minimum Standards for Drug Dependence Treatment.",""],[1,"125","9","Drug Quality Standards and Essential Medical Products Access Improvement","Improve drug quality standards and access to essential medical products through the effective implementation of the National Policy for Controlled Medicines, Pain Management Guidelines and other relevant policies.",""],[1,"125","11","Mental Health Service Expansion and Inclusion Initiative","Expand access to mental health services to citizens and focus on avoiding exclusion of those affected by or at risk of mental illness.",""],[1,"140","5","Accessible and Affordable Public Health Services for Women and Vulnerable People","The National Health Policy 2016- 2018 promoted accessible and affordable public health services for women and vulnerable people.",""],[1,"140","5","Vesico Vaginal Fistula Rehabilitation and Psycho-social Support","rehabilitating 20 women suffering from Vesico Vaginal Fistula (VVF) through medical and psycho- social support",""],[1,"140","5","Diaper Distribution to Primary Health Care Centres and Orphanages","distributing diapers to 37 primary health care centres and orphanages in the FCT",""]],"103":[[1,"128","1","National Home-Grown School Feeding Programme","The Government began the National Home-Grown School Feeding Programme and the National Cash Transfer Programme under the Office of the Vice President in the Presidency in December, 2015.",""],[1,"128","1","National Cash Transfer Programme","The Government began the National Home-Grown School Feeding Programme and the National Cash Transfer Programme under the Office of the Vice President in the Presidency in December, 2015.",""],[1,"128","6","Nutrition Security Support for Vulnerable Communities","Ensure Nutrition Security within vulnerable communities.",""],[1,"129","3","High-Energy and High-Nutrient Food Support for Vulnerable Groups","Encourage the expansion of production, distribution and marketing of high energy and high-nutrients- density foods or snacks for vulnerable groups including the control of severe acute malnutrition as well as nutritional support for OVCs as well as PLWAs.",""],[1,"129","4","School Feeding and Health Program","Ensure effective delivery of comprehensive packages of educational, health and nutritional interventions through the School Feeding and Health Program and other similar programmes.",""]],"104":[[1,"128","3","Food and Nutrition Coordination System","The goals to be achieved during the plan period among others include the establishment of a viable system that will guide and coordinate food and nutrition activities undertaken in the MDAs and at all levels",""],[1,"128","23","Multi-sectoral Food and Nutrition Intervention Support","Multi-sectoral collaboration aimed at facilitating capacity building and mobilizing resources for food and nutrition intervention programmes.",""],[1,"129","10","Food and Nutrition Coordination Mechanisms","Strengthen coordination of food and nutrition mechanisms at all levels particularly at primary health care level.",""],[1,"129","12","Food Law Harmonization Reform","Harmonize existing food laws in the country.",""],[1,"129","14","Food Security and Nutrition Coordination and Supply Constraint Response","Supply constraints such as security issues and poor logistics accounting for food scarcity and rising food prices will be adequately addressed during this Plan period.",""],[1,"129","14","Inter-Agency Food Sector Coordination and Regulatory Collaboration","priority will be given to proper coordination and collaboration among the various MDAs and food processing and food products regulatory agencies such as NAFDAC and SON.",""],[1,"126","4","Nutrition Mainstreaming in Development Processes","Government will make deliberate efforts to increase investment and mainstream nutrition into relevant development processes.",""]],"105":[[1,"128","26","Food Fortification to Prevent Micronutrient Deficiency","Control and prevent micronutrient deficiency through food fortification by large, medium-scale and cottage food industries, as part of the National Food",""],[1,"129","1","Fortification Programme","Fortification Programme by NAFDAC.",""],[1,"129","2","Nutritional Enhancement and Supplementation Programme","Encourage the introduction of nutritional enhancements to mitigate nutrition risks, including vitamin mineral supplementation programs.",""],[1,"129","5","Comprehensive Nutrition Education and Services for Rural Communities","Ensure effective delivery of comprehensive package of nutrition education and services to rural communities along with investment to expand agricultural extension services.",""],[1,"129","6","Essential Nutrition Interventions Delivery Package","Ensure effective delivery of comprehensive package of essential nutrition interventions as part of health services and programs particularly at primary health care level.",""],[1,"129","11","Improve Working Conditions for Public Sector Nutrition Officers","Enhance the condition of services of public sector nutrition officers and improve their work environment.",""]],"106":[[1,"129","5","Expansion of Agricultural Extension Services","Ensure effective delivery of comprehensive package of nutrition education and services to rural communities along with investment to expand agricultural extension services.",""],[1,"129","7","Coordinated Media Strategies Against Child Marriage and for Nutrition Advocacy","Sustained and regular, coordinated national and sub-national media strategies against child marriage, for nutrition advocacy and public education.",""]],"107":[[1,"131","2","Integrated Water Resources Management and Regulatory Framework","the government will coordinate policy across the parameters of the service level to increase infrastructure investments and establish a regulatory framework that will improve the management of water resources.",""],[1,"131","4","National Irrigation Development Programme","The National Irrigation Development Programme (2016-2030) was launched to develop an additional 100,000Ha of irrigated irrigation land by 2020 and a total of 500,000Ha by 2030.",""],[1,"131","5","Transforming Irrigation Management in Nigeria (TRIMING) Project","The Transforming Irrigation Management in Nigeria (TRIMING) project is a World Bank intervention project launched in 2014 to support the rehabilitation and expansion of 42,000Ha of irrigation land on six",""],[1,"131","7","Feasibility Studies and Designs for Integrated Irrigation Projects","Feasibility studies and designs of some selected projects were carried out including those for Integrated Irrigation Development at Nasarawa state (covering 6,600 Ha) and Donga Suntai (covering 6,000 Ha)",""],[1,"131","8","Blueprint to Strengthen River Basin Development Authorities","Development of a Blueprint to Strengthen the River Basin Development Authorities (RBDAs) as enablers for food security and socio-economic development;",""],[1,"131","9","Irrigation Land Leasing to Commercial Farmers","Leasing of 55,000 Ha of Irrigation land to commercial farmers;",""],[1,"131","10","Establishment of Songhai Model Farms","Establishment of four Songhai Model farms in the RBDAs with 8,617 Graduate/Youths trained and empowered to deliver agricultural services.",""]],"108":[[1,"131","11","Hydropower Dam Development and Concession Programme","Government optimized existing capacity for hydropower generation by identifying 26 dams with potential for development and concession of mini and midi hydropower plants.",""],[1,"131","12","Hydropower Dam Concession and PPP Development Programme","Itisi multipurpose dam (40MW), Gurara II multipurpose dam(360MW), Kashimbila dam (40MW), DadinKowa Dam (40 MW), FarinRuwa multipurpose dam (20MW) are now in concession.",""],[1,"131","12","New Hydropower Projects Under PPP Arrangements","Additionally, the development of new hydropower projects was initiated under 8 PPP arrangements and are currently ongoing, notably Makurdi (1,500MW), Lokoja (750MW), Katsina-Ala (460MW), Tede (220MW), Mangu (182MW), Kiri (36MW), Bawarku (182MW) and Manya (136MW).",""]],"109":[[1,"132","18","Commercially Sound and Environmentally Sustainable Water Management Reform","Nigeria plans to significantly improve its water supply and sanitation services' capacity by introducing commercially sound and environmentally sustainable water management practices by 2025.",""],[1,"133","15","National Water Services Regulatory and Institutional Framework","Improve affordable water service delivery by developing a comprehensive regulatory and institutional framework with clear commercial, quality, and environmental requirements across the country.",""],[1,"133","16","Coordinated Water Resources and Sanitation Investment Plan","Design a coordinated investment plan to be used as a roadmap to secure required funding for the development, operation, deployment of human resources and maintenance of large structures for water resources and sanitation management.",""],[1,"133","16","Sustainable Financing Framework for Water Infrastructure","The Government will develop a sustainable financing framework in partnership with development partners to attract commercial finance and identify feasible financing options for water infrastructure project development across Nigeria.",""],[1,"133","17","Integrated Water Resources and Sanitation Planning and Policy Formulation","Adopt an integrated planning and policy formulation approach across the water resources and sanitation sector to ensure seamless coordination across related",""],[1,"133","18","Cross-Sectoral Coordination for Water Resources and Sanitation","Government will coordinate interventions across the power, agriculture, transportation, tourism, environment, health, education sectors to identify synergies and ensure that complementary strategies are implemented as it pertains to achieving water resources and sanitation goals.",""],[1,"133","18","Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Operations and Maintenance Collaboration","Additionally, the Federal Ministry of Water Resources will work closely with State and Local Government Authorities who are responsible for the operation and maintenance of rural water supply and sanitation schemes in collaboration with benefiting Communities.","Federal Ministry of Water Resources"]],"110":[[1,"133","19","Technology Adoption and Innovation Support for Water Resources and Sanitation","Facilitate the deployment of innovative solutions through technology adoption, research and development in the water resources and sanitation sector.",""],[1,"133","19","Hydrological Forecasting and Environmental Management Tools Development","Government will support the development of tools for hydrological forecasting, environmental management to ensure adequate preparedness and response mechanisms.",""],[1,"133","19","Wastewater and Natural Resources Management Innovation","Additionally, the introduction of wastewater and natural resources management innovations will optimize cost effective solutions more suitable to the Nigerian context.",""]],"111":[[1,"135","7","Environmental Sustainability Policy Review and Climate Adaptation Measures","To achieve this, targeted actions were identified including policy reviews, and increased emission-reduction and afforestation activities.",""],[1,"135","7","Green Bond Financing for Environmentally Friendly Infrastructure","Nigeria participated in the Paris Climate Agreement that will engender external financing support and as well spur the use of green bonds issuance for environmentally friendly infrastructural development.",""],[1,"137","3","Mobilization of External Climate Finance and Technology Assistance","The participation of Nigeria in the Paris Climate Agreement should make Nigeria eligible for external financial and technological assistance.",""],[1,"138","2","Climate Change Bill Enactment and Implementation","The priority will be to ensure enactment and effective implementation of the Climate Change Bill, which supports development of decarbonisation pathways in line with a new climate change adaptation and mitigation economy.",""],[1,"138","2","Cross-Policy Coherence for Emission Reduction","Measures will also be taken to strengthen coherence across policies, e.g., to ensure that policies do not simultaneously discourage and encourage emission reduction across sectors.",""],[1,"138","6","Carbon Financing Framework Development","Finally, measures will be taken to lay the groundwork for carbon financing, which will provide carbon credit options, purchasable by companies, in exchange for greenhouse emissions.",""],[1,"138","7","Environmental Sustainability Public Education Campaigns","Enhance community awareness on the importance of environmental sustainability through public education campaigns.",""],[1,"139","5","Resource Efficiency and Green Development Investment","An estimated public investment of N220bn over the next five years (2021-2025) is expected to, among other things, birth a psyche of environmental awareness, alternative sources of livelihoods, improved sanitation and public health infrastructure, sustained biodiversity and ecotourism growth.",""],[1,"139","6","Green, Bio- and Circular Economy Policy Reform Programme","Nigeria will make significant progress towards increasing sustainability through the green economy, bio-economy and circular economy",""]],"112":[[1,"135","5","Disaster Management System Strengthening","Strengthen disaster management capabilities at all levels of governance by ensuring that disaster preparedness and response planning are essential elements of coherent emergency management.",""],[1,"135","6","Expanded Disaster Mitigation Efforts","There is therefore a need to expand disaster mitigation efforts, for both natural disasters and the ones stemming from human activities.",""],[1,"137","1","Disaster Management Systems Strengthening","Finally, efficient disaster management systems can avoid the loss of lives and property and build resilience and sustainable development in the long-term.",""],[1,"137","8","Disaster and Emergency Preparedness and Response Improvement","Improve preparedness and responsiveness to disaster and emergency situations across regions.",""],[1,"138","3","NEMA Operational Efficiency and Disaster Response Strengthening","Improvement of operational efficiency of the National Emergency Management Agency (NEMA) across the country in quick response to disaster management through increased financing support and better infrastructural facilities.",""],[1,"139","3","Disaster Preparedness System Strengthening","Strengthen disaster preparedness systems across all regions through policy implementation and technological adoption.",""],[1,"139","3","National Emergency Management Agency Transformation","To build efficient disaster management systems, the focus will be to transform the National Emergency Management Agency (NEMA), from being mainly a relief agency, to a disaster management agency.",""],[1,"139","3","Disaster Management Act","The government will also introduce a Disaster Management Act that will secure budget allocation for disaster management.",""],[1,"139","6","Environmental and Disaster Management Systems Strengthening","ensuring financing and technical support to build strong environmental and disaster management systems",""]],"113":[[1,"135","4","Circular Economy Promotion","Circular economy which addresses the unsustainable exploitation of reuse and recycling of resources to eliminate waste.",""],[1,"135","8","Integrated Waste Management Facilities","There is also an ongoing establishment of integrated waste management facilities, to build a strong framework for a circular economy that ensures the sustainable management of resources.",""],[1,"135","8","Environmental Permitting and Compliance Monitoring","267 Environmental Impact Assessments (EIA) permits, and 44 Air/Gaseous Emissions permits were issued, to ensure that projects follow environmental guidelines aimed at cutting greenhouse emissions and are properly monitored.",""],[1,"136","1","Community-Based Waste Management Systems","there has only been a 40% implementation of the establishment of community-based waste management systems across all geopolitical zones.",""],[1,"136","1","Timely Funding for Project Execution","there is a need for timely availability of funds for project execution",""],[1,"136","1","Strengthening Institutional Frameworks for Environmental Programme Coordination","a need to strengthen existing institutional frameworks to ensure effective coordination of environmental programmes.",""],[1,"136","2","Ogoni Land Cleanup Efforts","Ongoing efforts to clean up the Ogoni land is a welcome development.",""],[1,"136","2","Oil Spill Impact Mitigation and Gas Flaring Reduction Measures","The various policies and programmes to mitigate oil spillage impact as well as discourage gas flaring will continue.",""],[1,"138","9","Circular Economy Policy and Waste Prevention Measures","Government will develop policies to encourage waste prevention, including eco-design, reuse, repair, refurbishment, re-manufacturing, and extended producer responsibility schemes.",""],[1,"138","9","National Waste Management System Expansion","Measures will also be taken to expand the building of waste management systems across Nigeria.",""],[1,"138","9","Public Recycling Station Expansion and Incentive Systems","Finally, efforts will also focus on increasing the number of public recycling stations and identifying financial incentive systems for waste",""],[1,"139","1","E-Waste Smuggling Control Measures","the priority will be to curb the smuggling of low-quality electronics that end up in landfills and exacerbate pollution.",""]],"114":[[1,"135","8","Afforestation and Reforestation Actions","In addition, Nigeria engaged in aggressive afforestation actions, to address current deforestation, and increase the country's goal of building eco-friendly societies.",""],[1,"135","8","Great Green Wall Programme","The Great Green Wall Programme48 has also made steady progress, with 11 states participating in activities, which include restoration of flood erosion sites, sensitization and awareness campaigns, the provision of alternative energy sources to households, and establishing woodlots in Kano and Gombe States.",""],[1,"135","10","Great Green Wall Reforestation Initiative","The Great Green Wall is a reforestation initiative launched in 2007 by the African Union to plant 8,000km of green vegetation across the entire width of Africa.",""],[1,"139","2","Dryland Rehabilitation and Crop-Water Productivity Improvement","Measures will also be taken to rehabilitate and sustainably manage dryland environments and improve crop-water productivity to reduce water waste in Nigeria's agriculture practices.",""]],"115":[[1,"135","9","Solar Naija Electrification Programme","The ongoing Solar Naija programme seeks to electrify 5 million households and 25 million people by 2023, leveraging solar mini-grids and standalone systems.",""],[1,"136","12","Renewable and Bioenergy Investment for Energy Access","increased investment in environmentally sustainable activities will support Nigeria's drive for concentric economic diversification from an oil-based economy, especially with opportunities to diversify energy production, through renewable and bioenergy options.",""],[1,"136","12","Energy Transition and Energy Poverty Reduction Pathway","pathways to reaching net-zero by 2050 must include first ending energy poverty by 2025.",""],[1,"136","12","Clean Energy Access Expansion","Access to energy will be addressed, taking cognizance of the trend towards renewable energy, so that Nigeria's increasing energy demand will be met with less polluting and deforesting fuels such as diesel, kerosene and firewood.",""],[1,"136","12","Climate-Smart Electricity Expansion for Jobs","the scale and quality of electricity services from environmentally friendly sources must increase significantly to create jobs and enable climate-smart",""],[1,"137","5","Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency Investment Scale-Up","Upscaling investments in renewable energy and energy efficiency for productivity, competitiveness and job creation.",""],[1,"137","12","Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency Investment Upscaling","Upscaling investments in renewable energy and energy efficiency",""],[1,"138","6","Renewable Energy Promotion Initiative","(iii) renewable energy;",""],[1,"138","8","Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency Investment Upscaling","Upscaling investments in renewable energy and energy efficiency for productivity, competitiveness and job creation.",""]],"116":[[1,"137","1","Circular and Bioeconomy Innovation Support","Circular and bioeconomy practices hold the potential to drive innovation and job creation in Nigeria's economic sectors, especially through new businesses, aimed at developing local agricultural and health solutions with bioeconomy practices, and incorporating circular economy systems across the manufacturing industry.",""],[1,"137","2","Sustainable Supply Chains and Responsible Investment Promotion","Other opportunities include; creating sustainable supply chains, integrating responsible investment, and leveraging sustainable finance.",""],[1,"137","2","Impact Investing Mobilization Mechanism","There is opportunity for impact investing to draw in the private sector and other funds for social, economic and environmental projects.",""],[1,"137","2","Natural Resource-Based Import Substitution and Export Earnings Strategy","We can also leverage our natural resources for import substitution and foreign exchange earnings.",""],[1,"138","4","Green Economy Skills Development and Curriculum Reform","Prepare for a transition to a greener economy by investing in the training and development of core skills.",""],[1,"138","4","International Knowledge and Technology Transfer Partnerships for Sustainable Systems","The Nigerian government will also partner with countries with advanced environmentally sustainable systems for knowledge acquisition and technological adaptation/ transfer.",""],[1,"138","5","Green Business Incubators and Innovative Financing Support","Increase access to finance and technical support for businesses and projects in environmentally sustainable sectors by setting up incubators and adopting innovative financing tools.",""],[1,"138","5","MSME Investment Incentives in Biodiversity Conservation Areas","Government will incentivise investment in MSMEs operating in biodiversity conservation areas, especially MSMEs aimed at (i) sustainable forestry;",""],[1,"138","6","Entrepreneur Incubation and Investor Matching Programme","Incubation programmes will also be introduced, to support entrepreneurs committed to building an environmentally sustainable society, and match businesses with local and international investors.",""],[1,"139","2","Bioeconomy Model Adoption Programme","government programmes will adopt bioeconomy models with a focus on (i) vaccine production and the production of active pharma ingredients in healthcare; (ii) the utilization of medicinal plants and herbs for exportable materials in healthcare; (iii) the development and use of biofuels in waste management; (iv) seed improvement for higher yields and climate resistant crop species in agriculture.",""],[1,"139","6","Skills Development for Environmental Innovation","strategic measures will focus on policy reform programs, expanding skills development for innovation",""]],"117":[[1,"139","4","Regional Risk Analysis and Resilience Systems","Foresight tools will also be introduced to develop regional risk analysis and resilience systems, in the event of major disruptions such as conflicts, restiveness, pandemics, and disasters, especially for food security and economic recovery.",""],[1,"139","3","Social Security and Safety Nets Expansion","These efforts will be complemented by building social security and safety nets, and developing affordable insurance instruments,",""],[1,"139","3","Affordable Insurance Instruments Development","These efforts will be complemented by building social security and safety nets, and developing affordable insurance instruments,",""]],"118":[[1,"140","2","Women’s Economic Empowerment Policy Environment","Nigeria will foster a policy environment that maximizes the potential of all Nigerian women and promotes their ability to productively contribute to the economy.",""],[1,"140","3","National Women Empowerment Fund","a National Women Empowerment Fund (NaWEF) was set up to provide soft loans to rural women",""],[1,"140","3","Women Vocational Training and Starter Pack Support","5,400 women were trained on vocations such as tailoring, hairdressing, soap making with starter packs and equipment given to them to start their businesses",""],[1,"140","3","Women Entrepreneurship and Financial Literacy Support","7,800 widows and indigent women benefited from vocational trainings, 2,000 women were trained on financial literacy and another 25,000 women were trained on online business and entrepreneurship, complemented by start-up grants to grow their businesses",""],[1,"140","3","Women Cooperative Association Strengthening","148 women cooperative associations were strengthened in 6 States",""],[1,"140","4","Microfinance Access for Rural Women","Micro-finance banks were established to provide women access to financing (loans, overdrafts, and credit), resulting in improved women participation in agri-business and improved agricultural production for food security and export.",""],[1,"142","9","Women’s Economic and Social Integration Framework Strengthening","Nigeria will strengthen the legislative and policy framework by 2025 to promote deeper integration of women into economic and social development.",""],[1,"142","10","Gender Policy Enforcement and Women's Economic Inclusion","Nigeria will strengthen the enforcement of existing gender policies and promote deeper integration of women into economic and social development.",""],[1,"143","3","Women’s Economic Empowerment and MSME Support Programme","Support the economic empowerment of women by facilitating access to financial literacy financing, providing skill building training and supporting MSMEs business viability.",""],[1,"143","3","Digital Finance and Advisory Support for Women Entrepreneurs","Facilitating access to funds through digital finance tools as well as access to advisory services will equip women entrepreneurs with the tools needed to grow their businesses into viable enterprises.",""],[1,"143","3","Women’s Financial Inclusion Partnership with Private Financial Institutions","To do so, the Government will collaborate with private financial institutions (i.e., banks, insurance companies) to negotiate reduced interest and premium rates for women, while paying particular attention to rural women especially in relation to financial literacy and access to agency banking.",""],[1,"143","3","Vocational Training Centre Capacity Expansion and Women in Business Training","In addition to increasing vocational and skills training centres capacity, the Government will facilitate training for Women in Business associations at the national and state level.",""],[1,"143","3","Expanded Advisory Support for Women-Owned MSMEs","For these policies to be effective, advisory support to women owned MSMEs will be ramped up to complement all skills building activities.",""]],"119":[[1,"143","2","Gender Mainstreaming Technical Support","Facilitate the mainstreaming of gender issues in existing policies by providing technical support to MDAs and stakeholders.",""],[1,"143","2","Gender-Responsive Policy Review and Social Protection Integration","Reviewing existing policies and strategies with a gender lens will identify bottlenecks and ensure a more effective incorporation of gender issues and social protection of the vulnerable groups at all stages of policymaking and implementation.",""],[1,"143","2","State-Level Enforcement and Action Plan Support for Gender Laws","The Ministry of Women Affairs will support states in enforcing approved laws such as the VAPP, SGBV policies, minimum benchmarks for women political representation, the CRA and build their capacity to develop state level action plans in line with these policies.","Ministry of Women Affairs"],[1,"143","2","Gender-Responsive Budgeting and Gender Management System","Additionally, the Federal Ministry of Women Affairs will assist federal, state, and local governments with adopting gender responsive budgeting and establishing a gender management system for monitoring and evaluation.","Federal Ministry of Women Affairs"],[1,"143","2","Capacity Building for Gender and Child-Sensitive Public Service Delivery","Additionally, building the capacity of all relevant public servants charged with implementation will ensure that gender and children considerations are systematically incorporated into programming.",""],[1,"143","4","Gender Data Collection and Management Strengthening","Effectively track gender related data by strengthening data collection capacity and management systems.",""],[1,"143","5","Technology-Enabled Gender Programming and Social Mobilization","Use technology to expand the reach and impact of gender programming and social mobilization campaigns.",""],[1,"143","7","Women and Gender Equity Public Investment Programme","An estimated public investment of N108bn will be allocated to achieve the goals outlined in women and gender equity over the Plan period.",""],[1,"143","7","Priority Projects and MDA Support for Women's Affairs","This will be used to execute priority projects in the sector as well as programmes essential to the operations of the relevant MDAs in charge of Women's Affairs and promote gender equity both at the National and sub-national levels.",""]],"120":[[1,"140","2","Protection Against Sexual and Gender-Based Violence","ensuring that women thrive in Nigerian society also involves protecting vulnerable women from sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV)",""],[1,"140","2","Children’s Rights Law Enforcement","and enforcing existing children's rights laws.",""],[1,"140","5","COVID-19 Relief Support for Vulnerable Women and Girls","providing relief materials, including food and hygienic items to 15,300 vulnerable women and girls in 3,060 households across 16 States and FCT who are worst affected by the effects of the COVID-19 pandemic",""],[1,"140","5","Community COVID-19 Awareness Training for Women and Girls","engaging within communities to raise awareness for COVID-19 by training 10,000 women and girls in 1,000 households in 10 states",""],[1,"140","6","National Counter Terrorism Strategy","Nigeria adopted the National Counter Terrorism Strategy (NACTEST) in 2016",""],[1,"140","6","Policy Framework and National Action Plan for Preventing and Countering Violent Extremism","the Policy Framework and National Action Plan for Preventing and Countering Violent Extremism (PCVE) in 2017.",""],[1,"141","1","Violence Against Women Response and Protection Framework","including State and Local Action Plans), the National IDP Policy, National Disaster Management Framework, a National Contingency Plan, State Anti-Human Trafficking Taskforces and setting up a Nigeria Sexual Offenders Register.",""],[1,"141","1","Shelter Provision for Gender-Based Violence Victims","As a result, 22 states have established shelters for gender-based violence (GBV) victims to date.",""],[1,"141","1","Child Protection and Anti-Child Marriage Campaign","Policies addressing violence and abuse against children were also prioritized over the past three years.",""],[1,"143","6","Gender-Based Violence Prevention and Victim Support Policy","Government will implement policies to prevent gender-based violence and support victims.",""],[1,"143","6","Victim Justice and Comprehensive Health Support Services","It will be ensured that victims are provided justice and comprehensive health service.",""],[1,"143","6","Online Referral System for SGBV Victims","Technology will also be used to support SGBV victims by setting up an online referral system to report incidences of violence which will provide a platform to support victims.",""]],"121":[[1,"144","13","National Identity Registration Drive","NIMC plans to register an additional 100 million people in 3 years and has embarked on a massive registration drive.",""],[1,"145","3","Robust Identity Management System","there is an urgent need for a robust identity management system as well as efficient population management programmes and policies.",""],[1,"145","4","Digital Identity Integration for Population Management","The adoption of digital tools in linking the National Identification Number (NIN) with the Bank Verification Number (BVN) and other feasible avenues (such as those seeking passports, through Immigration) and the telcos, provides an opportunity to ensure proper identity management.",""],[1,"145","7","National Digital Identification Coverage","Nigeria will also aim to provide its entire population with digital identification by 2025 to improve the delivery of services.",""],[1,"145","7","Identity Management Database Development","Further efforts will focus on public education, increased access to affordable contraceptives, and the development of a robust identity management database, which can be used to reliably estimate the population size and make broad economic projections.",""],[1,"145","12","National Identity Database Enhancement for Population Estimation","Ensure that Nigeria's identity database can be used to reliably estimate the population size and to make broad economic projections by factoring in births, deaths, migration patterns, and other parameters.",""],[1,"145","13","National Identification Number as Foundational ID Policy","Ensure that the National Identification Number (NIN) is the foundational ID for all Nigerians as specified in Sections 27 and 29 of the National Identity Management Commission (NIMC) Act 2007.",""],[1,"145","14","Functional ID Generation and NIN Linkage","Ensure that functional IDs are generated by all government MDAs and that, at the sub-national level, they have NINs attached to them.",""],[1,"145","15","Unique ID Registration for Foreigners","Ensure that foreigners, regardless of status, have unique IDs.",""],[1,"146","11","Strengthen ID Management Systems Through Technology Adoption","Strengthen current ID management systems by further adoption of technological tools - Nigeria will boost its technological integration to ensure a",""],[1,"146","12","Robust ID Management System","robust ID management system.",""],[1,"146","12","Expansion and Automation of Civil Registration and Vital Statistics","the National Population Commission will also focus on the expansion and automation of civil registration and vital statistics (CRVS) activities.",""],[1,"146","12","Deployment of Enrolment Agents for Hard-to-Reach Communities","in cases where digital tools alone cannot ensure the registration of Nigerians, enrolment agents will be appointed to reach them.",""],[1,"146","13","Identity Management Budget Support","Additionally, most of the budget for identity management is included in the budget of the Ministry of Communication & Digital Economy to strengthen and improve the sector.","Ministry of Communication & Digital Economy"],[1,"146","14","Digital Population Management Tools Deployment","Its efforts will focus on the promotion of family planning, the provision of contraceptives, and the utilisation of digital population management tools to gain timely and credible population data for proper economic planning.",""]],"122":[[1,"145","3","Population Management Programmes and Policies","there is an urgent need for a robust identity management system as well as efficient population management programmes and policies.",""],[1,"145","11","Population and Housing Census","Conduct a credible population and housing census by the third quarter of 2023, and subsequently, once every ten years.",""],[1,"146","13","National Census Funding","The Federal Government plans to allocate N42 billion as the capital expenditure to the National Population Commission for the Plan period.",""],[1,"146","14","Population and Identity Management Framework Improvement","The Nigerian government will improve its population and identity management framework to address existing challenges, including low penetration of family planning and ID registration, and to achieve sustainable economic development.",""],[1,"147","2","Demographic Transition and Workforce Development Policies","Nigeria will embark on policies that simultaneously accelerate the demographic transition and develop its workforce to be productive.",""],[1,"147","3","Nigeria Demographic Dividend Roadmap","The Nigeria Demographic Dividend Roadmap (2017) by the National Population Commission strives to put Nigeria on the path to reaping demographic dividend within the shortest possible time, through key deliverables, milestones and concrete activities.",""],[1,"147","4","Demographic Dividend Monitoring Scorecard","the NPC developed the Nigeria Demographic Dividend Effort Index (DDEI) and launched the Demographic Dividend Scorecard in 2020 for monitoring progress of the implementation of the roadmap.",""],[1,"149","6","New National Population Policy","This plan will foster the extension of family planning programs, introduce a new generation of population policies and monitor the population trends.",""],[1,"149","6","National Demographic Dividend Monitoring System","step up observatory procedure to monitor all policy and programmatic actions and collate this into the National demographic dividend assessment Index.",""],[1,"150","38","National DD Observatory Body","Setting up of an Observatory Body for DD activities (National)",""],[1,"150","44","Observatory Body for DD Activities","Setting up of an Observatory Body for DD activities (State)",""],[1,"150","46","Demographic Dividend Investment Program","Highlights of the investment program are: Accelerating fertility declines; Improving secondary education opportunities among adolescent girls; Increasing women's economic empowerment; and improving agricultural extension services.",""],[1,"150","48","Results-Based Monitoring and Data Collection","Government will also focus on results, data collection, and monitoring for results and impact.",""]],"123":[[1,"145","4","Women’s Empowerment for Family Planning Uptake","Such broad adoption will be achievable with the empowerment of women through education and financial access.",""],[1,"145","4","Expanded Access to Contraceptives","This trend, coupled with increased access to contraceptives, provides a key opportunity to drive effective family planning methods across the country.",""],[1,"145","7","Public Education and Contraceptive Access Expansion","Further efforts will focus on public education, increased access to affordable contraceptives, and the development of a robust identity management database, which can be used to reliably estimate the population size and make broad economic projections.",""],[1,"145","9","Family Planning and Birth Rate Reduction Measures","Reduce the population growth rate, particularly by reducing current birth rates through education, incentives, and family planning.",""],[1,"146","9","Population Management and Family Planning Strengthening Programme","Strengthen existing population management systems by increasing awareness and access to family planning benefits and options - Nigeria's population management programme will be based on ethical practices, taking into consideration the strengths and weaknesses of population control programmes in other countries.",""],[1,"146","9","Women's Empowerment and Family Planning Awareness Campaign","This programme will include efforts to support women's empowerment, increase public awareness by leveraging social media platforms, and enhance access to affordable contraceptives.",""],[1,"146","9","Child Rights Act Enforcement Against Early Marriage","The government will also expand its implementation of the 2003 Child Rights Act to abolish early child marriage",""],[1,"146","9","Family Planning Normalisation and Stakeholder Coordination Initiative","Additionally, the Government will improve stakeholder coordination to align family planning messages and efficient delivery of activities.",""],[1,"146","9","Modern Family Planning Provider Training Programme","Healthcare providers will be trained on modern family planning methods using a rights-based approach emphasizing adoption by informed and voluntary uptake54.",""],[1,"146","14","Family Planning Promotion and Contraceptive Provision","Its efforts will focus on the promotion of family planning, the provision of contraceptives, and the utilisation of digital population management tools to gain timely and credible population data for proper economic planning.",""],[1,"148","1","Prioritized Policies and Interventions for Rapid Fertility Decline","Firstly, a set of prioritized policies and interventions are envisioned in the plan to set the stage for a rapid fertility decline and",""],[1,"148","6","Free Comprehensive Family Planning Services","Improve access to free comprehensive family planning services.",""],[1,"148","14","Free Comprehensive Family Planning Services","Improve access to free comprehensive family planning services.",""],[1,"149","3","Comprehensive Family Planning Access Expansion","Improve access to comprehensive family planning services.",""],[1,"149","6","Family Planning Program Expansion","This plan will foster the extension of family planning programs, introduce a new generation of population policies and monitor the population trends.",""],[1,"150","47","Family Planning and Maternal and Child Health Investment","the plan explicitly lays the foundation for accelerating the demographic transition. It acknowledges that Nigeria as a Pre-Dividend country will prioritize investments in family planning, maternal and child health improvements,",""]],"124":[[1,"147","7","Human Capital Development Vision","The Government launched its Human Capital Development Vision (HCDV) in response to Nigeria's low ranking in the Human Capital Index.",""],[1,"148","4","Girls' Secondary School Enrolment Expansion Policy","Implement policies that increase girls' enrolment in secondary schools, including general increases in education access.",""],[1,"148","7","Women’s Labour Force Participation Empowerment","Empower women for greater participation in the labour force.",""],[1,"149","1","Girls' Secondary Education Access and Free Tuition Policy","Implement policies that can increase girls' enrolment in schools, including general increases in educational access, especially at the secondary level. Free secondary school education will be offered to all adolescent girls in Nigeria.",""],[1,"149","5","Microfinance and Community Banking Support for Women","this plan will focus on expanding availability of microfinance, establishment of local savings groups, and community banks that can support poor Nigerian women who may not possess collateral for loans from advanced financial institutions.",""],[1,"149","5","SME Scaling Support and Favorable Trade Policy Measures","the scaling of successful small and medium scale businesses will be supported by advanced financial institutions and favourable trade policies, especially those that will support women and the young populations.",""],[1,"150","48","Secondary School Education for Girls","secondary school education for its girls and empowerment of women.",""],[1,"150","48","Women’s Empowerment Initiative","secondary school education for its girls and empowerment of women.",""]],"125":[[1,"148","8","Multisectoral Leadership and Coordination on the Demographic Dividend Agenda","Foster multisectoral leadership and coordination on the demographic dividend agenda in Nigeria.",""],[1,"148","19","National and State Multisectoral Demographic Dividend Observatories","Establish a national and state level multisectoral observatories of the demographic dividend",""],[1,"149","6","Demographic Dividend Coordination Mechanism","establish a demographic dividend coordination mechanism that will enable all relevant sectors implement programmes and activities that will lead Nigeria to achieving demographic dividend; step up observatory procedure to monitor all policy and programmatic actions and collate this into the National demographic dividend assessment Index.","The Federal Ministry of Finance Budget and National Planning (Planning Arm) | NPopC"],[1,"150","48","Strategic Multisectoral Plan Implementation","Government will vigorously pursue effective implementation of this plan through a strategic multisectoral approach to accelerate the arrival of the demographic dividend while also expanding the income-earning opportunities of our current working- age population, especially women.",""]],"126":[[1,"151","2","National Poverty Reduction with Growth Strategy Implementation","This is in addition to the implementation of the National Poverty Reduction with Growth Strategy (NPRGS).",""],[1,"151","3","Social Protection Policy Framework","As a result, a new institutional framework named the Social Protection Policy Framework was established in 2017 to address social investment policy gaps.",""],[1,"151","3","Poverty Reduction and Social Housing Budget Allocation","The Federal Government began budgeting N500 billion from 2016 for poverty reduction and social housing in 2016, which funds were initially utilized to commence 4 social investment programmes under the Office of the Vice President (within the Presidency).",""],[1,"151","6","National Social Safety Net Program","the National Social Safety Net Program (NASSP) supported by the World Bank which was created as a platform to manage social welfare programs for the poor and vulnerable households.",""],[1,"151","6","National Social Registry","Furthermore, the NASSP created the National Social Registry which houses the data on poor households nationwide, from which 2 million households have been mined into a benefitting register for cash transfers from the government and other initiatives under the international development partners such as the UNDP and UN Women.",""],[1,"151","7","National Conditional Cash Transfer Program","The National Conditional Cash Transfer Program within the NASSP has resulted in (1) food security improvements;",""],[1,"151","7","Community and Social Development Micro-Grant Programme","The Community & Social Development Program (CSDP) awarded micro-grants to 4,134 poor communities hosting internally displaced and vulnerable people in North-eastern Nigeria to (3) improve social and physical infrastructure.",""],[1,"151","8","Government Enterprise and Empowerment Program","the Government Enterprise and Empowerment Program (GEEP) provided interest and collateral free loans to",""],[1,"152","2","Nationally Coordinated Social Protection System","This protection takes the form of a nationally coordinated system of institutions, policies, programmes and practices designed to support vulnerable individuals and households throughout their life cycle.",""],[1,"152","12","Comprehensive Social Protection Framework","the Government will take advantage of renewed interest in poverty alleviation programming to build on the existing social protection framework.",""],[1,"152","12","Innovative Poverty Alleviation Pilot Approaches","there is substantial funding available to test innovative approaches to poverty alleviation.",""],[1,"152","13","National Social Protection System","implement a national social protection system that will create a pathway from poverty to economic empowerment for all Nigerians.",""],[1,"152","17","Social Protection Ecosystem Development","Development of a social protection ecosystem to prevent people falling into or remaining in poverty",""],[1,"153","13","Poverty Eradication Investment Plan","Nigeria will develop a poverty eradication investment plan to be approved at the federal and state levels and increase fiscal allocation to social investment programs.",""],[1,"153","13","Innovative Financing for Social Protection","Diversify revenue generating streams to finance poverty social protection initiatives through an investment program.",""],[1,"153","14","Social Insurance Scheme Expansion and Overhaul","will overhaul and expand existing social insurance schemes (retirement funds, health insurance, home ownership) while creating a large pool of national savings.",""],[1,"153","15","National Social Protection System and Digital Cash Transfer Platform","The design and deployment of a national social protection system will be prioritized, supported by a robust data ecosystem that creates a seamless interface between the National Social Register and all social sector databases.",""],[1,"153","15","Electronic Cash Transfer Delivery System","Nigeria will systematically use electronic forms of cash transfers, including mobile money, card-based payments, or e-payment platforms to safeguard the safety, efficiency, and transparency of cash transactions, and to track beneficiaries.",""],[1,"153","15","National Social Register and ID-Based Beneficiary Identification","The Government will identify vulnerable Nigerians in need of social protection services through the National Social Register and the National ID program.",""],[1,"153","16","Social Investment Fund Allocation","a Social Investment Fund of N5.4 trillion from 2021-2025 will be allocated across many MDAs.",""],[1,"154","1","Strengthening the Social Protection Programme","The social protection programme will be strengthened to ensure that the most vulnerable members of society are empowered, more resilient to shocks and share in the country's prosperity.",""],[1,"158","8","Prioritization of Core Social Assistance Programmes","the Government will ensure that core programmes are prioritized and that services are designed for inclusive humanitarian intervention and assistance.",""]],"127":[[1,"151","4","Social Programme Coordination Mechanism","newly established Federal Ministry of Humanitarian Affairs, Disaster Management and Social Development (FMHADMSD) in 2019 to coordinate all social programme interventions across sectors and all levels of government.","Federal Ministry of Humanitarian Affairs, Disaster Management and Social Development (FMHADMSD)"],[1,"152","12","Multi-stakeholder Funding and Accountability Mechanisms","an increasing number of private sector actors such as commercial banks, micro- finance banks, NGOs and social enterprise consortiums are keen to get involved and improve multi-stakeholder funding and accountability mechanisms.",""],[1,"152","12","Federal and State Social Programme Coordination","calls for better governance and coordination at the federal and state level will ensure that new social programs reach the right beneficiaries, achieve desired outcomes and are sustainable.",""],[1,"153","7","Social Protection Data Ecosystem","Design a social protection data ecosystem to reach the most vulnerable Nigerians",""],[1,"153","11","Social Protection System Harmonization and Coordination Framework","Harmonize policy, legal and institutional frameworks at the Federal and state level by identifying and addressing regulatory bottlenecks.",""],[1,"153","11","Cross-Sectoral Social Protection Programme Alignment","The Government will support the development of a comprehensive and efficient social protection system in Nigeria by resolving policy objective conflicts among existing cross-sectoral social protection programmes.",""],[1,"153","11","National Feedback and Grievance System","Engaging at the community level through a national feedback and grievance system will improve programme accountability, impact, and effectiveness.",""],[1,"153","11","Social Reform Support and Coordination Network","Additionally, a harmonized and transparent approach will generate support for social reforms, strengthen existing governance networks and develop a robust coordination framework to create a sustainable path to economic empowerment for over 50 million Nigerians.",""],[1,"153","12","National Poverty Reduction Coordination and Tracking Mechanism","Harmonise community, LGA & State efforts with National coordination (as provided under the NPRGS), and the utilization of the multi-dimensional index tracking tool, for the measurement and reduction of poverty.",""],[1,"153","14","Strengthening Financial Management for Social Investments","The country will also strengthen financial management practices to ensure efficiency and accountability in social investments and fund management.",""],[1,"153","14","Transparency Measures to Secure ODA for Poverty Eradication Pilots","Establishing transparency in financial management should enable Nigeria to secure additional ODA to pilot poverty eradication initiatives.",""],[1,"154","1","Diversification of Social Protection Financing","the Government will work with multiple stakeholders to diversify revenue sources that will ensure the sustainability of social protection programmes without relying on oil revenue.",""]],"128":[[1,"151","7","National Home Grown School Feeding Program","efforts under the National Social Investment Programme (NSIP) particularly the National Home Grown School Feeding Program fed over 9 million primary school children, reducing incidences of malnutrition in public schools primary children and enhanced enrolment there by reducing out-of-school children;",""],[1,"151","8","Health Centre and Classroom Construction Micro-Projects","The program's micro-projects surpassed original targets with 1,187 health centres and 4,832 classrooms built;",""],[1,"155","17","National Home-Grown School Feeding Program","Between 2016 and October 2019, the Office of the Vice President in the Presidency ensured that over 9 million pupils in classes 1-3 benefitted from the National Home -Grown School Feeding Program (NHGSFP) in 34","Office of the Vice President in the Presidency"]],"129":[[1,"151","8","Basic Needs and Reintegration Support for Internally Displaced Persons","the provision of basic needs for over 2 million internally displaced persons in the North East region and support resettling, reintegrating and rehabilitating them;",""],[1,"155","5","Humanitarian Response System Strengthening and Proactive Social Protection Framework","With efficient humanitarian response systems that address current bottlenecks and provide a comprehensive framework to ensure the provision of proactive social protection measures, inclusion and assistance for vulnerable people, the Government can ensure social protection and wealth generation at the grassroots level.",""],[1,"156","2","Relief Materials and Emergency Shelter Support","the FMHADMSD has provided relief materials and emergency shelters for vulnerable households","FMHADMSD"],[1,"156","3","Reconstruction, Rehabilitation, and Resettlement Programme","The Reconstruction, Rehabilitation, and Resettlement (RRR) Programme commencing with 1000 in Borno State, scaling up to 10,000 houses, roads, schools, health facilities, in all six states of the North East is currently ongoing.",""],[1,"156","3","Rapid Response Intervention","The Rapid Response Intervention (RRI) and the Agricultural Integrated Scheme (AIS) were also being implemented as part of the programmes geared towards achieving the ERGP.",""],[1,"157","2","Humanitarian Response and Disaster Management Plan","The focus of the objectives for the Humanitarian Affairs plan is geared towards promoting humanitarian responses, preventing, mitigating, and managing disasters across the country.",""],[1,"157","4","Humanitarian Relief Delivery for Conflict-Displaced People","Identify where they are based and make provisions for delivery of necessary food and non-food items to people of concern (POCs) displaced by conflict;",""],[1,"157","5","Sector-Level Resilience and Emergency Management Plans","Delineate the various forms of humanitarian crisis and develop specific sector level plans for building resilience and emergency management for the vulnerable population;",""],[1,"158","7","Strengthening the National Humanitarian Framework","The Plan would strengthen the Government's humanitarian framework, to ensure that Nigeria can leverage its partnership with multilateral organizations, global institutions, and local stakeholders, to provide lasting, sustainable, and durable responses to humanitarian issues, for inclusive economic development.",""]],"130":[[1,"155","16","Federal Humanitarian Coordination One-Stop Shop","The FMHADMSD now serves as a one-stop shop to coordinate all humanitarian issues and interventions across all the sectors and levels of government;","Federal Ministry of Humanitarian Affairs, Disaster Management and Social Development (FMHADMSD)"],[1,"155","17","National Policy on Humanitarian Affairs, Disaster Management and Social Development","It is also developing the National Policy on Humanitarian Affairs, Disaster Management and Social Development for improved living standard for the elderly, vulnerable, socially disadvantaged persons and victims of human trafficking.",""],[1,"156","2","Disaster Risk Management Framework","The development of a Disaster Risk Management Framework has resulted in effective coordination and response to disasters in Nigeria and thus improved humanitarian responses.",""],[1,"157","1","Humanitarian Service Delivery Reform and Technology Support","Other opportunities to improve humanitarian service delivery include the ongoing reform of existing policies, partnerships with other key stakeholders, among other internal strengths.",""],[1,"157","1","Information Technology for Innovative Humanitarian Service Design","The employment of technological tools, including the adoption of information technology to support the design of innovative products and collaborative efforts, remain key levers to ensure the design of services, which ensure that vulnerable members of the society have access to humanitarian relief, and that the increased demand for such social and humanitarian initiatives can be met.",""],[1,"157","3","Capacity Building for Ministries, Departments and Agencies on Humanitarian and Social Investment Management","Building the Capacity of Nigerian Ministries, Departments and Agencies responsible for managing humanitarian crisis, disaster risk and social investments;",""],[1,"157","6","Sub-national Humanitarian Affairs Planning","Drive sub-national efforts at developing humanitarian affairs plans for preparedness and resilience",""],[1,"157","7","Humanitarian Crisis Financing and Operations Liaison Framework","Develop a framework for Liaising with private domestic and foreign donors to manage financing and operations for humanitarian crises.",""],[1,"157","9","Humanitarian Policy and Institutional Framework Strengthening","Strengthen policies and institutional framework on humanitarian issues through policy development and organizational development.",""],[1,"157","10","Humanitarian Response Coordination and Policy Harmonization","that will harmonize all activities of the government in the sphere of providing humanitarian responses.",""],[1,"157","10","Policy Review and Gap Updating for Humanitarian Response","efforts will also focus on ensuring the coalition and review of all relevant policies, identifying and updating policy gaps",""],[1,"157","10","MDA Capacity Development and Feedback Mechanism","the capacity of relevant MDAs will be improved through the restructuring of organizational value systems, continuous capacity development for all staff, and the development of a stakeholders' feedback and evaluation mechanism to improve service delivery.",""],[1,"157","11","Humanitarian Coordination Systems Framework","Promote effective governance by developing humanitarian coordination systems and cross- MDA collaboration.",""],[1,"157","11","L.I.F.E Cycle Framework","This coordination initiative will be anchored on a framework tagged as the framework to \"Lead an Inclusive and Innovative Futures-thinking Ecosystem (L.I.F.E Cycle).\"",""],[1,"157","11","State-Federal Programme Harmonisation Regulatory Framework","a regulatory framework will be introduced to harmonise the management of programmes between the state and federal government.",""],[1,"157","12","Evidence-Based Transparency and Accountability Systems","Build evidence-based systems for transparency and accountability through the adoption of technological tools for monitoring and management.",""],[1,"157","12","Humanitarian Project Coordination and Management Information System","To achieve this, the FMHAMSD shall coordinate all humanitarian projects across all MDAs, identify and manage operational gaps across all agencies, ensure monthly performance reporting, facilitate digital automated processes and procedures, and develop continuous capacity development for all staff.",""],[1,"158","1","National Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","Nigeria shall ensure proper evaluation and monitoring of all initiatives, projects and programmes across all ministries, departments and agencies in line with the overall mandate of the government to ensure that every Nigerian benefits meaningfully from the programmes and initiatives of the government.",""],[1,"158","1","Management Information System Sensitization","The stakeholders will also be adequately sensitized about the Management Information System (MIS) that will be used.",""],[1,"158","2","Humanitarian Partnership and Disability Inclusion Initiative","Increase existing humanitarian efforts through strategic partnerships and collaboration with humanitarian organizations and ensure disability inclusion.",""],[1,"158","3","Efficient Budget Management and Resource Planning Framework","Optimizing funding and resourcing through efficient budget management systems, and funding partnerships with social and private sector actors.",""]],"131":[[1,"158","5","Comprehensive SDGs Project List Development","Nigeria will develop a comprehensive SDGs project list that will be made up of innovative social programs that have direct impact on humanitarian affairs.",""],[1,"158","5","Stakeholder Engagement Coordination Mechanism","There will also be effective coordination of stakeholders' engagement",""],[1,"158","5","Social Program Performance and Feedback Mechanism","a projects performance and feedback mechanism on social programs will be developed and deployed across the country.",""],[1,"158","5","SDGs Impact Challenge Mitigation Plan","Possible impact challenges will be identified and mitigation plan to tackle these challenges will be developed.",""],[1,"158","5","Global SDGs Partnerships and Awareness Campaign","Nigeria will continue to establish and maintain sustainable relationship with global platforms for knowledge and resources opportunities while creating awareness and sensitization across the country for the various programmes and initiatives launched under the SDGs umbrella.",""]],"132":[[1,"159","3","National Youth Investment Fund","the government established a N75 billion National Youth Investment Fund (NYIF) to finance youth-led businesses and create more jobs.",""],[1,"160","14","Cross-Sector Job Creation Initiatives","Drive job creation initiatives across various sectors, including sports.",""],[1,"163","3","Safety Net Job Scheme","addressing employment-related vulnerabilities by setting up a safety net job scheme to engage up to 20,000 unskilled workers per state, per year;",""],[1,"163","6","N-Power and Youth Employment and Support Operations Programmes","Furthermore, the Government established the N-Power and Youth Employment and Support operations programs.",""],[1,"163","9","Youth Employment and Support Operations Programme","the Youth Employment and Support operations programs were designed to support extending youth employment opportunities and award targeted grant funding to the most vulnerable such as internally displaced people (IDPs).",""],[1,"163","9","Youth Public Works Employment Programme","An additional 85,000 youths were engaged in public works projects across the country as part of this program;",""],[1,"164","17","Agricultural Value Chain Development and Youth Job Creation","The agriculture sector will be geared for job creation, particularly for the youths through investments in value chain development, capacity building and improving linkages across sectors.",""],[1,"164","18","Massive Job Programmes","Job growth in these sectors will be stimulated through massive job programmes to achieve the ambitious objective of lifting 35 million people out of poverty by 2025.",""],[1,"164","19","Sector-Specific Job Creation Strategies","GDP growth, complemented with sector-specific job creation strategies that will identify and optimise impactful opportunities across high growth sectors.",""],[1,"164","20","Entrepreneur and MSME Financing Access Support","Ease access to financing for entrepreneurs especially MSMEs;",""],[1,"164","21","Youth and Female Inclusion in Job Creation and Diversification","Promote inclusion of youths and females in job creation and diversification",""],[1,"165","9","Intersectoral Linkages for Job Creation","Create intersectoral linkages to unlock the potential of high growth sectors critical to creating 21 million jobs by mapping and identifying synergies and opportunities with the most potential for massive, secure and sustainable job creation.",""],[1,"165","9","Public-Private Partnerships for Priority Sector Investment","The Government will establish public-private partnerships focused on priority sectors to secure investments in capital intensive sectors with the highest probability of spurring job creation such as mining, construction, manufacturing, agriculture, sports, entertainment, tourism, and hospitality.",""],[1,"165","9","Unskilled Persons Database and Safety Net Jobs","Safety net jobs will be created for unskilled persons by developing a database of all unskilled persons in all the 36 states and the FCT.",""],[1,"165","9","Labour-Intensive Stop-Gap Jobs and Training Mapping","Map sectors of focus to create labour- intensive massive stop-gap jobs and provide training needs for the unskilled in each of the 774 LGAs in the country.",""],[1,"165","12","Youth Agribusiness and Construction Employment Support","Emphasis will be youth participation in sustainable agribusiness and construction by creating job opportunities in these sectors through financing schemes and training initiatives.",""],[1,"166","4","Youth Engagement, Empowerment and Employment Mechanism","Government in close collaboration with the private sector to develop a mechanism to Engage, Empower and Employ our teaming energetic youths, by ensuring that Nigerian youths below age of 35 should either be in school, gainfully employed or be the owner of skilful enterprises by 2025.",""],[1,"166","6","Gender-Balanced Job Opportunities Initiative","Government will fully support gender equality for gender balanced job opportunities across all sectors to significantly reduce the alarming rate of unemployment among women.",""],[1,"160","21","Youth Economic Opportunity and Participation Initiatives","Between 2021 and 2025, Government will undertake important initiatives to create economic opportunities for which the youths will be prepared to take advantage.",""]],"133":[[1,"159","4","Youth Capacity Building and Vocational Training Initiatives","Several capacity building and vocational training initiatives have equally been executed to build the skills of the Nigerian youth in areas such as agriculture, fashion, digital marketing, technology and entrepreneurship.","Ministry of Youth and Sports Development"],[1,"159","9","Targeted Youth Training Initiatives","Ample opportunities exist to increase the human capital of the youths through targeted academic and non-academic training initiatives to prepare them for the current leadership and market needs within and outside the country.",""],[1,"160","11","Youth Development Initiative Implementation Strengthening","Strengthen the implementation of initiatives and policies targeted at youth development such as the National Youth Investment Fund (NYIF)",""],[1,"160","12","Youth Capacity Building Programmes","Introduce and improve relevant capacity building programmes for youths through academic, vocational and entrepreneurship trainings, especially with a focus on the unskilled and uneducated category.",""],[1,"160","20","Youth Development Public Investment Programme","An estimated public investment of N60 billion will be allocated to achieve the goals outlined for youths' development from 2021-2025.",""],[1,"163","8","N-Power Skills and Entrepreneurship Programme","N-Power program was created to help young Nigerians acquire and develop life-long skills to become active players in the domestic and global market.",""],[1,"163","9","Youth Skills Training and Seed Funding Initiative","Under the programme, 24,000 young people were trained for skilled jobs and given seed funding to start their businesses.",""],[1,"163","10","Technical and Vocational Skills Training and Skills Upgrade Support","another 1,090,000 youths were trained on various technical and vocational skills, and 310,000 artisans benefited from skills upgrade support;",""],[1,"163","10","Specialized Skills Centres Construction Programme","the Government built 9 specialized skills centres in Borno, Kogi, Ebonyi, Enugu, Anambra, Nasarawa, Kaduna, Katsina and Ondo states.",""],[1,"164","15","Health, Education and WASH Workforce Hiring and Training Initiative","The strategy to improve the quality of the health, education and WASH sectors, will include significant hiring and training initiatives necessary to enhance service delivery.",""],[1,"165","9","Private Sector Curriculum Development Framework","The private sector will be encouraged to i) develop a robust framework for educational and training curricular development and reviews ii) invest in young unemployed persons, and iii) establish a functional multi-sectoral task team to facilitate implementation.",""],[1,"165","13","Private Sector Skills Partnership Framework","Develop a partnership framework with the private sector by identifying skills gaps and designing skills development programmes aligned with their needs.",""],[1,"165","13","Skills Development Curriculum Review and Update","Government will continuously engage the private sector on the review and update of skills development curricula to meet the demands of the emerging labour market, with a special focus on the needs of the Fourth Industrial Revolution and the GIG economy.",""],[1,"165","13","Rural Training Centre Construction","The Government will build training centres, especially in rural areas, to facilitate access to the sections of the population who require skilling or up-skilling to become competitive on the job market.",""],[1,"166","2","Sports Skills for Employability Programme","Encourage the sports ministries to build skills for employability (especially youth employment).",""],[1,"166","3","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Promotion","Promote Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) towards creating sustainable jobs for the teeming unemployed and underemployed youth in Nigeria.",""],[1,"167","6","Sports Industry Employability Skills Development","The sports industry will be encouraged to build skills for employability.",""],[1,"167","6","Comprehensive Workforce Skills-Building Programme","This approach will be supported by a comprehensive skill-building program to prepare tomorrow's workforce's ability to contribute to Nigeria's industrialization efforts.",""]],"134":[[1,"160","7","Youth Participation in Governance Initiative","Increase the participation of youths in governance",""],[1,"160","15","Youth Participation in Governance Initiative","Increase youth participation in governance through existing platforms and implementation of relevant legislation.",""],[1,"160","16","Youth Political Engagement and Trust-Building Initiative","awareness of and leverage platforms such as the NYCN and NYP to engage youths in the political process whilst working to resolve issues that create mistrust of such platforms.",""],[1,"160","17","Youth Engagement and Demand Implementation Initiative","Ensure that the voices of youths are heard by implementing the \"5 for 5 demands\" submitted during the nationwide #EndSARS protests in 2020.",""],[1,"160","18","Implementation of the Not Too Young to Run Act","Implement critical legislation such as the Not too Young to Run Act.",""],[1,"160","19","National Youth Policy Implementation and Periodic Review","Be committed to implementing the National Youth Policy and ensure it is reviewed on a periodic and regular basis.",""]],"135":[[1,"161","2","National Sports Industry Modernization and Industrialization Policy","It seeks to redirect the focus of sports from purely recreational and participatory, to a modernization and industrialisation of the sector through collaboration with the private sector, backed with a properly defined implementation framework.",""],[1,"161","6","Sports Sector Legal and Regulatory Framework Reform","the country is yet to establish a comprehensive legal and regulatory framework to exploit the economic potentials of sports and set the stage for associated legislation.",""],[1,"161","6","Public-Private Partnership Model for Sports Investment","Other countries harness the potential of sports through Public-Private Partnership (PPP) models where the government establishes a regulatory framework that incentivizes the private sector to invest in sports and sets up institutions such as domestic Courts of Arbitration for Sports to resolve relevant disputes through arbitration, without recourse to potentially unending and costly litigation in the regular courts.",""],[1,"161","6","Domestic Sports Arbitration Institution","sets up institutions such as domestic Courts of Arbitration for Sports to resolve relevant disputes through arbitration, without recourse to potentially unending and costly litigation in the regular courts.",""],[1,"161","8","Sports Sector Legal and Regulatory Framework Reform","Nigeria can convert its sports sector into an economic and social contributor through the establishment of appropriate legal and regulatory frameworks that enable public-private partnerships and unlock the full economic potential of the sector.",""],[1,"162","17","Sports Sector Investment Promotion Framework","Develop an encompassing framework in making the sports sector a thriving and attractive sector for both domestic and foreign investors' participation.",""],[1,"162","18","Sports Private Sector Participation Framework","Set up and implement a legal and regulatory framework for increased private sector participation in sports.",""],[1,"162","19","Private Sector Investment in Sports Industry Development","Private sector participation will help provide critical investments to unlock the economic potentials in Nigeria's sports industry and create jobs that further engage the vibrant youth population.",""],[1,"162","20","Sports Facilities Implementation in Education Institutions","Increase synergy with the ministries of education to ensure and implement sports facilities as part",""],[1,"162","23","Sports Development Public Investment Programme","An estimated public investment of N88 billion will be allocated to achieve the goals outlined for sports development from 2021-2025.",""],[1,"162","24","Sports Sector Investment Attraction and Strengthening","Government's plan is to attract investment into the sector and make it a significant contributor to the development of the country.",""],[1,"162","24","Sports Industry Development for Jobs and Social Cohesion","Under this Plan therefore, the sports industry will be further strengthened such that it can become a viable contributor to the Nigerian economy and create jobs that can engage and unite the citizens, especially the youths.",""]],"136":[[1,"163","5","National Reporting Template for Child Labour Action Plan","developing a National Reporting Template on the National Action Plan on the elimination of Child Labour by training relevant stakeholders on its application.",""],[1,"165","12","Occupational Health and Safety Compliance Enforcement","Government will prioritize compliance with Occupational Health and Safety (OSH) legislation to all workplaces to improve the productivity and performance of workers over time.",""],[1,"165","14","Enforcement of Unionization Rules and Sanctions","Adopting strict adherence to the guiding rules and principles of unionization with appropriate sanctions will reduce incidence of disruptions to economic activities due to perennial trade disputes and strikes from violation of rights of workers on free unionism.",""],[1,"166","1","Child Labour Eradication Collaboration and Monitoring Framework","fostering networks and collaboration among local, national and international organizations on child labour eradication and the development of effective Monitoring and Evaluation framework to enforce implementation.",""]],"137":[[1,"172","2","Replication of Regional Development Commission Model","The federal government will take the lead in encouraging subnational governments to replicate this model between and among states under the Plan.",""],[1,"172","3","Concurrent Development of the Six Geopolitical Zones","Government will ensure that the six geopolitical zones are developed concurrently to achieve balanced economic growth by leveraging economic activity as a strategy for",""],[1,"173","16","Inter-State Economic Cooperation and Collaboration Initiative","foster collaboration and economic cooperation across states within geopolitical zones",""],[1,"173","17","Central-Subnational Coordination for Balanced Regional Development","ensure synergy and coordination between the central government and the subnational governments to encourage even development of communities across all regions",""],[1,"173","19","Refocusing Regional Development Commissions for Community Development Outcomes","Refocus existing regional development commissions like the NDDC and the North East Development Commission to facilitate developmental outcomes across communities",""],[1,"175","3","Plan Implementation Unit Coordination Mechanism","The new Plan Implementation Unit of Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget and National Planning [Budget and Planning Arm] would be expected to make this happen through its coordination power as a Planning Arm for the three tiers of government.","Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget and National Planning"],[1,"175","3","Inter-State Economic Collaboration Initiative","States are encouraged to reach out to other States outside of their region with mutually beneficial and complementary economic interests.",""],[1,"175","3","Regional Mega Project Financing Collaboration","States within the same region are also encouraged to collaborate in raising funds for financing mega projects in their region, which ordinarily would have been unattainable if funded individually.",""],[1,"175","5","Coordinated Regional Development Strategy","Nigeria faces unequal access to economic opportunities and social amenities across geographic regions, necessitating a coordinated development strategy at the regional, state, and local levels.",""],[1,"177","4","Resource Mobilization Plan","Beyond allocation, a mobilization plan would also be initiated to facilitate the sourcing of the needed resources.",""],[1,"177","6","Plan Coordination and Ownership Mechanism","Coordination and work progress should be synchronized by the ministry responsible for budgeting and planning at Federal and subnational levels.",""],[1,"177","11","Central Plan Coordination Secretariat","Leverage existing government structures such as FMBNP (the National Planning Arm) to serve as a central coordination secretariat.",""],[1,"177","15","Federal-State Coordination for Development Plan Delivery","Given the importance of state governments in implementation, coordination of efforts between the federal and state governments will be critical for the efficient delivery of development outcomes.",""],[1,"177","16","State Development Plan Development and Review","State governments will work with the Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget and National Planning (FMBNP) and the plan implementation unit to develop or review the SDP in line with the Plan.","Federal Ministry of Finance, Budget and National Planning (FMBNP)"],[1,"177","17","Intergovernmental Development Plan Coordination Strengthening","Strengthening the synergy among federal, states and local government institutions towards implementing the Development Plans.",""],[1,"179","20","State Development Plan Coordination and Harmonization","Coordinate preparation of state development plans and budgets in line with defined goals · Integrate and harmonize state plans in line with national development goals and objectives · Monitor the implementation of plans and submit reports on them",""],[1,"179","21","Private Sector Engagement and Strategy Alignment Mechanism","Engage with the National Planning Arm to identify ways for private sector's contribution to goals and to ensure alignment of relevant strategies with private sector needs",""]],"138":[[1,"173","20","Economic Clustering Along Value Chains","Explore the potential for economic clustering along value chains for subnational government collaboration.",""],[1,"174","11","State-Based Local Production and Growth Lever Development Plan","Identify economic growth levers and spur local production opportunities across states based on their respective competitive advantage.",""],[1,"174","11","High-Growth Sector Prioritization and Regional Product Development Plan","The government will prioritize key high growth sectors and identify products based on each states' unique characteristics such as natural endowments, geographic proximity to large markets or cultural know-how to ensure sustainability and competitiveness.",""],[1,"174","11","Regional Characteristics Cultivation Plan for Job Creation","The Government will develop a plan to cultivate these unique regional characteristics to fuel job creation efforts and develop",""],[1,"174","14","Subnational Economic Clustering Initiative","Encourage subnational governments to identify the potential for possible economic clustering along the value chains to improve production capacities for regional economic prosperity.",""],[1,"174","15","Competitive State Policy Promotion","Promote competitive state policies which will ultimately lead to greater business productivity, resulting in sustainable economic growth and development.",""],[1,"175","5","Regional Competitive Advantage and Inter-State Collaboration Initiative","Efforts will also be made to capitalise on regions' distinct competitive advantages to develop local products and strengthen inter-state collaboration.",""]],"139":[[1,"145","10","Rural-Urban Divide Reduction Initiative","Slow rural-urban migration by identifying and reducing the rural-urban divides in terms of economic opportunities, infrastructural facilities and social amenities.",""],[1,"146","10","Rural Economic Opportunity and Urban Infrastructure Support Measures","Introduce measures to contain urbanisation while preparing for its continued increase, by providing economic opportunities in rural areas and infrastructural development in urban areas",""],[1,"174","10","Rural Social Amenities Expansion Programme","Close the regional gap in social amenities coverage by investing in programmes that will extend services and build infrastructure in rural areas.",""],[1,"174","10","Primary Healthcare Centre Development and Social Services Access Expansion","The government will secure investments to close social amenity gaps by developing primary healthcare centres and improving access to energy, water, and quality education across regions, particularly in the North of Nigeria.",""],[1,"174","10","Subnational Infrastructure Collaboration and Public-Private Partnership Mechanism","Encourage subnational governments to collaborate to jointly build infrastructure in partnership with the private sector and promote access to social services.",""],[1,"174","12","Innovative Co-financing Mechanism for Programme Expansion","These initiatives will be financed by introducing innovative co-financing tools across MDAs, private, and social sector organizations to expand the reach of these programmes across regions.",""],[1,"174","13","Oversight Strengthening for Regional Development Commissions","Institutionalise and improve the oversight function of statutory regional development commissions to foster communities' development across geopolitical zones.",""]],"140":[[1,"177","14","ICT Deployment through Young Graduate Placement","Deployment of ICT and relevant technology through the careful insertion of young graduates with strong ICT skills to strengthen efficiency and value.",""],[1,"178","5","Integrated Management and Geographic Information System Deployment","Deploy an integrated Management and Geographic Information (MIS/GIS) System that is uniform across MDAs.",""],[1,"178","8","Development and Harmonization of Digital Tools","The government will invest in the development of new cost-effective digital tools and harmonization of existing ones to enable and accelerate the implementation of",""],[1,"178","10","Policy Implementation Automation Initiative","Begin the automation process of policy implementation, monitoring and evaluation by the end of 2022.",""],[1,"178","11","Technology Gap Assessment in MDAs","Conduct technology gap assessment in MDAs.",""],[1,"178","12","Technology Skills Enhancement Framework for MDAs","Develop technology skills enhancement framework for MDAs.",""],[1,"178","13","Technology Deployment for Policy Implementation and M&E in MDAs","Begin gradual deployment of technology concerning existing skills for policy implementation, monitoring and evaluation in MDAs.",""],[1,"178","14","Policy and Project Implementation Monitoring Dashboards","Develop and deploy policy/project implementation and monitoring dashboards in MDAs.",""]],"141":[[1,"184","24","Establishment of the Nigerian Statistical Trust Fund","Establishment of the Nigerian Statistical Trust Fund (NSTF) through Voluntary contributions from Development Partner Organizations (Local and International):",""]],"142":[[1,"168","2","Disability Anti-Discrimination Law","The law aims to fully integrate PWDs into society, prevent any form of discrimination and established the National Commission for Persons with Disabilities.",""],[1,"168","3","National Programs for the Economic and Social Integration of Persons with Disabilities","The Discrimination Against People With Disabilities Act defined comprehensive guidelines and launched national programs in support of the economic and social integration of PWDs.",""],[1,"169","2","Disability Inclusion Act Enforcement Support","Strong efforts will be made to ensure that the Act is applied so that PWDs are systematically included by organizations.",""],[1,"169","2","State Support for Disability Law Implementation","The Government recognizes the importance of PWDs to foster an inclusive society and will continue supporting states to ensure that provisions",""],[1,"169","11","Commission for Persons with Disability Establishment","Set up Commission for persons with disability following 2019 Discrimination Against Persons with Disabilities (Prohibition) Act",""],[1,"169","12","State-Level Disability Law Adoption","Encourage States to pass their respective state-level disability laws",""],[1,"169","22","Disability Discrimination Act Enforcement Framework","Support the enforcement of the Discrimination Against People with Disabilities Act by developing a robust implementation framework in collaboration with states.",""],[1,"169","23","Inclusive Policymaking for Persons with Disabilities","Adopt an inclusive lens in policymaking by systematically incorporating concerns of PWDs in programme planning and implementation.",""],[1,"169","26","Strengthening the National Commission for Persons with Disabilities","The government will strengthen the National Commission for Persons with Disabilities for operational effectiveness and improve public awareness.",""]],"143":[[1,"168","6","Accessibility Infrastructure Upgrade for Persons with Disabilities","the design and upgrade of infrastructure to facilitate access to the physically challenged",""],[1,"168","6","Assistive Mobility Aids Provision for Persons with Disabilities","the provision of 5,000 mobility aids such as crutches, wheelchairs and canes to PWDs",""],[1,"168","6","Artificial Limb Provision for Persons with Disabilities","the provision of prophylaxis (artificial limbs) to 300 PWDs",""],[1,"168","6","Vocational Skills Training and Starter Grant Support for Persons with Disabilities","the training of 150 PWDs on vocational skills in beads making, tying and dying, weaving with starter pack grants given to graduate trainees",""],[1,"169","16","Mobility Aids and Assistive Technology Access Improvement","Improve access to mobility aids and assistive technology",""],[1,"169","18","Disability Rehabilitation Services Expansion","Strengthen the provision of rehabilitation services to persons with disabilities",""],[1,"169","25","Disaggregated Data Collection and Survey Programme for Persons with Disabilities","Expand the availability of data on PWD to inform national planning and programme performance monitoring.",""],[1,"170","1","Assistive Devices and Mobility Aids Mass Production Programme","Encourage mass production of high quality locally produced assistive devices/mobility aids/ assistive technology for free distribution to deserving beneficiaries across the country",""],[1,"170","2","National Rehabilitation Facilities Upgrade and Expansion","Upgrading of existing and building new rehabilitation facilities across the country to provide services and train volunteers in scaling down clinical and non- clinical rehabilitation services to community and households levels.",""]],"144":[[1,"188","13","Establishment of the National Climate Change Fund","Government will work with Development Partners to establish the NCEF.",""]]}});